现在，首先，什么是网络安全？
Now, first and foremost, what is cybersecurity?

59
00:05:59,936 --> 00:06:10,830
自从计算机诞生以来，我们就一直在处理网络安全的三个主要支柱，它们被称为机密性、
完整性和可用性三要素，也称为 CIA，不要和美国中央情报局搞混了。
There are three main pillars of cybersecurity that we deal with since the inception of computers,
and they're known as the confidentiality, integrity, and availability triad, also known as CIA,

60
00:06:10,830 --> 00:06:14,096
自从计算机诞生以来，我们就一直在处理网络安全的三个主要支柱，它们被称为机密性、
完整性和可用性三要素，也称为 CIA，不要和美国中央情报局搞混了。
not to be confused with the American Intelligence Agency.

61
00:06:14,336 --> 00:06:24,976
但在这里，我们看的是三个不同的支柱：我们希望数据保持
机密，数据的完整性保持完好，并且数据在任何时间都可用。
but here we're looking at three different pillars where we want our data to remain confidential,
the integrity of the data to be intact, and the data to be made available at all points in time.

62
00:06:25,216 --> 00:06:28,016
那么，让我们来谈谈这三个方面。
So let's talk about these three aspects.

63
00:06:28,270 --> 00:06:34,576
机密性原则规定，只有授权方才能访问信息和功能。
The principle of confidentiality asserts that the information and functions can be accessed only by authorized parties.

64
00:06:34,736 --> 00:06:39,936
例如，即使你给文件设置了密码保护，你到底想达到什么目的？
So, for example, even if you password protect your file, what is it that you're trying to do?

65
00:06:40,096 --> 00:06:47,376
你是为了防止其他用户访问你的数据并窥探你的文件，从而确保你的数据保持机密。
You're trying to prevent other users accessing your data and peeping into your files so that your data remains confidential.

66
00:06:47,536 --> 00:06:50,976
它只与知道密码的人共享。
It is only shared with people who know the password.

67
00:06:51,216 --> 00:06:51,856
完整性。
Integrity.

68
00:06:52,016 --> 00:06:54,896
这里涉及到数据的可信度。
This is where the trustworthiness of that data comes into the picture.

69
00:06:55,136 --> 00:07:09,124
也就是说，如果数据要被更改，比如你有一个包含大量用户信息、登录活动等内容的电子表格，
你要确保这些数据不会被任何未授权用户修改。
Where if the data is going to be changed, for example, you have a spreadsheet which has a lot of information about users and their
login activities and whatnot, and you want to ensure that that data is not modified by any unauthorized user.

70
00:07:09,296 --> 00:07:16,896
所以你要验证信息是正确的，并且没有被任何未授权人员篡改。
So you're going to verify that the information is correct and is not modified by anybody who's unauthorized.

71
00:07:17,102 --> 00:07:23,696
可用性部分确保所有授权用户在他们需要的时间和地点都能获取这些数据。
The availability part ensures that this data is made available to all authorized users when and where they want it.

72
00:07:23,886 --> 00:07:24,176
对吧？
Right?

73
00:07:24,576 --> 00:07:32,896
可用性原则规定，在系统中，功能和数据必须根据基于服务水平协议的约定参数，按需提供。
The principles of availability assert that in systems functions and data must be
available on demand according to agreed upon parameters based on levels of service.

74
00:07:33,056 --> 00:07:35,856
这就是服务水平协议发挥作用的地方。
Now, this is where your service level agreements would come in.

75
00:07:36,016 --> 00:07:42,496
例如，当我们登录 Gmail 时，我们总是假设 Gmail 可以正常运行并且在线可用。
For example, when we log on to Gmail, we always assume that Gmail is going to work and it's going to be available online.

76
00:07:42,736 --> 00:07:50,336
几乎从未发生过，或者说极少发生过，你上网输入 gmail.com 时网站不可用的情况。
At no point in time, or very few times has it ever occurred that you've
gone onto the internet typed in gmail.com and the website is not available.

77
00:07:50,496 --> 00:07:54,656
事实上，如果网站打不开，我们会认为是网络没通，对吧？
In fact, if the website doesn't open, we figure out the internet is not working, right?

78
00:07:54,736 --> 00:07:57,476
但作为一项服务，Gmail 始终是可用的。
But Gmail as a service is always made available.

79
00:07:57,776 --> 00:08:06,500
现在，当我们谈论对 CIA（机密性、完整性和可用性）的威胁时，
我们从网络犯罪和黑客攻击两个不同的维度来谈论。
Now, when we talk about threats to CIA, the confidentiality, integrity, and availability,
we talk about them in two different parameters cybercrime and hacking.

80
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:08,256
那么，什么是网络犯罪？
So, what is cybercrime?

81
00:08:08,558 --> 00:08:20,384
网络犯罪是指任何涉及使用计算设备且会导致受害者
端发生安全事件的犯罪活动或任何未经授权的活动。
Cybercrime is any criminal activity or any unauthorized activity that would involve the usage of any computing device which would
result as a security incident at the victim's end.

82
00:08:20,622 --> 00:08:24,064
大多数网络犯罪都是为了谋取利益而实施的。
Most cybercrimes are carried out in order to profit from them.

83
00:08:24,224 --> 00:08:39,582
犯罪分子会尝试进行网络钓鱼攻击来盗取你银行账户里的钱，或者试图欺骗你提供凭据，
从而入侵你的电子邮件账户或社交媒体账户，并试图获取你的身份。
Criminals would try to do phishing attacks to steal your money out of your bank accounts or would try to con you into giving out your
credentials, thus compromising your email accounts or your social media accounts and try to gain access to your identity.

84
00:08:39,885 --> 00:08:48,864
网络犯罪通常是直接针对计算机或设备实施的，目的
是破坏或禁用它们、传播恶意软件、窃取机密信息等。
Cybercrimes are generally carried out against computers or devices directly
to damage or disable them, spread malware, steal secret information, etc.

85
00:08:49,184 --> 00:08:52,384
所以这里谈论的是网络犯罪的动机部分。
So this talks about the motivation part of cybercrimes.

86
00:08:52,544 --> 00:08:57,744
一个人进行此类活动的动机是什么？
What would be the motivational aspect for a person to conduct such an activity?

87
00:08:57,984 --> 00:08:58,304
对吧？
Right?

88
00:08:58,544 --> 00:09:02,944
基本上就是为了造成破坏，就像 2017 年发生的 WannaCry 事件一样。
So basically to cause damage like WannaCry happened in 2017.

89
00:09:03,184 --> 00:09:15,904
犯罪嫌疑人，也就是那些使用 WannaCry 的人，可能从他们要求的解密数据赎金中获得了大量收
益，但这也导致全球损失了大量的利润。
The perpetrators, those those used WannaCry probably gained a lot in the ransom that they demanded for that data to be decrypted,
but it also cost the world a lot of money in profits that were lost.

90
00:09:16,144 --> 00:09:18,304
那么让我们来谈谈网络犯罪的类型。
So let's talk about types of cybercrime.

91
00:09:18,464 --> 00:09:24,704
第一种是计算机辅助犯罪，即使用计算机作为工具来协助特定的犯罪。
The first type is a computer assisted crime where the computers are used as tools to assist a particular crime.

92
00:09:24,878 --> 00:09:33,744
例如，欺诈或在线银行劫持，其中黑客入侵银行并从银行数字盗取资金。
For example, frauds or online bank hijacking where hackers hack into a bank and digitally steal money from a bank.

93
00:09:33,904 --> 00:09:41,824
这种情况也可以在没有电脑帮助的情况下发生，但在这里，电脑辅助了犯罪行为，
因此它属于计算机辅助犯罪这一类。
Now this could have happened without the help of computers as well, but here computer
assisted the crime and hence it would fall under the computer assisted crime section.

94
00:09:42,030 --> 00:09:45,104
第二种情况是电脑本身就是犯罪的目标。
The second part is where the computer itself was a target of a crime.

95
00:09:45,184 --> 00:09:55,664
例如，拒绝服务攻击或病毒导致电脑无法使用，或者是
嗅探网络上的数据包，从而窃取密码和其他机密信息。
For example, a denial of service attack or viruses which rendered the computer useless or sniffing of data packets on the network,
thus compromising passwords and other confidential information.

96
00:09:55,904 --> 00:09:59,140
第三种是电脑与犯罪行为无关。
The third is a computer which is incidental to the crime.

97
