D 的值可以使用以下函数计算，结果为 29。
The value of D can be calculated using the following function which gives it as 29.

5552
08:40:30,126 --> 08:40:36,996
公钥可以打包为 91,5，私钥可以打包为 91.29。
The public key can then be packaged as 91,5 and the private key can then be packaged as 91.29.

5553
08:40:38,126 --> 08:40:41,284
明文如果是 10，用 m 表示。
The plain text if it is 10, which is denoted by m.

5554
08:40:41,710 --> 08:40:48,228
密文可以根据公式 c 等于 m 的 e 次方模 n 计算，结果为 82。
Ciphertext can be calculated to the formula c equal to m to the power e mod n which gives us 82.

5555
08:40:48,750 --> 08:40:58,500
如果有人收到这个密文，他们可以使用公式 c 的 d 次
方模 n 来计算明文，结果就是我们选定的明文 10。
If somebody receives this ciphertext, they can calculate the plain text using the formula
c to the power d mod n which gives us the value of 10 as selected as our plain text.

5556
08:40:59,694 --> 08:41:07,012
现在我们可以看看 RSA 算法在这一课的优势主题中，相比于竞争对手有哪些突出的特点。
We can now look at the factors that make the RSA algorithm stand out versus its competitors in the advantageous topics of this lesson.

5557
08:41:09,198 --> 08:41:16,516
RSA 加密依赖于使用接收者的公钥，这样你就不需要为了接收别人的消息而分享任何密钥。
RSA encryption depends on using the receiver's public key so that you
don't have to share any secret key to receive the messages from others.

5558
08:41:17,038 --> 08:41:23,780
这是对称算法面临的最明显的缺陷，最终通过非对称加密结构得到了解决。
This was the most glaring flaw faced by symmetric algorithms which were eventually fixed by asymmetric cryptography structure.

5559
08:41:25,230 --> 08:41:33,764
由于密钥对是相互关联的，接收者无法截获消息，因为他们没有正确的私钥来解密信息。
Since the key pairs are related to each other, a receiver cannot intercept the
message since they didn't have the correct private keys to decrypt the information.

5560
08:41:34,254 --> 08:41:43,620
如果公钥能解密信息，发送者就无法拒绝用他的私钥进行签名，
否则就等于承认私钥不再是私有的了。
If a public key can decrypt the information, the sender cannot refuse signing it with
his private key without admitting the private key is not in fact private anymore.

5561
08:41:45,134 --> 08:41:48,452
加密过程比 DSA 算法更快。
The encryption process is faster than that of the DSA algorithm.

5562
08:41:49,038 --> 08:42:00,388
即使 RSA 的密钥生成较慢，但全球许多系统倾向于重复使用相同的密钥，
这样它们就可以减少在密钥生成上的时间，把更多时间花在实际的密文管理上。
Even if the key generation is slower in RSA, many systems across the world tend to reuse the same keys so that they can spend less
time in key generation and more time on actual ciphertext management.

5563
08:42:01,454 --> 08:42:06,852
数据在传输中将是防篡改的，因为篡改数据会改变密钥的使用。
Data will be tamper proof in transit since meddling with the data will alter the usage of the keys.

5564
08:42:07,342 --> 08:42:13,508
私钥将无法解密信息，从而提醒接收者中间存在任何形式的篡改。
The private key won't be able to decrypt the information, hence alerting the receiver of any kind of manipulation in between.

5565
08:42:14,094 --> 08:42:22,224
接收者必须警惕任何持有私钥的第三方，因为他们可
以在传输中途篡改数据，这种情况发生的概率相当低。
The receiver must be aware of any third party who possesses the private key
since they can alter the data mid-transit, the cases of which are rather low.

5566
08:42:22,510 --> 08:42:28,164
我们要对密码学做一个简短的回顾，了解密码学的类型以及我们今天的重点。
We're going to take a small recap on cryptography and understand the types of cryptography and our focus for the day.

5567
08:42:28,814 --> 08:42:31,716
然后我们深入探讨对称密钥加密及其工作原理。
We then dive into symmetric key cryptography and its working.

5568
08:42:32,078 --> 08:42:41,316
我们学习私钥加密背后的术语，学习目前使用的密码算法类型，以及使用对称密钥加密的优势。
We learn about the terminology behind private key cryptography, we learn the type
of ciphers being used today and the advantages of using symmetric key cryptography.

5569
08:42:43,150 --> 08:42:46,144
在我们继续前进之前，让我们做一个简短的回顾。
Let's have a small recap before we move ahead.

5570
08:42:47,118 --> 08:42:52,292
密码学是数据加密和解密的科学，旨在防止未经授权的访问。
Cryptography is the science of encryption and decryption of data to prevent unauthorized access.

5571
08:42:52,878 --> 08:42:59,108
加密是使明文对任何第三方都无法阅读的过程，它生成了密文。
Encryption is the process of making the plain text unreadable to any third party which generates the ciphertext.

5572
08:42:59,662 --> 08:43:05,796
解密是将加密文本还原回原始可读格式的过程，也就是明文。
Decryption of process of reversing the encrypted text back to its original readable format, that is the plain text.

5573
08:43:06,414 --> 08:43:10,596
如你在图片中看到的，例子中的明文是单词 study。
As you can see in the image, the plaintext in the example is the word study.

5574
08:43:11,246 --> 08:43:18,788
发送者使用加密密钥将明文转换为密文，对于没有解密密钥的人来说，它是无法阅读的。
The sender uses an encryption key to convert the plain text into ciphertext,
which will be unreadable to the people who don't have the decryption key.

5575
08:43:19,374 --> 08:43:22,948
密文可以是随机字母和数字的组合。
The ciphertext can be a combination of random alphanumeric characters.

5576
08:43:23,566 --> 08:43:31,140
然后它被直接发送给接收者，接收者再使用解密密钥将密文转换回明文，也就是单词 study。
It is then sent directly to the receiver who then converts the ciphertext
back to the plain text, that is the word study, using a decryption key.

5577
08:43:31,790 --> 08:43:39,716
根据所使用的密码学类型，解密密钥可以是与加密相同的密钥，也可以是完全不同的密钥。
Depending on the type of cryptography being used, the decryption key can
be the same key used for the encryption or it can be completely different.

5578
08:43:42,126 --> 08:43:49,764
密码学中有两种加密类型：对称密钥加密和非对称密钥加密。
There are two types of encryption in cryptography: symmetric key cryptography, and asymmetric key cryptography.

5579
08:43:50,414 --> 08:43:54,756
这两个类别都有各自的优缺点，区别仅在于它们的实现方式。
Both of these categories have their pros and cons and differ only by their implementation.

5580
08:43:55,470 --> 08:43:59,396
今天我们将专门关注对称密钥加密。
Today we are going to focus exclusively on symmetric key cryptography.

5581
08:44:01,070 --> 08:44:04,996
让我们看看它的应用，以便更好地理解它的重要性。
Let us have a look at its applications in order to understand its importance better.

5582
08:44:06,254 --> 08:44:13,764
这种密码学变体主要用于银行应用，其中需要对个人身份信息进行加密。
This variant of cryptography is primarily used in banking applications
where personally identifiable information needs to be encrypted.

5583
08:44:14,318 --> 08:44:19,876
随着银行的许多环节转向互联网，拥有可靠的安全网至关重要。
With so many aspects of banking moving on to the internet, having a reliable safety net is crucial.

5584
08:44:20,366 --> 08:44:26,852
对称加密有助于检测银行欺诈，并提升这些支付网关的整体安全指数。
Symmetric cryptography helps in detecting bank fraud and boosts the security index of these payment gateways in general.

5585
08:44:28,334 --> 08:44:33,988
它们还有助于保护非传输中、处于服务器和数据中心中的静态数据。
They are also helpful in protecting data that is not in transit and rest on servers and data centers.

5586
08:44:34,574 --> 08:44:46,628
这些中心存储了海量数据，需要使用快速高效的算法进行加密，
这样当相关服务需要调取数据时，可以确保几乎没有延迟。
These centers house a massive amount of data that needs to be encrypted with a fast and efficient algorithm so that when the data
needs to be recalled by the respective service, there is the assurance of minor to no delay.

5587
08:44:48,014 --> 08:44:55,140
在浏览互联网时，我们需要对称加密来访问安全的 HTTPS 网站，从而获得全方位的保护。
While browsing the internet, we need symmetric encryption to browse secure HTTPS websites so that we get an all-around protection.

5588
08:44:55,566 --> 08:45:06,564
它在验证网站服务器真实性、交换所需的加密密钥以及利用
这些密钥生成会话以确保最大安全性方面发挥着重要作用。
It plays a significant role in verifying website server authenticity, exchanging the necessary encryption keys required,
and generating a session using those keys to ensure maximum security.

5589
08:45:07,214 --> 08:45:11,492
这有助于我们防止使用安全性较低的 HTTP 网站格式。
This helps us in preventing the rather insecure HTTP website format.

5590
08:45:12,814 --> 08:45:18,564
所以，在进入具体算法之前，让我们先了解对称密钥加密的工作原理。
So let us understand how symmetric key cryptography works first before moving on to the specific algorithms.

5591
08:45:20,174 --> 08:45:25,412
对称密钥加密依赖于单个密钥来进行信息的加密和解密。
Symmetric key cryptography relies on a single key for the encryption and decryption of information.

5592
08:45:26,062 --> 08:45:34,468
消息的发送者和接收者都需要拥有一个预共享密钥，
他们将使用该密钥将明文转换为密文，反之亦然。
Both the sender and receiver of the message need to have a pre-shared secret
key that they will use to convert the plaintext into ciphertext and vice versa.

5593
08:45:34,990 --> 08:45:41,156
如图像所示，用于加密的密钥与另一端用于解密消息的密钥是相同的。
As you can see in the image, the key used for encryption is the same key needed for decrypting the message at the other end.

5594
08:45:41,614 --> 08:45:48,132
密钥不应随密文一起发送给接收者，因为那样就违背了使用密码学的整个目的。
The secret key shouldn't be sent along with the ciphertext to the receiver,
because that would defeat the entire purpose of using cryptography.

5595
08:45:48,654 --> 08:45:54,276
密钥交换可以提前完成，例如使用 Diffie Hellman 密钥交换协议等其他算法。
Key exchange can be done beforehand using other algorithms like the Diffie Hellman key exchange protocol, for example.

5596
08:45:56,302 --> 08:46:06,564
例如，如果 Paul 想给 Jane 发送一条简单消息，他们需要拥有一个共同的加密密钥，
且双方都必须保密，以防止恶意行为者窃听。
For example, if Paul wants to send a simple message to Jane, they need to have a single encryption key that both of them must keep
secret to prevent snooping on by malicious actors.

5597
08:46:08,014 --> 08:46:13,284
密钥可以由他们中的任何一方生成，但在消息开始传输前，必须双方都拥有该密钥。
It can be generated by either one of them, but must belong to both of them before the messages start flowing.

5598
08:46:13,934 --> 08:46:20,452
假设 Paul 使用特定的替换密码将我准备好的消息转换成密文。
Suppose the message I am ready is converted into ciphertext using a specific substitution cipher by Paul.

5599
08:46:20,848 --> 08:46:27,460
在这种情况下，Jane 也必须知道替换偏移量，以便在密文到达她手中时进行解密。
In that case, Jane must also be aware of the substitution shift to decrypt the ciphertext once it reaches her.

5600
08:46:28,462 --> 08:46:38,596
无论是否有人在传输过程中截获密文并试图读取消息，如果没有密钥，
所有试图窃听的人都会无功而返。
Irrespective of the scenario where someone manages to grab the ciphertext mid-transit to try and read the message,
not having the secret key renders everyone helpless looking to snoop in.

5601
08:46:39,470 --> 08:46:48,196
像数据加密标准这样的对称密钥算法自 20 世纪 70 年代以来就在使用，
而像 AES 这样流行的算法如今已成为行业标准。
The symmetric key algorithms like the data encryption standard have been in use since the 1970s,
while the popular ones like the AES have become the industry standard today.

5602
08:46:50,446 --> 08:47:00,036
由于对称加密的整个架构都依赖于使用的单个密钥，你
可以理解为什么在任何情况下保持其保密性都至关重要。
With the entire architecture of symmetric cryptography depending on the single key being used,
you can understand why it's of paramount importance to keep it secret on all occasions.

5603
08:47:01,358 --> 08:47:06,884
使用单个密钥进行加密和解密的副作用是，它成为了单点故障。
The side effect of having a single key for the encryption and decryption is it becomes a single point of failure.

5604
08:47:07,374 --> 08:47:14,628
任何拿到密钥的人都可以读取所有加密消息，而且
通常在发送者和接收者不知情的情况下完成此操作。
Anyone who gets their hand on it can read all the encrypted messages and
do so mainly without the knowledge of the sender and with the receiver.

5605
08:47:15,342 --> 08:47:19,684
所以，始终保持加密和解密密钥的私密性是重中之重。
So it is the priority to keep the encryption and decryption key private at all times.

5606
08:47:20,398 --> 08:47:27,556
如果密钥落入他人手中，第三方就可以使用相同的密钥，向发送者或接收者发送消息。
Should it fall into the wrong hands, the third party can send messages to
either the sender or the receiver using the same key to encrypt the message.

5607
08:47:28,014 --> 08:47:33,060
在收到消息并用密钥解密后，根本无法判断消息的来源。
Upon receiving the message and decrypting it with the key, it is impossible to guess its origin.

5608
08:47:33,870 --> 08:47:40,452
如果发送者在传输密文的同时也把密钥传了出去，任何人都能拦截数据包并获取信息。
If the sender somehow transmits the secret key along with the ciphertext, anyone can intercept the package and access the information.

5609
08:47:41,006 --> 08:47:50,724
因此，这种加密类别被称为私钥加密，因为数据完整性的很大一部分取决于用户能否保密密钥。
Consequently, this encryption category is termed private key cryptography, since a big part of the data's integrity is riding on the
promise that the users can keep the keys secret.

5610
08:47:51,214 --> 08:47:59,728
这个术语与非对称密钥加密形成对比，后者被称为公钥
加密，因为它涉及两个不同的密钥，其中一个是公开的。
This terminology contrasts with asymmetric key cryptography, which is called public key cryptography,
because it has two different keys at play, one of which is public.

5611
08:48:01,808 --> 08:48:08,772
只要我们能保密密钥，我们仍需选择使用哪种密码算法来加密这些信息。
Provided we manage to keep the keys secret, we still have to choose what kind of ciphers we want to use to encrypt this information.

5612
08:48:09,230 --> 08:48:13,728
在对称密钥加密中，我们大致可以使用两类密码算法。
In symmetric key cryptography, there are broadly two categories of ciphers that we can employ.

5613
08:48:13,998 --> 08:48:14,820
让我们来看看。
Let us have a look.

5614
08:48:16,846 --> 08:48:21,668
流加密是按位逐个加密基础信息的算法。
Stream ciphers are the algorithms that encrypt basic information one bit at a time.

5615
08:48:22,446 --> 08:48:29,252
这取决于所使用的算法，但通常它依赖于单个比特或字节来进行加密。
It can change depending on the algorithm being used, but usually it relies on a single bit or byte to do the encryption.

5616
08:48:29,966 --> 08:48:36,004
考虑到算法不需要同时处理数据块，这是一种相对较快的选择。
This is the relatively quicker alternative considering the algorithm doesn't have to deal with blocks of data at a single time.

5617
08:48:36,654 --> 08:48:42,020
进入加密过程的每一条数据都可以且必须转换为二进制格式。
Every piece of data that goes into the encryption can and needs to be converted into binary format.

5618
08:48:42,368 --> 08:48:46,564
在流加密中，每个二进制数字都是按顺序依次加密的。
In stream ciphers, each binary digit is encrypted one after the other.

5619
08:48:47,086 --> 08:48:51,268
最流行的包括 RC4、salsa 和 Panama。
The most popular ones are the RC4, salsa, and Panama.

5620
08:48:52,014 --> 08:48:56,580
二进制数据通过一个加密密钥，即一个随机生成的比特流。
The binary data is passed through an encryption key, which is a randomly generated bitstream.

5621
08:48:57,134 --> 08:49:03,460
通过处理后，我们得到密文，它可以安全地传输给接收者，不用担心中间人攻击。
Upon passing it through, we receive the ciphertext that can be transferred to the receiver without fear of man-in-the-middle attacks.

5622
08:49:04,142 --> 08:49:06,884
二进制数据可以经过一个算法函数。
The binary data can be passed through an algorithmic function.

5623
08:49:07,406 --> 08:49:14,724
它可以是大多数情况下的 XOR 操作，也可以是任何旨在打乱数据的数学计算。
It can have either XOR operations as it is most of the time, or any other
mathematical calculations that have the singular purpose of scrambling the data.

5624
08:49:15,342 --> 08:49:21,668
加密密钥是使用随机比特流生成器生成的，它作为算法函数的一个补充。
The encryption key is generated using the random bitstream generator and it acts as a supplement in the algorithmic function.

5625
08:49:22,158 --> 08:49:28,708
输出是二进制形式，然后转换为十进制或十六进制格式，从而得到最终的密文。
The output is in binary form, which is then converted into the decimal or hexadecimal format to give our final ciphertext.

5626
08:49:31,598 --> 08:49:36,964
另一方面，分组密码将原始信息分割成固定大小的数据块。
On the other hand, block ciphers dissect the raw information into chunks of data of fixed size.

5627
08:49:37,390 --> 08:49:40,528
这些块的大小取决于所使用的具体加密算法。
The size of these blocks depends on the exact cipher being used.

5628
08:49:40,814 --> 08:49:48,388
128 位分组密码会将明文分解为每个 128 位的块，并加密这些块而不是单个数字。
A 128-bit block cipher will break the plaintext into blocks of 128-bit each and encrypt those blocks instead of a single digit.

5629
08:49:49,038 --> 08:49:54,052
一旦这些块被分别加密，它们就会串联在一起形成最终的密文。
Once these blocks are encrypted individually, they are chained together to form a final ciphertext.

5630
08:49:55,726 --> 08:50:02,724
分组密码速度慢得多，但它们更防篡改，并被用于当今一些最广泛使用的算法中。
Block ciphers are much slower, but they are more tamper-proof and are used in some of the most widely used algorithms employed today.

5631
08:50:04,750 --> 08:50:10,180
与流加密一样，在开始处理之前，原始密文会被转换为二进制格式。
Just like stream ciphers, the original ciphertext is converted into binary format before beginning the process.

5632
08:50:10,702 --> 08:50:17,168
转换完成后，这些块会连同加密密钥一起传递给加密算法。
Once the conversion is complete, the blocks are passed to the encryption algorithm along with the encryption key.

5633
08:50:17,582 --> 08:50:22,276
这将为我们提供加密后的二进制数据块。
This would provide us with the encrypted blocks of binary data.

5634
08:50:24,142 --> 08:50:27,908
一旦这些块合并，我们就得到了最终的二进制字符串。
Once these blocks are combined, we get a final binary string.

5635
08:50:30,894 --> 08:50:34,724
这个字符串随后被转换为十六进制格式，从而得到我们的密文。
This string is then converted into hexadecimal format to get our ciphertext.

5636
08:50:35,342 --> 08:50:43,076
如今最流行的对称密钥算法，如 AES、DES 和 3DES，都是分组密码方法的子集。
Today the most popular symmetric key algorithms like AES, DES, and 3DES are all block cipher methodology subsets.

5637
08:50:45,070 --> 08:50:51,908
由于涉及众多因素，对称密钥加密在某些方面表现出色，但在其他方面则有所不足。
With so many factors coming into play, there are quite a few things
symmetric key cryptography excels at while falling short in some other.

5638
08:50:54,478 --> 08:51:00,036
与非对称密钥加密相比，对称密钥加密是速度快得多的变体。
Symmetric key cryptography is much faster variant when compared to asymmetric key cryptography.

5639
08:51:00,494 --> 08:51:07,908
与非对称加密不同，这里只有一把密钥，这大大提高了加密和解密时的计算速度。
There is only one key in play, unlike asymmetric encryption, and this
drastically improves calculation speed in the encryption and decryption.

5640
08:51:08,558 --> 08:51:14,628
同样，在类似的计算限制下，对称加密的性能要高效得多。
Similarly, the performance of symmetric encryption is much more efficient under similar computational limitations.

5641
08:51:15,022 --> 08:51:18,308
更少的计算有助于宿主机更好地进行内存管理。
Fewer calculations help in better memory management for the host system.

5642
08:51:19,534 --> 08:51:24,484
需要加密的海量数据非常适合使用对称算法。
Bulk amounts of data that need to be encrypted are very well suited for symmetric algorithms.

5643
08:51:24,910 --> 08:51:30,948
因为它们速度快得多，处理大量数据在服务器和数据中心中非常简单且易于使用。
Since they are much quicker, handling large amounts of data is simple and easy to use in servers and data farms.

5644
08:51:31,278 --> 08:51:35,236
这有助于在数据检索过程中降低延迟，并减少数据包混淆。
This helps in better latency during data recall and fewer mixed packets.

5645
08:51:36,110 --> 08:51:46,244
由于其简单的单密钥结构，对称密钥加密算法更容易建立通信信道，且维护工作也更简单。
Thanks to its simple single key structure, symmetric key cryptography algorithms are much easier to set up a communication channel
with and offer a much more straightforward maintenance duties.

5646
08:51:46,734 --> 08:51:56,772
一旦密钥在没有事先疏忽的情况下传输给发送者和接收者，
剩下的系统就能轻松对齐，日常通信也会变得简单且安全。
Once the secret key is transmitted to both the sender and receiver without any prior mishandling,
the rest of the system aligns easily and everyday communications becomes easy and secure.

5647
08:51:57,294 --> 08:52:05,572
如果按照文档要求应用算法，对称算法非常稳健，可以用极低的开销加密海量数据。
If the algorithm is applied as per the documentation, symmetric algorithms
are very robust and can encrypt vast amounts of data with very less overhead.

5648
08:52:06,382 --> 08:52:07,172
让我们认识一下 Joe。
Let's meet Joe.

5649
08:52:07,982 --> 08:52:12,260
Joe 是一名记者，他需要通过远程消息与 Ryan 进行沟通。
Joe is a journalist who needs to communicate with Ryan via long distance messaging.

5650
08:52:12,942 --> 08:52:18,916
由于信息的关键性，人们正等待任何消息离开 Joe 家，以便截获它。
Due to the critical nature of the information, people are waiting for any message to leave Joe's house so that they can intercept it.

5651
08:52:19,630 --> 08:52:27,396
现在 Joe 可以轻松使用对称密钥加密来发送加密数据，
这样即使有人截获了消息，也无法理解其中的内容。
Now Joe can easily use symmetric key cryptography to send the encrypted data so
that even if someone intercepts the message, they cannot understand what it says.

5652
08:52:27,728 --> 08:52:29,028
但这里有个棘手的问题。
But here's the tricky part.

5653
08:52:29,582 --> 08:52:32,388
Joe 该如何把所需的解密密钥发送给 Ryan 呢？
How will Joe send the required decryption key to Ryan?

5654
08:52:33,006 --> 08:52:39,428
消息的发送者和接收者都需要拥有相同的解密密钥，这样他们才能交换消息。
The sender of the message as well as the receiver need to have the same decryption key so that they can exchange messages.

5655
08:52:39,758 --> 08:52:44,196
否则，即使 Ryan 收到了密文，也无法解密信息。
Otherwise, Ryan cannot decrypt the information even when he receives the ciphertext.

5656
08:52:44,686 --> 08:52:52,292
如果有人在传输过程中截获了密钥，那么使用密码学就毫无意义了，
因为第三方现在可以轻松解码所有信息。
If someone intercepts the key while transmitting it, there is no use in employing
cryptography since the third party can now decode all the information easily.

5657
08:52:52,910 --> 08:52:57,444
密钥共享是使用对称密钥加密时始终存在的风险。
Key sharing is a risk that will always exist when symmetric key cryptography is being used.

5658
08:52:57,966 --> 08:53:01,732
幸运的是，非对称密钥加密已经解决了这个问题。
Thankfully, asymmetric key encryption has managed to fix this problem.

5659
08:53:02,862 --> 08:53:07,108
我是来自 Simplilearn 的 Beba，欢迎来到这个关于非对称密钥加密的视频。
This is Beba from Simply Learn and welcome to this video on asymmetric key cryptography.

5660
08:53:07,790 --> 08:53:09,924
让我们来看看我们今天要学什么。
Let's take a look at what we are going to learn today.

5661
08:53:10,574 --> 08:53:14,916
我们首先解释什么是非对称密钥加密以及它是如何工作的。
We begin by explaining what asymmetric key cryptography is and how it works.

5662
08:53:15,566 --> 08:53:29,956
我们将了解它的应用和用途，理解为什么它被称为公钥加密，然后学习一点关于 RSA 加密的内容，
接着我们将学习非对称密钥加密优于对称密钥加密的优点。
We take a look at its application and uses, we understand why it's called public key cryptography and then learn a little bit about
RSA encryption, and then we learn about the advantages of asymmetric key cryptography over symmetric key cryptography.

5663
08:53:30,990 --> 08:53:33,636
让我们来了解什么是非对称密钥加密。
Let's understand what asymmetric key cryptography is.

5664
08:53:36,078 --> 08:53:39,460
非对称加密使用双层保护。
Asymmetric encryption uses a double layer of protection.

5665
08:53:40,046 --> 08:53:43,716
这里涉及两种不同的密钥：私钥和公钥。
There are two different keys at play here: a private key and a public key.

5666
08:53:44,334 --> 08:53:51,108
公钥用于在传输前加密信息，私钥用于在传输后解密数据。
A public key is used to encrypt the information pre-transit, and a private key is used to decrypt the data post-transit.

5667
08:53:51,758 --> 08:53:54,948
这一对密钥必须属于消息的接收者。
These pair of keys must belong to the receiver of the message.

5668
08:53:55,406 --> 08:54:00,708
公钥可以通过消息、博客文章或密钥服务器共享，没有任何限制。
The public keys can be shared via messaging, blog posts, or key servers, and there are no restrictions.

5669
08:54:01,344 --> 08:54:04,740
正如你在图像中看到的，这两个密钥在系统中协同工作。
As you can see in the image, the two keys are working in the system.

5670
08:54:05,198 --> 08:54:10,788
发送者首先使用接收者的私钥加密消息，然后我们收到密文。
The sender first encrypts the message using the receiver's private key, after which we receive the ciphertext.

5671
08:54:11,246 --> 08:54:14,436
密文随后被传输给接收者，不需要任何其他密钥。
The ciphertext is then transmitted to the receiver without any other key.

5672
08:54:14,894 --> 08:54:20,292
收到密文后，接收者使用他的私钥对其进行解密，从而还原出明文。
On getting the ciphertext, the receiver uses his private key to decrypt it and get the plaintext back.

5673
08:54:20,704 --> 08:54:28,932
整个过程中不需要任何密钥交换，因此解决了对称密钥加密面临的最明显的缺陷。
There has been no requirement of any key exchange throughout this process,
therefore solving the most glaring flaw faced in symmetry key cryptography.

5674
08:54:29,838 --> 08:54:37,124
众所周知的公钥无法用于解密消息，而能够解密消息的私钥则不需要与任何人共享。
The public key known to everyone cannot be used to decrypt the message, and
the private key which can decrypt the message need not be shared with anyone.

5675
08:54:37,614 --> 08:54:42,692
发送者和接收者可以使用同一组密钥尽可能频繁地交换个人数据。
The sender and receiver can exchange personal data using the same set of keys as often as possible.

5676
08:54:44,064 --> 08:54:47,940
为了更好地理解这一点，我们可以用你的邮箱做个类比。
To understand this better, take the analogy of your mailbox.

5677
08:54:48,782 --> 08:54:53,956
任何想要给你寄信的人都可以接触到这个邮箱，并能轻松地与你共享信息。
Anyone who wants to send you a letter has access to the box and can easily share information with you.

5678
08:54:54,670 --> 08:55:03,108
从某种程度上说，你可以说邮箱是所有人都可以使用
的，但只有你能拥有打开邮箱并读取其中信件的钥匙。
In a way, you can say the mailbox is publicly available to all, but only you
have access to the key that can open the mailbox and read the letters in it.

5679
08:55:04,206 --> 08:55:06,384
这就是私钥发挥作用的方式。
This is how the private key comes to play.

5680
08:55:06,670 --> 08:55:10,596
由于消息是加密的，没有人能截获消息并读取其内容。
No one can intercept the message and read its contents since it's encrypted.

5681
08:55:11,214 --> 08:55:15,972
一旦接收者拿到内容，他就可以使用自己的私钥来解密信息。
Once the receiver gets its contents, he can use his private key to decrypt the information.

5682
08:55:16,686 --> 08:55:23,716
公钥和私钥都是生成的，它们是相互关联的，你不能用其他的私钥来解密数据。
Both the public key and the private key are generated so they are
interlinked and you cannot substitute other private keys to decrypt the data.

5683
08:55:24,686 --> 08:55:30,308
再举个例子，如果 Alice 想给 Bob 发个消息，假设内容是「今天叫我」。
In another example, if Alice wants to send a message to Bob, let's say it reads call me today.

5684
08:55:30,638 --> 08:55:33,444
她在加密消息时必须使用 Bob 的公钥。
She must use Bob's public key while encrypting the message.

5685
08:55:33,934 --> 08:55:44,932
收到加密消息后，Bob 可以使用他的私钥来解密消息，从
而在无需共享密钥的情况下实现传输过程中的完全安全性。
Upon receiving the cipher message, Bob can proceed to use his private key in order to decrypt the message and hence complete security
is attained during transmission without any need for sharing the key.

5686
08:55:48,494 --> 08:55:54,660
由于这种加密方式高度安全，它在许多需要高机密性的领域都有广泛应用。
Since this type of encryption is highly secure, it has many uses in areas that require high confidentiality.

5687
08:55:55,982 --> 08:56:00,932
它被用于管理数字签名，从而为文件的真实性提供有效的证明。
It is used to manage digital signatures, so there is valid proof of a document's authenticity.

5688
08:56:01,582 --> 08:56:09,572
随着商业的许多方面转向数字化，关键文件在被视为真实并采取行动之前，需要经过验证。
With so many aspects of business transitioning to the digital sphere, critical
documents need to be verified before being considered authentic and acted upon.

5689
08:56:10,062 --> 08:56:14,788
得益于非对称密钥加密，发送者现在可以用他们的私钥来签署文件。
Thanks to asymmetric key cryptography, senders can now sign documents with their private keys.

5690
08:56:15,184 --> 08:56:21,316
任何需要验证此类签名真实性的人，都可以使用发送者的公钥来解密签名。
Anyone who needs to verify the authenticity of such signatures can use the sender's public key to decrypt the signature.

5691
08:56:21,934 --> 08:56:28,996
由于公钥和私钥在数学上是相互关联的，使用重复的密钥无法重复此验证过程。
Since the public and the private keys are linked to each other mathematically,
it's impossible to repeat this verification with duplicate keys.

5692
08:56:29,582 --> 08:56:35,908
按照今天的标准，文件加密已经变得非常简单，但背后的实现原理与之类似。
Document encryption has been made very simple by today's standards, but the background implementation follows a similar approach.

5693
08:56:37,006 --> 08:56:43,140
在区块链架构中，非对称密钥加密被用于授权交易并维护系统。
In blockchain architecture, asymmetric key cryptography is used to authorize transactions and maintain the system.

5694
08:56:43,662 --> 08:56:50,692
得益于其双密钥结构，只有在两端都获得批准的情况下，更改才会反映到区块链的点对点网络中。
Thanks to its two key structures, changes are reflected across the
blockchain's peer-to-peer network only if it is approved from both ends.

5695
08:56:51,310 --> 08:56:59,140
除了非对称密钥加密的防篡改架构外，它的不可分派性特征也有助于保持网络稳定。
Along with asymmetric key cryptography's tamper proof architecture, its
non-repartiation characteristic also helps in keeping the network stable.

5696
08:57:00,494 --> 08:57:14,116
我们还可以将非对称密钥加密与对称密钥加密结合，来监控 SSL 或 TLS 加密的浏览会话，
确保在访问银行网站或一般互联网时，不会有人窃取个人信息。
We can also use asymmetric key cryptography combined with symmetric key cryptography to monitor SSL or TLS encrypted browsing sessions
to make sure nobody can steal up personal information when accessing banking websites or the internet in general.

5697
08:57:14,702 --> 08:57:28,708
它在验证网站服务器真实性、交换所需的加密密钥，以及利用这些密钥生成会话方面发挥着重要
作用，从而确保比安全性较低的 HTTP 网站格式更高的安全性。
It plays a significant role in verifying website server authenticity, exchanging the necessary encryption keys required,
and generating a session using those keys to ensure maximum security instead of the rather insecure HTTP website format.

5698
08:57:29,262 --> 08:57:37,060
安全参数在每个会话中都不同，因此验证过程是高度一致的，且对现代数据安全至关重要。
Security parameters differ on a session-by-session basis, so the verification
process is consistent and utterly essential to modern data security.

5699
08:57:38,190 --> 08:57:44,548
非对称密钥加密结构的另一个重要用途是传输对称密钥加密的密钥。
Another great use of the asymmetric key cryptography structure is transmitting keys for symmetric key cryptography.

5700
08:57:45,006 --> 08:57:51,556
由于对称加密最大的困难在于密钥交换，非对称密钥可以帮助消除这一缺陷。
With the most significant difficulty in symmetric encryption being key exchange, asymmetric keys can help clear the shortcoming.

5701
08:57:52,078 --> 08:57:55,396
原始信息首先使用对称密钥进行加密。
The original message is first encrypted using a symmetric key.

5702
08:57:55,726 --> 08:58:00,932
用于加密数据的密钥随后使用接收者的公钥转换为密文。
The key used for encrypting the data is then converted into the ciphertext using the receiver's public key.

5703
08:58:01,454 --> 08:58:03,940
现在我们有了两个密文要发送给接收者。
Now we have two ciphertexts to transmit to the receiver.

5704
08:58:04,384 --> 08:58:08,932
接收到这两个密文后，接收者使用他的私钥来解密对称密钥。
On receiving both of them, the receiver uses his private key to decrypt the symmetric key.

5705
08:58:09,326 --> 08:58:14,436
获取用于加密数据的密钥后，他就可以用它来解密原始信息。
He can then use it to decrypt the original information on getting the key used to encrypt the data.

5706
08:58:14,990 --> 08:58:24,644
虽然这看起来比单纯使用非对称密钥加密更复杂，但在某些情况下，
对称加密算法在处理海量数据时优化得更好。
While this may seem more complicated than just asymmetric key cryptography alone,
symmetric encryption algorithms are much more optimized for vast amounts of data on some occasions.

5707
08:58:25,550 --> 08:58:30,980
使用非对称算法加密密钥，无疑会更节省内存且更安全。
Encrypting the key using asymmetric algorithms will definitely be more memory efficient and secure.

5708
08:58:32,878 --> 08:58:37,540
你们可能还记得我们讨论过为什么对称加密被称为私钥加密。
You might remember us discussing why symmetric encryption was called private key cryptography.

5709
08:58:38,158 --> 08:58:41,508
让我们来了解一下为什么非对称加密属于公钥加密。
Let us understand why asymmetric falls under the public key cryptography.

5710
08:58:42,734 --> 08:58:44,452
我们手头有两种密钥。
We have two keys at our disposal.

5711
08:58:45,038 --> 08:58:47,300
加密密钥对所有人开放。
The encryption key is available to everyone.

5712
08:58:48,270 --> 08:58:50,500
解密密钥应该是私有的。
The decryption key is supposed to be private.

5713
08:58:52,206 --> 08:58:58,180
与对称密钥加密不同，要建立加密消息系统，不需要私下共享任何内容。
Unlike symmetric key cryptography, there is no need to share anything privately to have an encrypted messaging system.

5714
08:58:58,702 --> 08:59:03,748
打个比方，我们会把电子邮件地址分享给任何想要与我们联系的人。
To put that into perspective, we share our email address with anyone looking to communicate with us.

5715
08:59:04,142 --> 08:59:11,748
它的设计初衷就是公开的，这样我们的电子邮件登
录凭据就是私有的，这有助于防止任何数据误用。
It is supposed to be public by design so that our email login
credentials are private and they help in preventing any data mishandling.

5716
08:59:12,128 --> 08:59:19,460
既然他们想给我们发送任何加密信息时不需要隐藏任何内容，这一类别就被称为公钥加密。
Since there is nothing hidden from the world if they want to send us any encrypted information,
this category is called the public key cryptography.

5717
08:59:21,678 --> 08:59:29,348
如今有相当多的算法遵循非对称密钥加密的架构，其中最著名的就是 RSA 加密。
There are quite a few algorithms being used today that follow the architecture
of asymmetric key cryptography, none more famous than the RSA encryption.

5718
08:59:30,414 --> 08:59:37,028
RSA 加密是使用非对称密钥方法的最广泛使用的加密或公钥加密标准。
RSA encryption is the most widely used encryption or public key encryption standard using asymmetric key approach.

5719
08:59:37,550 --> 08:59:43,780
它以其创始人 Rivest、Shamir 和 Adleman 的名字命名，它使用分组加密来隐藏信息。
Named after its founders Revest, Shamir, and Edelman, it uses block ciphers to obscure the information.

5720
08:59:44,430 --> 08:59:51,908
如果你不熟悉分组加密的工作原理，它们是把原始数据分成等大小块的加密算法。
If you are unfamiliar with how block ciphers work, they are encryption
algorithms that divide the original data into blocks of equal size.

5721
08:59:52,526 --> 08:59:55,172
块大小取决于所使用的具体加密算法。
The block size depends on the exact cipher being used.

5722
08:59:55,566 --> 09:00:02,468
一旦分解，这些块就会被单独加密，稍后串联在一起形成最终的密文。
Once they are broken down, these blocks are encrypted individually and later chained together to form the final ciphertext.

5723
09:00:03,662 --> 09:00:17,636
它被广泛认为是安全性最高的加密形式，尽管比对称加密算法稍慢一些，
但它广泛应用于网页浏览、安全身份验证、VPN、电子邮件和其他聊天应用。
Widely considered to be the most secure form of encryption, albeit relatively slower than symmetric encryption algorithms,
it is widely used in web browsing, secure identification, VPNs, emails, and other chat applications.

5724
09:00:18,830 --> 09:00:27,364
考虑到这么多变量，非对称密钥加密肯定有一些优势，使其优于传统的对称加密方法。
With so many variables in play, there must be some advantages that give asymmetric
key cryptography an edge over the traditional symmetric encryption methodologies.

5725
09:00:27,950 --> 09:00:29,124
让我们来看看其中的一些内容。
Let's go through some of them.

5726
09:00:31,278 --> 09:00:35,620
在非对称加密中，不需要任何可靠的密钥共享信道。
There is no need for any reliable key sharing channel in asymmetric encryption.

5727
09:00:36,078 --> 09:00:41,796
私钥加密中存在的一种额外风险，在公钥架构中已被完全消除。
It was an added risk in private key cryptography that has been completely eliminated in public key architecture.

5728
09:00:42,382 --> 09:00:51,268
公开的密钥无法解密任何机密信息，而唯一能够解密的密钥在任何情况下都不需要公开共享。
The key which is made public cannot decrypt any confidential information, and the
only key that can decrypt doesn't need to be shared publicly under any circumstance.

5729
09:00:52,366 --> 09:01:00,900
我们在 RSA 加密和其他非对称算法中拥有更广泛的密钥长度，
例如 2048-bit 密钥和 4096-bit 密钥。
We have much more extensive key lengths in RSA encryption and other asymmetric algorithms like 2048-bit key and 4096-bit keys.

5730
09:01:01,486 --> 09:01:05,732
更大的密钥更难通过暴力破解攻破，安全性也更高。
Larger keys are much harder to break into via brute force and are much more secure.

5731
09:01:07,278 --> 09:01:15,844
非对称密钥加密可作为真实性证明，因为只有密钥的合法所有者才能生成由私钥解密的报文。
Asymmetric key cryptography can be used as a proof of authenticity, since only the
rightful owner of the keys can generate the messages to be decrypted by the private key.

5732
09:01:16,334 --> 09:01:18,128
这种情况也可以反过来。
The situation can also be reversed.

5733
09:01:18,446 --> 09:01:29,124
使用私钥进行加密，使用公钥进行解密，如果没用正确的私
钥生成报文，就无法正常工作，从而证明了所有者的真实性。
Encryption is done using a private key and decryption is done by the public key, which would not function if the correct private key
is not used to generate the message, hence, proving the authenticity of the owner.

5734
09:01:29,728 --> 09:01:37,764
它还具有防篡改保护功能，在不使用于加密数据的私钥失效的情况下，报文无法被拦截和篡改。
It also has a tamper protection feature where the message cannot be intercepted
and changed without invalidating the private key used to encrypt the data.

5735
09:01:38,478 --> 09:01:47,748
因此，公钥无法解密报文，而且在需要时很容易发现信息并非 100% 合法。
Consequently, the public key cannot decrypt the message and it is easy to
realize the information is not 100% legitimate when and where the case requires.

5736
09:01:48,462 --> 09:01:53,732
这是一种对称密钥加密算法，用于以分组方式对信息进行加密和重加密。
It is a symmetric key cipher that is used to encrypt and recrypt information in a block-by-block manner.

5737
09:01:54,542 --> 09:02:01,348
每个分组单独加密，然后它们被串联在一起形成最终的密文，随后发送给接收者。
Each block is encrypted individually and they are later chained
together to form our final ciphertext, which is then sent to a receiver.

5738
09:02:02,611 --> 09:02:11,076
DES 将被称为明文的原始未更改数据放入 64-bit 分组中，并将其转换为被称为密文的加密文本。
DES takes the original unaltered piece of data called the plain text in a 64-bit
block and it is converted into an encrypted text that is called the ciphertext.

5739
09:02:11,950 --> 09:02:19,716
它在加密过程中使用 48-bit 密钥，并在整个过程中遵
循一种称为 Feistel cipher structure 的特定结构。
It uses 48-bit keys during the encryption process and follows a specific
structure called the Fistal cipherstructure during the entire process.

5740
09:02:20,558 --> 09:02:29,060
它是一种对称密钥算法，这意味着 DES 可以使用加密格式中相同的密钥将密文解密回原始明文。
It is a symmetric key algorithm, which means DES can reuse the keys used in
the encryption format to decrypt the ciphertext back to the original plaintext.

5741
09:02:29,518 --> 09:02:34,596
一旦 64-bit 分组被加密，它们就可以在传输前组合在一起。
Once the 64 bit blocks are encrypted, they can be combined together before being transmitted.

5742
09:02:36,238 --> 09:02:39,588
让我们来看看 DES 的起源和创立原因。
Let's take a look at the origin and the reason DES was founded.

5743
09:02:41,518 --> 09:02:49,668
DES 基于一种名为 Lucifer 的 Feistel block cipher，
由 IBM 密码学研究员 Horst Fistel 于 1971 年开发。
DES is based on a fistal block cipher called Lucifer developed in 1971 by IBM cryptography researcher Horst Fistel.

5744
09:02:50,286 --> 09:02:54,724
DES 使用该 Feistel 结构的 16 轮，每轮使用不同的密钥。
DES uses 16 rounds of this fistal structure using a different key for each round.

5745
09:02:55,246 --> 09:03:00,164
它还利用一个具有两个输入并提供单个输出变量的随机函数。
It also utilizes a random function with two inputs and provides a single output variable.

5746
09:03:01,198 --> 09:03:12,516
DES 于 1976 年 11 月成为该机构批准的加密标准，并随后在 1983 年、
1988 年以及最终在 1999 年再次被确认作为标准。
DES became the organization's approved encryption standard in November 1976
and was later reaffirmed as a standard in 1983, 1988, and finally in 1999.

5747
09:03:13,006 --> 09:03:19,972
但最终 DES 被破解，不再被认为是所有官方通信渠道的安全解决方案。
But eventually DES was cracked and it was no longer considered a secure solution for all official routes of communication.

5748
09:03:20,846 --> 09:03:23,236
因此，开发了三重DES。
Consequently, triple DES was developed.

5749
09:03:23,758 --> 09:03:28,228
三重DES是一种使用双重DES加密的对称密钥分组密码。
Triple DES is a symmetric key block cipher that uses a double DES cipher.

5750
09:03:28,814 --> 09:03:34,404
用第一个密钥加密，用第二个密钥解密，再用第三个密钥加密。
Encrypt with the first key, delete encryption with the second key, and encrypt again with the third key.

5751
09:03:34,958 --> 09:03:39,812
还有一种两种密钥的变体，其中第一个和第二个密钥是彼此重复的。
There is also a variation of the two keys where the first and second key are duplicate of each other.

5752
09:03:40,334 --> 09:03:49,092
但三重DES最终被认为对于日益增长的快速通信信道需求来说太慢了，
人们最终退回到使用 DES 来加密消息。
But triple DES was ultimately deemed too slow for the growing need for fast communication channels,
and people eventually fell back to using DS for encrypting messages.

5753
09:03:49,870 --> 09:04:00,292
为了寻找更好的替代方案，组织了一场全行业的竞赛，帮
助密码学家开发自己的算法作为下一代全球标准的提案。
In order to search for a better alternative, a public-wide competition was organized and helped cryptographers develop their own
algorithm as a proposal for the next global standard.

5754
09:04:00,942 --> 09:04:07,236
这就是 Rijndael算法发挥作用的地方，它后来被认为是下一个高级加密标准。
This is where the Ring Dial algorithm came into play and was later credited to be the next advanced encryption standard.

5755
09:04:07,982 --> 09:04:12,004
在很长一段时间里，DES一直是数据加密和数据安全的标准。
For a long time, DES was the standard for data encryption for data security.

5756
09:04:12,590 --> 09:04:21,764
它的统治在2002年结束，当时高级加密标准在公开竞赛中胜出，取代了DES成为公认的标准。
Its rule ended in 2002 when finally the advanced encryption standard replaced
DES as an acceptable standard following a public competition for a place.

5757
09:04:23,918 --> 09:04:28,612
为了理解 Feistel cipher 的结构，我们可以参考这张图。
To understand the structure of a Fistal cipher, we can use the following image as a reference.

5758
09:04:29,198 --> 09:04:37,476
被加密的分组被分成两部分，其中一部分传递给函数，另一部分与函数的输出进行 XOR 运算。
The block being encrypted is divided into two parts, one of which is being passed on to the function,
while the other part is XORed with the function's output.

5759
09:04:38,126 --> 09:04:42,212
该函数还使用每一轮都不同的加密密钥。
The function also uses the encryption key that differs for each individual round.

5760
09:04:42,990 --> 09:04:49,348
这个过程一直持续到最后一步，直到左右两部分交换位置。
This keeps going on until the last step until where the right hand side and the left hand side are being swapped.

5761
09:04:49,838 --> 09:04:51,780
在这里，我们得到了最终的密文。
Here we receive our final ciphertext.

5762
09:04:52,558 --> 09:04:59,492
在解密过程中，整个过程是反向进行的，从密钥顺序到分组排序全部反转。
For the decryption process, the entire procedure is reversed, starting from the order of the keys to the block sorting.

5763
09:04:59,982 --> 09:05:07,236
如果按相反顺序重复整个过程，我们最终就能找回明文，这种简洁性有助于提高速度。
If the entire process is repeated in a reverse order, we will eventually get back our plain text, and this simplicity helps the speed.

5764
09:05:07,822 --> 09:05:13,764
总的来说，这后来损害了算法的效率，因此安全性被入侵。
Overall, this was later detrimental to the efficiency of the algorithm, hence, the security was compromised.

5765
09:05:16,238 --> 09:05:23,716
Feistel block cipher 是一种用于推导许多对称分组密码的结构，比如我们之前提到的 DES。
A fistal block cipher is a structure used to derive many symmetric block ciphers such as DES,
which as we have discussed in our previous comment.

5766
09:05:24,814 --> 09:05:32,964
Feistel cipher 提出了一种交替执行置换与置换的
结构，这样我们就可以从明文获得密文，反之亦然。
Fistal cipher proposed a structure that implements substitution and permutation
alternately so that we can obtain ciphertext from the plain text and vice versa.

5767
09:05:33,454 --> 09:05:39,620
这有助于减少程序的冗余，并增加复杂度以对抗暴力破解攻击。
This helps in reducing the redundancy of the program and increases the complexity to combat brute force attacks.

5768
09:05:41,006 --> 09:05:46,084
Feistel cipher 实际上是基于1945年提出的 Shannon 结构。
The fistal cipher is actually based on the Shannon structure that was proposed in 1945.

5769
09:05:46,638 --> 09:05:54,052
Feistel cipher 是由 Horst Feistel 提出的结构，在开发许多对称分组密码时被视为核心架构。
The fistel cipher is the structure suggested by Horst Feistel, which was
considered to be a backbone while developing many symmetric block ciphers.

5770
09:05:54,990 --> 09:05:59,108
Shannon 结构强调了交替混淆和扩散的实现。
The Shannon structure highlights the implementation of alternate confusion and diffusion.

5771
09:06:00,014 --> 09:06:05,540
正如我们之前讨论过的，Feistel cipher 结构可以根据数据完全反转。
And like we already discussed, the fistal cipher structure can be completely reversed depending on the data.

5772
09:06:06,062 --> 09:06:15,140
然而，我们必须考虑到，要通过反转 Feistel 结构来解密信息，
我们需要精确的多项式函数和密钥顺序。
However, we must consider the fact that to decrypt the information by reversing the fistal structure,
we will need the exact polynomial functions and the key orders.

5773
09:06:17,197 --> 09:06:26,915
为了理解分组是如何计算的，我们取一个 64-bit 的明文，并将其分成两个相等的 32-bit 部分。
To understand how the blocks are being calculated, we take a plaintext which
is of 64 bit and with it is later divided into two equal halves of 32 bit each.

5774
09:06:27,982 --> 09:06:33,796
其中，右半部分立即传递到下一轮，成为第二轮的新左半部分。
In this, the right half is immediately transferred to the next round to become the new left half of the second round.

5775
09:06:34,733 --> 09:06:42,372
右半部分再次传递给一个函数，该函数在 Feistel cipher 中为每一轮使用唯一的加密密钥。
The right hand is again passed off to a function which uses an encryption key that is unique to each round in the fistal cipher.

5776
09:06:42,894 --> 09:06:50,116
无论函数输出什么，它都会作为 XOR 输入与初始明文的左半部分结合。
Whatever the function gives off as an output, it is passed on as an XOR input with the left half of the initial plain text.

5777
09:06:50,798 --> 09:06:55,428
下一个输出将成为明文第二轮的右半部分。
The next output will become the right half of the second round for the plain text.

5778
09:06:56,046 --> 09:07:00,464
整个过程构成 Feistel cipher 中的单轮。
This entire process constitutes of a single round in the fistal cipher.

5779
09:07:01,485 --> 09:07:09,284
考虑到多项式函数中发生的情况，我们取分组的一半并将其通过扩展盒。
Taking into account what happens in a polynomial function, we take one half of the block and pass it through an expansion box.

5780
09:07:09,710 --> 09:07:16,644
扩展盒的作用是将半部分的大小从 32-bit 增加到 48-bit 文本。
The work of the expansion box is to increase the size of the half from 32-bit to 48-bit text.

5781
09:07:17,230 --> 09:07:22,275
这样做是为了让文本与我们预先生成的 48-bit 密钥兼容。
This is done to make the text compatible to a 48-bit keys we have generated beforehand.

5782
09:07:23,502 --> 09:07:27,748
一旦我们将其通过 XOR 函数，我们就得到一个 48-bit 的输出文本。
Once we pass it through the XOR function, we get a 48-bit text as an output.

5783
09:07:28,334 --> 09:07:31,076
现在记住，一半应该是 32-bit。
Now remember, a half should be of 32-bit.

5784
09:07:31,374 --> 09:07:35,652
所以这个 48-bit 的输出随后会被传递到替换盒。
So this 48-bit output is then later passed on to a substitution box.

5785
09:07:36,014 --> 09:07:44,036
这个替换盒将其大小从 48-bit 减少到 32-bit 输出，随后会与明文的第一半部分进行异或运算。
This substitution box reduces its size from 48-bit to 32-bit output, which is then later XORed with the first half of the plaintext.

5786
09:07:48,430 --> 09:07:57,028
如果块大小足够大，分组密码就被认为是更安全的，
但较大的块大小也可能降低加密和解密的速度。
A block cipher is considered the safest if the size of the block is large, but
large block sizes can also slow down encryption speed and the decryption speed.

5787
09:07:57,646 --> 09:07:59,875
通常情况下，块大小是 64-bit。
Generally, the size is 64-bit.

5788
09:08:00,303 --> 09:08:04,612
有时现代分组密码如 AES 也有 128-bit 的块大小。
Sometimes modern block ciphers like AES have a 128-bit block size as well.

5789
09:08:06,478 --> 09:08:14,275
分组密码的安全性随着密钥长度的增加而提高，但更大的密钥长度也可能降低处理速度。
The security of the block cipher increases with increasing key size, but larger key sizes may also reduce the speeds of the process.

5790
09:08:14,701 --> 09:08:17,572
早些时候，64-bit 密钥被认为已经足够。
Earlier, 64-bit keys were considered sufficient.

5791
09:08:18,030 --> 09:08:24,196
由于现代计算标准的复杂性日益增加，现代密码算法需要使用 128-bit 密钥。
Modern ciphers need to use 128-bit keys due to the increasing complexity of today's computational standards.

5792
09:08:25,582 --> 09:08:29,411
轮数的增加也会提高分组密码的安全性。
The increasing number of rounds also increase the security of the block cipher.

5793
09:08:29,966 --> 09:08:33,444
同样，它们与加密速度成反比。
Similarly, they are inversely proportional to the speed of encryption.

5794
09:08:35,822 --> 09:08:39,716
高度复杂的轮函数可以增强分组密码的安全性。
A highly complex round function enhances the security of the block cipher.

5795
09:08:40,046 --> 09:08:43,811
我们必须始终在速度和安全性之间保持平衡。
Always, we must maintain a balance between the speed and security.

5796
09:08:45,966 --> 09:08:51,203
对称分组密码在软件应用中实现，以获得更好的执行速度。
The symmetric block cipher is implemented in a software application to achieve better execution speed.

5797
09:08:51,822 --> 09:09:01,252
如果一个算法无法在现实世界的框架中实现，从而帮助
组织及时加密或解密数据，那么这个算法就毫无用处。
There is no use of an algorithm if it cannot be implemented in a real life framework
that can help organizations to encrypt or decrypt the data in a timely manner.

5798
09:09:02,350 --> 09:09:11,235
既然我们了解了 Feistel cipher 的基础，现在我们可以
看看 DES 是如何运行 16 轮这种结构并最终提供密文的。
Now that we understand the basics of Fistal ciphers, we can take a look at how DES
manages to run through 16 rounds of this structure and provide the ciphertext at the end.

5799
09:09:12,206 --> 09:09:21,188
既然我们了解了 Feistel cipher 的基础，现在我们可
以看看 DES 是如何运行 16 轮这种结构并提供密文的。
Now that we understand the basics of Fistal ciphers, we can take a look at how
DES manages to run through 16 rounds of this structure and provide a ciphertext.

5800
09:09:21,805 --> 09:09:27,908
简单来说，DES 接收一个 64-bit 的明文，并将其转换为一个 64-bit 的密文。
In simple terms, DES takes a 64-bit plaintext and converts it into a 64-bit ciphertext.

5801
09:09:28,302 --> 09:09:34,244
而且既然我们在讨论非对称算法，在解密数据时也会使用相同的密钥。
And since we are talking about asymmetric algorithms, the same key is being used when it is decrypting the data as well.

5802
09:09:36,782 --> 09:09:41,956
我们首先获取一个 64-bit 的明文，并将其通过初始置换函数。
We first take a 64 bit plain text and we pass it through an initial permutation function.

5803
09:09:42,446 --> 09:09:50,052
初始置换函数的作用是将块分成两个不同的部分，以便我们对其执行 Feistel cipher 结构。
The initial permutation function has the job of dividing the block into
two different parts so that we can perform pistol cipher structures on it.

5804
09:09:51,566 --> 09:09:57,316
DES 算法中包含多个轮数，即 16 轮 Feistel cipher 结构。
There are multiple rounds being procured in the DS algorithm, namely 16 rounds of fistal cipher structure.

5805
09:09:57,870 --> 09:09:59,811
这些轮数中的每一轮都需要密钥。
Each of these rounds will need keys.

5806
09:10:00,654 --> 09:10:04,932
最初，我们取一个 56-bit 的加密密钥，但它是一个单一密钥。
Initially, we take a 56-bit cipher key, but it is a single key.

5807
09:10:05,485 --> 09:10:13,059
我们将其传递给轮密钥生成器，它为 Feistel cipher 运行的每一轮生成 16 个不同的密钥。
We pass it on to a round key generators which generate 16 different keys for each single round that the fistal cipher is being run.

5808
09:10:13,517 --> 09:10:17,316
这些密钥以 48-bit 的形式传递到各个轮中。
These keys are passed on to the rounds as 48 bits.

5809
09:10:17,838 --> 09:10:25,636
这些 48-bit 密钥的大小就是我们在 Feistel cipher
的多项式函数中使用置换与置换 boxes 的原因。
The size of these 48 bits keys is the reason we use the substitution
and permutation bonks in the polynomial functions of the fistal ciphers.

5810
09:10:26,638 --> 09:10:33,796
在通过所有这些轮时，我们到达第 16 轮，此时最终
密钥从轮密钥生成器传递过来，我们得到最终置换。
When passing through all these rounds, we reach round 16 where the final key
is passed on from the round key generator and we get a final permutation.

5811
09:10:34,286 --> 09:10:38,660
在最终置换中，各轮进行交换，我们得到最终的密文。
In the final permutation, the rounds are swapped and we get a final ciphertext.

5812
09:10:39,406 --> 09:10:44,324
这就是 DES 的整个过程，其中包含了 16 轮 Feistel cipher。
This is the entire process of DES with 16 rounds of Fistal ciphers encompassed in it.

5813
09:10:44,814 --> 09:10:53,987
为了将密文解密回明文，我们只需要反转 DES 算法中的处理过程，并同时反转密钥顺序和函数。
To decrypt our ciphertext back to the plaintext, we just have to reverse the process
we did in the DES algorithm and reverse the key order along with the functions.

5814
09:10:54,606 --> 09:11:04,580
这种简洁性让 DES 在速度方面获得了优势，但最终在安全性因素方面，它损害了程序的整体效率。
This kind of simplicity is what gave DES the bonus when it comes to speed, but eventually it was detrimental to the overall efficiency
of the program when it comes to security factors.

5815
09:11:05,262 --> 09:11:08,676
DES 有五种不同的工作模式可供选择。
DES have five different modes of operation to choose from.

5816
09:11:09,966 --> 09:11:11,972
其中一种是电子密码本。
one of those is electronic codebook.

5817
09:11:12,462 --> 09:11:17,732
在电子密码本模式下，每个 64-bit 数据块都是独立进行加密和解密的。
Each 64-bit block is encrypted and decrypted independently in the electronic codebook format.

5818
09:11:18,413 --> 09:11:21,252
我们还有密码块链接，也就是 CBC 方法。
We also have cipher block chaining or the CBC method.

5819
09:11:21,742 --> 09:11:27,716
在这里，每个 64-bit 数据块都依赖于前一个块，并且它们都使用初始化向量。
Here, each 64-bit block depends on the previous one and all of them use an initialization vector.

5820
09:11:28,910 --> 09:11:35,235
我们还有密码反馈块机制，其中前一个密文块成为加密算法的输入。
We have a cipher feedback block mechanism where the preceding ciphertext becomes the input for the encryption algorithm.

5821
09:11:35,854 --> 09:11:40,324
它会产生伪随机输出，然后与明文进行异或运算。
It produces a pseudo-random output, which in turn is XORed with the plain text.

5822
09:11:42,030 --> 09:11:51,811
还有一种输出反馈方法，它与密码反馈相同，不同之处在于加密算法的输入是前一个 DES 的输出。
There is an output feedback method as well, which is the same as cipher feedback,
except that the encryption algorithm input is the output from the preceding DES.

5823
09:11:53,614 --> 09:12:00,292
计数器模式采用不同的方法，每个明文块都与加密后的计数器进行异或运算。
A counter method has a different way of approach where each plain text block is XORed with an encrypted counter.

5824
09:12:00,814 --> 09:12:03,811
然后，计数器会为每个后续块递增。
The counter is then incremented for each subsequent block.

5825
09:12:04,589 --> 09:12:13,667
除了这些工作模式，还有一些其他的替代方案，但上述提
到的五种在行业内应用最广，也是全球密码学家推荐的。
There are a few other alternatives to these modes of operation, but the five mentioned
above are the most widely used in the industry and recommended by cryptographers worldwide.

5826
09:12:14,701 --> 09:12:16,580
让我们来看看 DES 的未来。
Let's take a look at the future of DES.

5827
09:12:18,254 --> 09:12:25,956
当高级加密标准取代 DES 加密算法成为公认标准时，DES 的统治地位在 2002 年就结束了。
The dominance of DES ended in 2002 when the advanced encryption
standard replaced the DES encryption algorithm as the accepted standard.

5828
09:12:26,350 --> 09:12:29,540
这是在经过公开竞争寻找替代方案后完成的。
It was done following a public competition to find a replacement.

5829
09:12:30,190 --> 09:12:39,203
NIST 在 2005 年 5 月正式撤销了全球认可标准，尽管三
重DES仍被批准用于某些敏感的政府信息，直到 2030 年。
NIST officially withdrew the global acceptance standard in May 2005, although
Triple DES has approved for some sensitive government information through 2030.

5830
09:12:39,982 --> 09:12:47,140
NIST 还不得不更改 DES 算法，因为考虑到新电脑处理能力的提升，它的密钥长度太短了。
NIST also had to change the DES algorithm because its key length was
too short given the increased processing power of the new computers.

5831
09:12:47,694 --> 09:12:54,595
加密能力与密钥大小有关，而 DES 成了计算技术不断进步的牺牲品。
Encryption power is related to the size of the key, and DES found itself a victim of ongoing technological advances in computing.

5832
09:12:55,150 --> 09:13:00,836
我们已经到了 56-bit 不再是追踪电脑挑战的程度。
We have received a point where 56-bit was no longer a challenge to the computers of tracking.

5833
09:13:01,453 --> 09:13:07,424
请注意，因为 DES 不再是 NIST 联邦标准，并不意味着它不再被使用。
Note that because DES is no longer the NIST federal standard, it does not mean that it is no longer in use.

5834
09:13:07,822 --> 09:13:12,324
三重DES至今仍在使用，并且仍被视为一种遗留加密算法。
Triple DS is still used today and is still considered a legacy encryption algorithm.

5835
09:13:13,453 --> 09:13:19,343
为了更好地了解这些密钥和密文是什么样子的，我们可以利用在线工具。
To get a better understanding of how these keys and ciphertext look like, we can use an online tool for our benefit.

5836
09:13:19,504 --> 09:13:23,843
正如我们已经知道的，要加密任何数据，密钥都是必须的。
As we already know, to encrypt any kind of data, a key is mandatory.

5837
09:13:24,494 --> 09:13:31,203
这个密钥可以使用数学函数或计算机密钥生成程序来生成，就像这个网站提供的这样。
This key can be generated using mathematical functions or computerized key generation program such as this website offers.

5838
09:13:31,917 --> 09:13:35,904
它可以基于任何文本，假设这个词是 Simplilearn。
It can be based on any piece of text, Let's say the word is simply learn.

5839
09:13:40,078 --> 09:13:46,756
一旦确定了密钥，我们就提供需要使用上述密钥加密的明文。
Once the key is settled, we provide the plain text or the clear text that needs to be encrypted using the aforementioned key.

5840
09:13:47,584 --> 09:13:52,224
假设我们这个例子中的句子是：这是我的第一条信息。
Suppose our sentence for this example is this is my first message.

5841
09:13:56,174 --> 09:13:59,716
我们已经满足了两个前提条件：信息和密钥。
We have satisfied two prerequisites, the message and the key.

5842
09:14:00,398 --> 09:14:03,555
另一个起作用的变量是工作模式。
Another variable that goes into play is the mode of operation.

5843
09:14:04,589 --> 09:14:09,667
我们已经学到了五种不同的工作模式，同时我们也能在这里看到一些其他的选项。
We have already learned about five different modes of operation, while we can see some other options here as well.

5844
09:14:10,318 --> 09:14:14,915
让我们选择 CBC 变体，这基本上就是指密码块链接方法。
Let us go with the CBC variant, which basically means the cipher block chaining method.

5845
09:14:15,758 --> 09:14:20,228
CBC 的一个关键特征是它使用了链式处理过程。
One of CBC's key characteristics is that it uses a chaining process.

5846
09:14:20,622 --> 09:14:26,436
它导致一个密文块的解密完全依赖于前面的密文块。
It causes the decryption of a block of ciphertext to depend all on the preceding ciphertext blocks.

5847
09:14:27,021 --> 09:14:33,059
因此，所有块的有效性都包含在之前的相邻块中。
As a result, the entire validity of all the blocks is contained in the previous adjacent blocks as well.

5848
09:14:33,646 --> 09:14:38,500
密文块中的单个比特错误会影响所有后续块的解密。
A single bit error in a ciphertext block affects the decryption of all the subsequent blocks.

5849
09:14:39,150 --> 09:14:44,228
例如，如果改变这些块的顺序，可能会导致解密过程损坏。
Rearrangement of the order of these, for example, can cause the decryption process to get corrupted.

5850
09:14:45,230 --> 09:14:48,996
关于显示二进制信息的方式，我们这里有两个选项。
Regarding the manner of displaying binary information, we have two options here.

5851
09:14:49,582 --> 09:14:52,771
我们可以选择 base64 或者十六进制格式。
We can either go with base64 or the hexadecimal format.

5852
09:14:53,742 --> 09:14:55,492
现在我们先用 base64。
Let's go with the base 64 right now.

5853
09:14:58,606 --> 09:15:01,508
如你所见，密文已经出来了。
As you can see, the ciphertext is readily available.

5854
09:15:01,934 --> 09:15:08,612
Base64 比十六进制稍微高效一点，所以使用 base64 时得到的密文更小。
Base64 is a little more efficient than hex, so we will be getting a smaller ciphertext when it comes to base 64.

5855
09:15:10,638 --> 09:15:13,059
尽管这两种格式的大小是一样的。
Albeit the size of both the formats will be the same.

5856
09:15:13,517 --> 09:15:21,216
十六进制的密文更长，因为 base64 每三个字节占用四个字符，
而十六进制每个字节占用两个字符。
The hex has a longer ciphertext since base64 takes four characters for every three bytes,
while hex will take two characters for each byte.

5857
09:15:21,550 --> 09:15:23,843
因此，base64 显得更高效。
Hence, base64 turns out to be more efficient.

5858
09:15:25,710 --> 09:15:28,996
现在要解密密文，我们也采用相同的格式。
Now to decrypt the ciphertext, we go by the same format.

5859
09:15:29,902 --> 09:15:31,235
我们选择 base64。
We choose base64.

5860
09:15:33,294 --> 09:15:39,940
我们将密文复制到解密工具中，并且必须确保我们使用的密钥完全一致。
We copy the ciphertext onto a decryption tool, and we have to make sure that the key we are using is exactly the same.

5861
09:15:41,165 --> 09:15:49,536
我们选择类似的运行模式，并选择正确的编码格式，在这种情况下是 base64。
We choose similar mode of operation and we choose the correct encoding format as well, which is base64 in this case.

5862
09:15:51,246 --> 09:15:55,652
如你所见，解密完成了，我们得到了明文。
As you can see, the decryption is complete and we get a plain text back.

5863
09:15:56,398 --> 09:16:03,696
即使你保持所有内容不变，但只要更改编码格式，就无法解密任何内容。
Even if you keep everything the same, but we just change the encoding format, it will not be able to decrypt anything.

5864
09:16:04,269 --> 09:16:08,612
不幸的是，即使没有密钥的帮助，DES 也变得相当容易破解。
Unfortunately, DES has become rather easy to crack even without the help of a key.

5865
09:16:09,230 --> 09:16:16,256
在对称加密安全性方面，高级加密标准仍然处于领先地位，并且很可能会保持一段时间。
The advanced encryption standard is still on top when it comes to
symmetric encryption security and will likely stay there for a while.

5866
09:16:17,006 --> 09:16:23,811
最终，随着计算能力的巨大增长，为了保护我们的个人数据，有必要使用更强大的算法。
Eventually, with so much computing power growth, the need for a stronger algorithm was necessary to safeguard our personal data.

5867
09:16:24,622 --> 09:16:32,836
尽管 DES 很可靠，但今天的计算机可以通过反复尝试轻松破解加密，从而使数据安全失效。
As solid as DES was, the computers of today could easily break the encryption with repeated attempts,
thereby rendering the data security helpless.

5868
09:16:33,453 --> 09:16:40,708
为了应对这个难题，引入了一个新的标准，被称为高级加密标准或 AES 算法。
To counter this dilemma, a new standard was introduced which was termed as the advanced encryption standard or the AES algorithm.

5869
09:16:41,934 --> 09:16:44,548
让我们来了解什么是高级加密标准。
Let's learn what is advanced encryption standard.

5870
09:16:47,726 --> 09:16:55,460
AES 算法也称为 Rijndael 算法，是一种块大小为 128 位的对称分组密码。
The AES algorithm, also known as the Rindial algorithm, is a symmetric block cipher with a block size of 128 bits.

5871
09:16:56,046 --> 09:17:01,796
它使用 128、192 或 256 位的密钥转换为密文。
It is converted into ciphertext using keys of 128, 192, or 256 bits.

5872
09:17:02,446 --> 09:17:07,108
它在世界各地的软件和硬件中被用于加密敏感数据。
It is implemented in software and hardware throughout the world to encrypt sensitive data.

5873
09:17:07,854 --> 09:17:19,012
美国国家标准技术研究院（NIST）于 1997 年开始开发 AES，
当时宣布需要一种替代数据加密标准的方法。
The National Institute of Standards and Technology, also known as NIST, started development on AES in 1997 when it was announced the
need for an alternative to the data encryption standard.

5874
09:17:19,917 --> 09:17:24,388
新的互联网需要一个替代 DES 的方案，因为它的密钥长度太小了。
The new internet needed a replacement for DES because of its small key size.

5875
09:17:25,038 --> 09:17:30,116
随着计算能力的提升，它被认为在面对全密钥搜索攻击时是不安全的。
With increasing computing power, it was considered unsafe against entire key search attacks.

5876
09:17:31,053 --> 09:17:34,016
三重DES的设计就是为了克服这个问题。
The Triple DES was designed to overcome this problem.

5877
09:17:34,222 --> 09:17:38,084
然而，它被认为运行太慢，无法在全球范围内的机器上部署。
However, it was deemed to be too slow to be deployed in machines worldwide.

5878
09:17:38,896 --> 09:17:53,156
Mars、RC6、Serpent和Two Fish算法都有很强的表现，但最终被
选为标准对称密钥加密算法的是Rindal加密算法，也就是AES。
Strong cases were present by the Mars, RC6, Serpent, and the Two Fish algorithms, but it was the Rindal encryption algorithm,
also known as AES, which was eventually chosen as the standard symmetric key encryption algorithm to be used.

5879
09:17:53,742 --> 09:18:01,411
它的选择在2001年11月发布联邦信息处理标准出版物197时正式确定。
Its selection was formalized with the release of Federal Information Processing Standards Publication 197 in the November of 2001.

5880
09:18:01,870 --> 09:18:04,388
它获得了美国商务部的批准。
It was approved by the US Secretary of Commerce.

5881
09:18:06,318 --> 09:18:13,411
既然我们了解了AES的起源，现在让我们来看看让AES加密算法独特的特性。
Now that we understand the origin of AES, let us have a look at the features that make AES encryption algorithm unique.

5882
09:18:15,629 --> 09:18:20,163
AES算法使用置换网络，也就是SP网络。
The AES algorithm uses a substitution permutation or SP network.

5883
09:18:20,654 --> 09:18:23,492
它包含多个轮次来生成密文。
It consists of multiple rounds to produce a ciphertext.

5884
09:18:24,014 --> 09:18:33,508
它有一系列连锁操作，包括用特定输出替换输入，即替换，以及涉及位洗牌的操作，也就是排列。
It has a series of linked operations, including replacing inputs with specific outputs, that is substitutions,
and others that involve bit shuffling, which is permutations.

5885
09:18:34,478 --> 09:18:42,436
在加密过程开始时，我们只从一个密钥开始，它可以是128位密钥、192位密钥或256位密钥。
At the beginning of the encryption process, we only start out with a single
key, which can be either a 128-bit key, a 192-bit key, or a 256-bit key.

5886
09:18:42,989 --> 09:18:48,900
最终，这个密钥会被扩展，用于整个加密和解密循环中的多个轮次。
Eventually, this one key is expanded to be used in multiple rounds throughout the encryption and the decryption cycle.

5887
09:18:49,326 --> 09:18:57,156
有趣的是，AES所有的计算都是在字节数据上进行的，而不是像DES算法那样在位数据上进行。
Interestingly, AES performs all its calculations on byte data instead of bit data, as seen in the case of the DES algorithm.

5888
09:18:57,710 --> 09:19:02,980
因此，AES将128位的明文块视为16个字节。
Therefore, AES treats 128 bits of a clear text block as 16 bytes.

5889
09:19:04,014 --> 09:19:08,516
加密过程中的轮数取决于所使用的密钥长度。
The number of rounds during the encryption process depends on the key size that is being used.

5890
09:19:09,197 --> 09:19:18,052
128位密钥长度固定为10轮，192位密钥长度固定为12轮，而256位密钥则包含14轮。
The 128-bit key size fixes 10 rounds, the 192-bit key size fixes 12 rounds, and the 256-bit key holds 14 rounds.

5891
09:19:18,702 --> 09:19:29,156
这些轮次中的每一轮都需要一个轮密钥，但由于算法中只输入一个密钥，
因此需要将单个密钥扩展到获取每一轮的密钥，包括第0轮。
A round key is required for each of these rounds, but since only one key is input into the algorithm,
the single key needs to be expanded to get the key for each round, including the round 0.

5892
09:19:31,374 --> 09:19:37,508
由于后台有这么多数学计算，整个过程中肯定会有很多步骤。
With so many mathematical calculations going on in the background, there are bound to be a lot of steps throughout the procedure.

5893
09:19:38,030 --> 09:19:40,452
让我们来看看AES遵循的步骤。
Let's have a look at the steps followed in AES.

5894
09:19:42,894 --> 09:19:48,740
在我们继续之前，我们需要了解在AES加密过程中数据是如何存储的。
Before we move ahead, we need to understand how data is being stored during the process of AES encryption.

5895
09:19:50,094 --> 09:19:53,956
过程中的所有内容都以4x4矩阵格式存储。
Everything in the process is stored in a 4 into 4 matrix format.

5896
09:19:55,150 --> 09:20:04,324
这个矩阵也被称为状态数组，我们将使用这些状态数
组在不同步骤之间、以及在不同轮次之间传输数据。
This matrix is also known as a state array, and we'll be using these state arrays
to transmit data from one step to another and from one round to the next round.

5897
09:20:05,838 --> 09:20:11,652
每一轮都以状态数组作为输入，并输出一个状态数组，供下一轮传输。
Each round takes state array as an input and gives a state array as output to be transferred into the next round.

5898
09:20:12,942 --> 09:20:20,016
它是一个16字节的矩阵，每个单元格代表一个字节，每四个字节代表一个字。
It is a 16-byte matrix with each cell representing one byte, with each four bytes representing a word.

5899
09:20:20,430 --> 09:20:24,132
所以每个状态数组总共将包含四个字来代表它。
So every state array will have a total of four words representing it.

5900
09:20:28,270 --> 09:20:34,884
正如我们之前讨论的，我们取一个密钥，并将其扩展到我们需要使用的轮数。
As we previously discussed, we take a single key and expand it to the number of rounds that we need the key to be used in.

5901
09:20:35,438 --> 09:20:44,612
假设轮数为n，那么密钥必须扩展到n+1轮，因为第一轮是第0轮密钥。
Let's say the number of rounds are n, then the key has to be expanded to
be used with n plus 1 rounds because the first round is the key 0 round.

5902
09:20:46,798 --> 09:20:51,856
假设n是轮数，密钥被扩展到n+1轮。
Let's say n is the number of rounds, the key is expanded to n plus 1 rounds.

5903
09:20:52,110 --> 09:20:56,016
它也是一个包含4个字的状态数组。
It is also a state array having 4 words in its vicinity.

5904
09:20:56,366 --> 09:21:03,076
每个密钥用于单轮，第一个密钥在任何轮次开始前作为轮密钥使用。
Every key is used for a single round and the first key is used as a round key before any round begins.

5905
09:21:04,878 --> 09:21:11,044
最开始，明文被捕获，并与轮密钥进行 XOR 操作。
In the very beginning, the plaintext is captured and passed through an XOR function with the round key as a supplement.

5906
09:21:12,910 --> 09:21:17,156
这个密钥可以看作是从 n+1 扩展密钥集中提取出的第一个密钥。
This key can be considered the first key from the n plus 1 expanded set.

5907
09:21:18,158 --> 09:21:24,016
接下来，上一步生成的状态数组被传递到字节替换进程中。
Moving on, the state array resulting from the above step is passed on to a byte substitution process.

5908
09:21:25,454 --> 09:21:29,220
在那之后，还有在状态数组中进行行移位的规定。
Beyond that, there is a provision to shift rows in the state arrays.

5909
09:21:30,062 --> 09:21:40,292
随后，状态数组与一个常数矩阵混合，在列混淆环节中打乱其列，
之后我们加上该特定轮次的轮密钥。
Later on, the state array is mixed with a constant matrix to shuffle its column in the mix column segment,
after which we add the round key for that particular round.

5910
09:21:42,190 --> 09:21:47,748
最后提到的四个步骤是加密算法经历的每一个轮次中的组成部分。
The last four steps mentioned are part of every single round that the encryption algorithm goes through.

5911
09:21:48,334 --> 09:21:51,972
状态数组随后作为输入从一轮传递到下一轮。
The state arrays are then passed from one round to the next as an input.

5912
09:21:52,814 --> 09:21:58,884
然而，在最后一轮，我们跳过列混淆部分，其余流程保持不变。
In the last round, however, we skip the mix columns portion with the rest of the process remaining unchanged.

5913
09:21:59,854 --> 09:22:03,044
但是，这些字节替换和行移位进程到底是什么呢？
But what are these byte substitution and row shifting processes?

5914
09:22:03,374 --> 09:22:05,860
让我们详细了解每一个步骤。
Let's find out regarding each step in more detail.

5915
09:22:08,846 --> 09:22:17,252
在第一步中，明文存储在状态数组中，并与 K0 进行 XOR 操作，
K0 是扩展密钥集中的第一个密钥。
In the first step, the plaintext is stored in a state array and it is exorbed with the K0,
which is the first key in the expanded key set.

5916
09:22:17,998 --> 09:22:24,548
这一步仅对一个数据块执行一次，而在每轮结束时，根据迭代需求重复执行。
This step is performed only once on a block while being repeated at the end of each round as per iteration demands.

5917
09:22:25,582 --> 09:22:32,196
状态数组与密钥进行 XOR 操作以获得新的状态数组，然后将其作为输入传递给字节替换进程。
The state array is exorbed with the key to get a new state array, which is then passed off as input to the sub-bytes process.

5918
09:22:34,030 --> 09:22:36,388
在第二阶段，我们进行字节替换。
In the second stage, we have byte substitution.

5919
09:22:36,928 --> 09:22:42,692
我们利用一个被称为 S box 的替换盒，在每个元素之间随机交换数据。
We leverage an X box called as a substitution box to randomly switch data among each element.

5920
09:22:43,470 --> 09:22:47,268
每一个字节都被转换为包含两个部分的十六进制值。
Every single byte is converted into a hexadecimal value having two parts.

5921
09:22:47,758 --> 09:22:51,780
第一部分代表行值，第二部分代表列值。
The first part denotes the row value and the second part denotes the column value.

5922
09:22:52,686 --> 09:23:01,220
整个状态数组通过 S box 创建一个全新的状态数组，然后将其作为输入传递给行移位进程。
The entire state array is passed through the S box to create a brand new state array,
which is then passed off as an input to the row shifting process.

5923
09:23:01,998 --> 09:23:06,788
通过查看设计中给出的固定表，替换 16 个输入字节。
The 16 input bytes are replaced by looking at a fixed table given in the design.

5924
09:23:07,214 --> 09:23:10,848
最后我们得到一个四行四列的矩阵。
We finally get a matrix with four rows and four columns.

5925
09:23:12,526 --> 09:23:17,764
说到行移位，矩阵中的四行中的每个比特都会向左移动。
When it comes to row shifting, each bit in the four rows of the matrix is shifted to the left.

5926
09:23:18,222 --> 09:23:21,828
移出的条目会被重新插入到行的右侧。
An entry that is a falloff is reinserted to the right of the line.

5927
09:23:22,350 --> 09:23:24,068
变化如下所示。
The change is done as follows.

5928
09:23:24,622 --> 09:23:37,092
第一行没有任何移动，第二行向左移动一个位置，第
三行向左移动两个位置，第四行向左移动三个位置。
The first line is not moved in any way, the second line is shifted to a single position to the left,
the third line is shifted two positions to the left, and the fourth line is shifted three positions to the left.

5929
09:23:37,774 --> 09:23:45,636
结果是一个包含相同 16 个字节的新矩阵，但它们
彼此之间的位置发生了变化，以增加程序的复杂度。
The result is a new matrix that contains the same 16 bytes but has been
moved in relation to each other to boost the complexity of the program.

5930
09:23:47,566 --> 09:23:53,188
在列混淆中，每个由四个字节组成的列现在使用特殊的数学函数进行替换。
In mixed columns, each column of four bytes is now replaced using a special mathematical function.

5931
09:23:53,870 --> 09:23:58,916
该函数以一列的四个字节作为输入，并输出四个全新的字节。
The function takes four bytes of a column as input and outputs four completely new bytes.

5932
09:24:00,078 --> 09:24:08,740
我们将得到一个大小同样为 16 字节的新矩阵，需要注意的是，
这一阶段在迭代的最后一轮中不会执行。
We will get a new matrix with the same size of 16 bytes and it should be
noted that this phase has not been done in the last round of the iteration.

5933
09:24:12,974 --> 09:24:20,996
说到加上轮密钥，矩阵的 16 个字节被视为 128 位，并与轮密钥的 128 位进行 XOR 操作。
When it comes to adding a round key, the 16 bytes of the matrix are treated as 128 bits and the 128 bits of the round key are XOR.

5934
09:24:21,646 --> 09:24:24,996
如果是最后一轮，输出就是密文。
If it is the last round, the output is the ciphertext.

5935
09:24:25,422 --> 09:24:32,996
如果还有几轮剩余，生成的 128 位将被解释为 16 字节，然后我们开始下一轮类似的循环。
If we still have a few rounds remaining, the resulting 128 bits are interpreted as 16 bytes and we start another similar round.

5936
09:24:35,822 --> 09:24:39,236
让我们举个例子来了解所有这些过程是如何运作的。
Let's take an example to understand how all these processes work.

5937
09:24:39,694 --> 09:24:47,888
如果我们的明文是字符串 2192，我们首先将其转换为如下的十六进制格式。
If our plain text is the string 2192, we first convert it into a hexadecimal format as follows.

5938
09:24:48,494 --> 09:24:54,768
我们使用加密密钥，也就是我的 Kungfu，它同样被转换成十六进制格式。
We use an encryption key which is that's my Kungfu and it is converted into a hexadecimal format as well.

5939
09:24:55,758 --> 09:25:06,180
按照指南，我们使用单个密钥，稍后将其扩展为 n+1
个密钥，在这种情况下，10 轮需要 11 个密钥。
As per the guidelines, we use a single key which is then later expanded into n plus one number of keys,
in which case it's supposed to be 11 keys for 10 different rounds.

5940
09:25:08,334 --> 09:25:10,468
在第 0 轮，我们加入轮密钥。
In round 0, we add the round key.

5941
09:25:10,894 --> 09:25:18,756
明文与 0 进行 XOR 运算，我们得到一个状态数组，作为字节替换过程的输入。
The plain test is exhausted with the case 0 and we get a state array that is passed off as an input to the substitution bytes process.

5942
09:25:22,734 --> 09:25:31,204
在字节替换过程中，我们利用 S box 将每个字节的元素替换为全新的字节。
When it comes to the substitution bytes process, we leverage an S box
to substitute the elements of each byte with a completely new byte.

5943
09:25:31,630 --> 09:25:37,636
这样，我们收到的状态数组就作为下一步行移位的输入。
This way the state array that we receive is passed off as an input to the row shifting process of the next step.

5944
09:25:39,950 --> 09:25:51,524
在行移位时，每个元素向左移动几个位置，第一行移动 0 位，第二行移动 1 位，
第三行移动 2 位，最后一行移动 3 位。
When it comes to row shifting, each element is shifted a few places to the left, with the first row being shifted by 0 places,
second row by 1 place, third row by 2 places, and the last by 3.

5945
09:25:54,414 --> 09:26:00,068
从行移位中获得的状态数组作为列混淆的输入。
The state array that we received from the row shifting is passed off as an input to mix columns.

5946
09:26:00,526 --> 09:26:08,900
在列混淆中，我们将状态数组与一个常数矩阵相乘，
之后我得到一个新的状态数组，将其传递到下一步。
In mixed columns we multiply the state array with a constant matrix,
after which I receive a new state array to be passed on onto the next step.

5947
09:26:12,942 --> 09:26:18,576
我们将新的状态数组与特定轮次的轮密钥进行 XOR 运算。
We add the new state array as an XOR with the round key of the particular iteration.

5948
09:26:19,022 --> 09:26:24,036
无论我们在这里收到什么状态数组，它都会成为这一轮的输出。
Whatever state array we receive here, it becomes an output for this particular round.

5949
09:26:25,870 --> 09:26:34,372
现在，由于这是整个加密过程的第一轮，我们收到的状态数组将作为新一轮的输入。
Now, since this is the first round of the entire encryption process, the
state array that we receive is passed off as an input to the new round.

5950
09:26:36,654 --> 09:26:41,380
我们重复这个过程 10 轮，最后我们得到密文。
We repeat this process for 10 more rounds and we finally receive a ciphertext.

5951
09:26:42,702 --> 09:26:52,772
一旦最终的状态数组可以表示为十六进制格式，它就变成了我们的最终密文，
可用于发送者和接收者之间的信息传输。
Once the final state array can be denoted in the hexadecimal format, this becomes our final ciphertext that we can use for
transferring information from the sender and receiver.

5952
09:26:55,662 --> 09:26:58,820
让我们来看看 AES 在这个世界中的应用。
Let's take a look at the applications of AES in this world.

5953
09:27:01,742 --> 09:27:10,436
AES 在无线安全领域应用最广，用于在路由器和客户端之间建立安全的身份验证模式。
AES finds most use in the area of wireless security in order to establish a secure mode of authentication between routers and clients.

5954
09:27:11,054 --> 09:27:20,420
像 WPA 和 WPA2PSK 这样高度安全的机制，广泛用于通过 Rijndael's 算法来保护 Wi-Fi 端点。
Highly secure mechanisms like WPA and WPA2PSK are extensively used in securing Wi-Fi endpoints with the help of Rindile's algorithm.

5955
09:27:21,294 --> 09:27:27,812
它还有助于 SSL TLS 加密，这对于加密我们的浏览器会话至关重要。
It also helps in SSL TLS encryption that is instrumental in encrypting our internet browser sessions.

5956
09:27:28,622 --> 09:27:39,044
AES 与其他非对称加密算法协同工作，确保浏览器和
Web 服务器配置正确，并使用加密通道进行通信。
AES works in tandem with other asymmetric encryption algorithms to make sure the web browser and web server are properly configured
and use encrypted channels for communication.

5957
09:27:40,654 --> 09:27:47,300
AES 也广泛应用于各种格式的通用文件加密，从特定文档到媒体文件。
AES is also prevalent in general file encryption of various formats ranging from particular documents to the media files.

5958
09:27:47,886 --> 09:27:54,020
拥有大密钥可以让人们以最高的安全性加密媒体和解密数据。
Having a large key allows people to encrypt media and decrypt data with maximum security possible.

5959
09:27:55,342 --> 09:28:02,724
AES 还用于硬件专用设备的处理器安全，用于防止机器劫持等其他用途。
AES is also used for processor security in hardware appliances to prevent machine hijacking, among other things.

5960
09:28:04,430 --> 09:28:11,524
作为 DES 算法的直接继任者，AES 在某些方面提供了明显的优势。
As a direct successor to the DES algorithm, there are some aspects that AES provides an immediate advantage in.

5961
09:28:12,206 --> 09:28:13,252
让我们来看看。
Let us take a look.

5962
09:28:15,886 --> 09:28:23,364
说到密钥长度，DES 算法最大的缺陷是其长度太短，在今天的标准下很容易受到攻击。
When it comes to key length, the biggest flaw in DES algorithm was its small length was easily vulnerable by today's standards.

5963
09:28:23,696 --> 09:28:30,852
AES 能够支持 128、192 和 256 位密钥长度，以进一步增强安全性。
AES has managed to nab up 128, 192, and 256-bit key lengths to bolster the security further.

5964
09:28:31,630 --> 09:28:36,900
由于算法更复杂，AES 的块大小也更大。
The block size is also larger in AES owing to more complexity of the algorithm.

5965
09:28:37,742 --> 09:28:42,308
DES 的轮数是固定的，无论使用的明文是什么。
The number of rounds in DES is fixed irrespective of the plain text being used.

5966
09:28:42,702 --> 09:28:51,940
在 AES 中，轮数取决于特定迭代所使用的密钥长度，从而为算法提供更高的随机性和复杂性。
In AES, the number of rounds depends on the key length that is being used for the particular iteration,
thereby providing more randomness and complexity in the algorithm.

5967
09:28:53,038 --> 09:29:03,268
DES 算法被认为比 AES 更简单，尽管在加密和解密的相对速度上，AES 优于 DES。
The DES algorithm is considered to be simpler than AES, even though AES
beats DES when it comes to relative speed of encryption and decryption.

5968
09:29:03,790 --> 09:29:12,548
与数据加密标准相比，这使得高级加密标准在部署到全球框架和系统中时更加高效。
This makes advanced encryption standard much more streamlined to be deployed in
frameworks and systems worldwide when it compares to the data encryption standard.

5969
09:29:14,158 --> 09:29:20,388
我们首先学习密码学的总体概念及其各种应用、历史意义和类别。
We start by learning about cryptography in general and its various applications, historical significance and categories.

5970
09:29:20,891 --> 09:29:26,308
我们还会演示密码学在当今行业中加密互联网流量的应用。
We also have a demonstration of how cryptography is used in today's industry when encrypting internet traffic.

5971
09:29:27,694 --> 09:29:30,436
接着，我们将深入探讨哈希。
We follow that up by taking a deep dive onto hashing.

5972
09:29:31,150 --> 09:29:36,868
我们涵盖哈希的基础知识，如哈希函数、指南以及加强哈希的方法等。
We cover the basics of hashing like hash functions, guidelines, ways to strengthen hashes among other things.

5973
09:29:38,286 --> 09:29:46,500
接下来，我们涵盖 MD5 哈希算法，解释数据混淆时的步骤，并查看其应用和优势。
Next, we cover the MD5 hash algorithm, explaining the steps taken when
scrambling the data and checking out its applications and advantages.

5974
09:29:47,790 --> 09:29:55,780
最后，我们还涵盖 SHA 哈希算法、其哈希过程中的阶段，以及它相对于此类其他算法的独特优势。
Finally, we also cover the SHA hash algorithm, its phases during hashing,
and the distinct advantages over other algorithms of this nature.

5975
09:29:58,030 --> 09:30:04,644
随着审查的增加和对隐私泄露的普遍担忧，消费者安全正面临前所未有的风险。
With the rise in censorship and general fear over privacy loss, consumer security is at an all-time high risk.

5976
09:30:04,974 --> 09:30:10,468
技术让我们的生活变得更加便利，但也让我们的个人信息成为了极具吸引力的目标。
Technology has made our life so much easier while putting up a decent target on our personal information.

5977
09:30:10,798 --> 09:30:18,276
有必要了解如何同时保护我们的数据，并紧跟最新的技术发展。
It is necessary to understand how to simultaneously safeguard our data and be up to date with the latest technological developments.

5978
09:30:18,606 --> 09:30:24,324
随着密码学在当今数字世界中的地位，维持这种平衡变得更加容易。
Maintaining this balance has become easier with cryptography taking its place in today's digital world.

5979
09:30:25,006 --> 09:30:27,844
那么，这里有一个故事来帮助你理解密码学。
So here's a story to help you understand cryptography.

5980
09:30:28,558 --> 09:30:29,348
认识一下 Anne。
Meet Anne.

5981
09:30:29,966 --> 09:30:33,540
Anne 想给最新的 iPhone 找点折扣。
Anne wanted to look for a decent discount on the latest iPhone.

5982
09:30:33,934 --> 09:30:40,644
她开始在网上搜索，发现了一个相当可疑的网站，提供首单 50% 的折扣。
She started searching on the internet and found a rather shady website that offered a 50% discount on the first purchase.

5983
09:30:41,198 --> 09:30:47,712
就在 Anne 提交支付详情后，几分钟内，她的银行账户就被扣除了一大笔钱。
Once Anne submitted her payment details, a huge chunk of money was withdrawn from a bank account just moments after.

5984
09:30:48,174 --> 09:30:56,452
Anne 崩溃了，她很快意识到自己没注意到那个网站是 HTTP 网页，而不是 HTTPS 网页。
Devastated, Anne quickly realized she had failed to notice that the website was a HTTP web page instead of an HTTPS one.

5985
09:30:57,070 --> 09:31:05,156
提交的支付信息没有经过加密，任何监视的人都能看到，包括网站所有者和黑客。
The payment information submitted was not encrypted and it was visible
to anyone keeping an eye, including the website owner and hackers.

5986
09:31:05,582 --> 09:31:14,020
如果她使用的是具有加密交易和员工密码学的知名网站，这位 iPhone 爱好者就能避免这次意外。
Had she used a reputed website which has encrypted transactions and employees cryptography,
our iPhone enthusiasts could have avoided this particular incident.

5987
09:31:14,542 --> 09:31:21,124
这就是为什么永远不建议访问未知网站或在上面分享任何个人信息。
This is why it's never recommended to visit unknown websites or share any personal information on them.

5988
09:31:21,678 --> 09:31:28,068
既然我们了解了为什么密码学如此重要，现在让我们来了解什么是密码学。
Now that we understand why cryptography is so important, let's now understand what cryptography is.

5989
09:31:29,870 --> 09:31:35,716
密码学是加密或解密信息以防止未经授权访问的科学。
Cryptography is the science of encrypting or decrypting information to prevent unauthorized access.

5990
09:31:36,032 --> 09:31:41,924
我们转换我们的数据和个人信息，以便只有正确的接收者才能理解信息。
We transform our data and personal information so that only the correct recipient can understand the message.

5991
09:31:42,192 --> 09:31:50,500
作为现代数据安全的重要方面，使用密码学允许在有意愿的各方之间安全地存储和传输数据。
As an essential aspect of modern data security, using cryptography allows
the secure storage and transmission of data between willing parties.

5992
09:31:51,152 --> 09:31:57,552
加密是应用密码学的首要途径，通过添加特定算法来混淆数据。
Encryption is the primary route for employing cryptography by adding certain algorithms to jumble up the data.

5993
09:31:57,870 --> 09:32:04,512
解密是撤销加密信息操作的过程，使数据重新变得可读。
Decryption is the process of reversing the work done by encrypting information so that the data becomes readable again.

5994
09:32:04,846 --> 09:32:08,004
这两种方法构成了密码学的基础。
Both of these methods form the basis of cryptography.

5995
09:32:08,974 --> 09:32:18,180
例如，当 Simplilearn 被打乱或以任何格式更改时，
很少有人能通过查看加密文本来猜出原始单词。
For example, when Simply Learn is jumbled up or changed in any format, not
many people can guess the original word by looking at the encrypted text.

5996
09:32:18,638 --> 09:32:25,540
只有知道如何解密编码单词的人才能做到这一点，从而逆转加密过程。
The only ones who can are the people who know how to decrypt the coded word, thereby reversing the process of encryption.

5997
09:32:27,534 --> 09:32:32,228
任何加密前的数据都被称为明文或 明文。
Any data pre-encryption is called plain text or clear text.

5998
09:32:32,654 --> 09:32:41,348
为了加密消息，我们使用特定的算法，其唯一目的是打乱数据，
使其在没有必要工具的情况下无法阅读。
To encrypt the message, we use certain algorithms that serve a single purpose
of scrambling the data to make them unreadable without the necessary tools.

5999
09:32:41,742 --> 09:32:43,684
这些算法被称为密码算法。
These algorithms are called ciphers.

6000
09:32:44,302 --> 09:32:52,836
它们是一系列按顺序执行的详细步骤，以确保数据在到达接收者之前尽可能无法被读取。
They are a set of detailed steps to be carried out one after the other to make
sure the data becomes as unreadable as possible until it reaches the receiver.

6001
09:32:53,390 --> 09:32:58,244
我们获取明文，将其传递给密码算法，然后得到加密数据。
We take the plaintext, pass it to the cipher algorithm, and get the encrypted data.

6002
09:32:58,670 --> 09:33:04,740
这个加密文本被称为密文，这也是在双方之间传输的消息。
This encrypted text is called the ciphertext, and this is the message that is transferred between the two parties.

6003
09:33:05,326 --> 09:33:09,188
用于打乱数据的密钥被称为加密密钥。
The key that is being used to scramble the data is known as the encryption key.

6004
09:33:09,774 --> 09:33:18,148
这些步骤，也就是密码算法和加密密钥，会告知接收者，接收者随后可以在收到消息时逆转加密。
These steps, that is the cipher and the encryption key are made known to
the receiver who can then reverse the encryption on receiving the message.

6005
09:33:18,670 --> 09:33:30,244
除非第三方设法同时发现算法和正在使用的密钥，否则他们无法解密消息，
因为这两者都是解锁隐藏内容所必需的。
Unless any third party manages to find out both the algorithm and the secret key that is being used,
they cannot decrypt the messages since both of them are necessary to unlock the hidden content.

6006
09:33:31,214 --> 09:33:34,244
想知道如果没有密码学，我们还会失去什么吗？
Wonder what else we would lose if not for cryptography?

6007
09:33:35,854 --> 09:33:39,364
任何拥有账户的网站都可以读取你的密码。
Any website where you have an account can read your passwords.

6008
09:33:39,711 --> 09:33:45,092
重要的电子邮件可能会被拦截，如果在传输过程中没有加密，其内容也可以被读取。
important emails can be intercepted and their contents can be read without encryption during the transit.

6009
09:33:45,614 --> 09:33:52,708
WhatsApp 每天发送超过 650 亿条消息，所有这些消息都由于端到端加密而受到保护。
More than 65 billion messages are sent on WhatsApp every day, all of which are secured thanks to end-to-end encryption.

6010
09:33:53,454 --> 09:34:04,548
加密货币市场正在大幅开放，这是由于区块链技术实现的，
它使用加密算法和哈希函数来确保数据安全。
There is a huge market opening up for cryptocurrency, which is possible due to blockchain technology that uses encryption algorithms
and hashing functions to ensure that the data is secure.

6011
09:34:04,832 --> 09:34:11,044
如果你对这个特别感兴趣，可以观看我们的区块链视频，链接将在描述中提供。
If this is of particular interest to you, you can watch our video on blockchain, the link of which will be in the description.

6012
09:34:11,470 --> 09:34:15,972
当然，对于像加密这样多样化的问题，并没有单一的解决方案。
Of course, there is no single solution to a problem as diverse as Xplain.

6013
09:34:16,398 --> 09:34:19,972
密码学的工作原理和实际应用有三种变体。
There are three variants of how cryptography works and is in practice.

6014
09:34:20,718 --> 09:34:27,140
它们是对称加密、非对称加密和哈希。
They are symmetric encryption, asymmetric encryption, and hashing.

6015
09:34:27,758 --> 09:34:30,308
让我们看看到目前为止我们理解了多少。
Let's find out how much we have understood until now.

6016
09:34:30,894 --> 09:34:34,212
你还记得密码算法和密文之间的区别吗？
Do you remember the difference between a cipher and ciphertext?

6017
09:34:34,606 --> 09:34:41,732
把你的答案留在评论区，在我们继续之前，如果你觉得这个视频有趣，请在继续之前点个赞。
Leave your answers in the comments, and before we proceed, if you find this video interesting,
make sure to give it a thumbs up before moving ahead.

6018
09:34:42,190 --> 09:34:44,672
让我们先来看看对称加密。
Let's look at symmetric encryption first.

6019
09:34:46,382 --> 09:34:51,492
对称加密在数据的加密和解密过程中使用同一个密钥。
Symmetric encryption uses a single key for both the encryption and decryption of data.

6020
09:34:51,950 --> 09:34:56,516
它比非对称加密安全性相对较低，但速度快得多。
It is comparatively less secure than asymmetric encryption but much faster.

6021
09:34:56,974 --> 09:35:04,676
这是一种必须接受的折中方案，目的是在不让信息完全暴露的情况下尽可能快速地传输数据。
It is a compromise that has to be embraced in order to deliver data
as fast as possible without leaving information completely vulnerable.

6022
09:35:05,358 --> 09:35:12,708
这种加密类型用于数据存储在服务器上时，以及用于识别支付应用程序和服务的人员。
This type of encryption is used when data rests on servers and identifies personnel for payment applications and services.

6023
09:35:13,102 --> 09:35:22,052
对称加密的潜在缺点是发送者和接收者都需要拥有相同的密钥，并且该密钥必须始终保密。
The potential drawback with symmetric encryption is that both the sender and
receiver need to have the same secret key and it should be kept hidden at all times.

6024
09:35:22,606 --> 09:35:27,844
凯撒密码和恩尼格玛机都是对称加密的例子，我们将进一步研究它们。
Caesar cipher and IGMA machine are both symmetric encryption examples that we will look into further.

6025
09:35:28,558 --> 09:35:44,580
例如，如果 Alice 想给 Bob 发消息，她可以用替换密码或移位密码来加密消息，
但 Bob 必须知道相同的密钥，这样他才能在需要读取整条消息时对其进行解密。
For example, if Alice wants to send a message to Bob, she can apply a substitution cipher or a shift cipher to encrypt the message,
but Bob must be aware of the same key itself so he can decrypt it when he finds it necessary to read the entire message.

6026
09:35:45,486 --> 09:35:51,140
对称加密使用两种密码算法之一：流加密和分组加密。
Symmetric encryption uses one of the two types of ciphers, stream ciphers and block ciphers.

6027
09:35:51,982 --> 09:35:58,468
分组加密将明文分解成固定大小的块，并使用密钥将其转换为密文。
Block ciphers break the plain text into blocks of fixed size and use the key to convert it into ciphertext.

6028
09:35:58,926 --> 09:36:06,404
流加密不是把明文分成大块，而是逐位将明文转换为密文。
Stream ciphers convert the plain text into ciphertext one bit at a time instead of resorting to breaking them up into bigger chunks.

6029
09:36:07,054 --> 09:36:22,180
在当今世界，最广泛使用的对称加密算法是 AES 256，即高级加密标准，它的密钥长度为 256 位，
同时也提供 128 位和 196 位的密钥长度。
In today's world, the most widely used symmetric encryption algorithm is AES 256 that stands for Advanced Encryption Standard,
which has a key size of 256-bit, with 128-bit and 196-bit key sizes also being available.

6030
09:36:22,606 --> 09:36:34,256
其他基础算法，如数据加密标准 DES、三重数据加密标准 3DES 以及 Blowfish，
由于 AES 的兴起，都已经不再流行了。
Other primitive algorithms like the data encryption standard that is the DES, the triple data encryption standard 3DES,
and Blowfish have all fallen out of favor due to the rise of AES.

6031
09:36:34,606 --> 09:36:43,268
AES 将数据切分成块，并进行 10 轮以上的混淆和替换，使消息变得无法阅读。
AES chops up the data into blocks and performs 10 plus rounds of obscuring and substituting the message to make it unreadable.

6032
09:36:44,654 --> 09:36:48,900
另一方面，非对称加密则拥有双重优势。
Asymmetric encryption on the other hand has a double whammy at its disposal.

6033
09:36:49,422 --> 09:36:53,156
这里涉及两种不同的密钥：公钥和私钥。
There are two different keys at play here: a public key and a private key.

6034
09:36:53,678 --> 09:37:01,536
公钥用于在传输前加密信息，而私钥用于在传输后解密信息。
The public key is used to encrypt information pre-transit, and a private key is used to decrypt the information post-transit.

6035
09:37:01,998 --> 09:37:08,676
如果 Alice 想使用非对称加密与 Bob 通信，她会使用 Bob 的公钥来加密消息。
If Alice wants to communicate with Bob using asymmetric encryption, she encrypts the message using Bob's public key.

6036
09:37:09,294 --> 09:37:14,016
收到消息后，Bob 使用他自己的私钥来解密数据。
After receiving the message, Bob uses his own private key to decrypt the data.

6037
09:37:14,254 --> 09:37:28,736
这样一来，没人能在传输过程中拦截消息。而且，由于加密是使用公钥完成的，
而解密是使用只有 Bob 能访问的私钥完成的，因此不需要任何安全的密钥交换。
This way, nobody can intercept the message in between transmissions, and there is no need for any secure key exchange for this to work
since the encryption is done with the public key and the decryption is done with the private key that no one except Bob has access to.

6038
09:37:29,070 --> 09:37:31,908
读取完整消息需要两种密钥。
Both the keys are necessary to read the full message.

6039
09:37:32,910 --> 09:37:39,140
还有一种相反的情况，我们可以使用私钥进行加密，并使用公钥进行解密。
There is also a reverse scenario where we can use the private key for encryption and the public key for decryption.

6040
09:37:39,630 --> 09:37:47,364
服务器可以使用其私钥对非机密信息进行签名，任何拥有其公钥的人都可以解密该消息。
A server can sign non-confidential information using its private key, and anyone who has its public key can decrypt the message.

6041
09:37:47,886 --> 09:37:54,564
这种机制还能证明发送者的身份已通过验证，且信息的来源没有问题。
This mechanism also proves that the sender is authenticated and there is no problem with the origin of the information.

6042
09:37:56,078 --> 09:38:00,676
RSA 加密是目前最广泛使用的非对称加密标准。
RSA encryption is the most widely used asymmetric encryption standard.

6043
09:38:01,070 --> 09:38:10,404
它是以其创始人 Rivest、Shamir 和 Adleman 的名字命名的，
它使用分组加密将数据分成块并对信息进行混淆。
It is named after its founders Revest, Shamir, and Edelman, and it uses
block ciphers that separate the data into blocks and obscure the information.

6044
09:38:11,054 --> 09:38:22,884
RSA 被广泛认为是安全性最高的加密形式，尽管它比 AES 慢一些，但它广泛应用于网页浏览、
安全身份验证、VPN、电子邮件和聊天应用。
Widely considered the most secure form of encryption, albeit relatively slower than AES, it is widely used in web browsing,
secure identification, VPNs, emails, and chat applications.

6045
09:38:23,758 --> 09:38:30,628
既然密钥的保密性如此重要，就必须有一种方法在
不让其他人读取我们私有数据的情况下传输密钥。
With so much hanging on the key's secrecy, there must be a way to transmit the keys without others reading our private data.

6046
09:38:31,246 --> 09:38:39,696
许多系统结合使用对称加密和非对称加密，以同时增强安全性并匹配处理速度。
Many systems use a combination of symmetric encryption and asymmetric encryption to bolster security and match speed at the same time.

6047
09:38:40,046 --> 09:38:49,188
由于非对称加密解密大量数据需要更长时间，因此完整信息是使用单个密钥加密的，即对称加密。
Since asymmetric encryption takes longer to decrypt large amounts of data, the
full information is encrypted using a single key, that is, symmetric encryption.

6048
09:38:49,614 --> 09:38:56,356
然后，这个单一密钥通过非对称加密传输给接收者，这样你就不用在任何一方面妥协。
That single key is then transmitted to the receiver using asymmetric encryption, so you don't have to compromise either way.

6049
09:38:56,736 --> 09:39:03,332
另一种途径是使用 Diffie-Hellman 密钥交换，它依赖于单向函数，破解难度要高得多。
Another route is using the Diffie Heldman key exchange, which relies on a one way function and is much tougher to break into.

6050
09:39:04,302 --> 09:39:07,300
密码学的第三种变体被称为哈希。
The third variant of cryptography is termed as hashing.

6051
09:39:10,286 --> 09:39:14,084
哈希是将一段数据打乱到无法识别的进程。
Hashing is the process of scrambling a piece of data beyond recognition.

6052
09:39:14,382 --> 09:39:20,420
它输出固定大小的结果，这就是原始数据的哈希值，或者通常简称为哈希。
It gives an output of fixed size, which is known as the hash value of the original data or just hash in general.

6053
09:39:20,974 --> 09:39:26,084
负责打乱数据集合的计算过程构成了哈希函数。
The calculations that do the job of messing up the data collection form the hash function.

6054
09:39:26,542 --> 09:39:36,260
如果没有强大的暴力破解机制，它们通常是不可逆的，而且
在存储不需要以明文形式保存的网站服务器数据时非常有用。
They are generally not reversible without resilient brute force mechanisms and are very
helpful when storing data on website servers that need not be stored in plain text.

6055
09:39:36,654 --> 09:39:44,292
例如，许多网站以哈希格式存储您的账户密码，这样甚至管理员也无法读取您的凭据。
For example, many websites store your account passwords in a hashed
format so that not even the administrator can read your credentials.

6056
09:39:44,782 --> 09:39:57,156
当用户尝试登录时，他们可以将输入的密码哈希值与服务器上已存储的哈希值进行对比，
从而进行身份验证，因为该函数对于相同的输入总是返回相同的值。
When a user tries to log in, they can compare the entered passwords hash value with the hash value that is already stored on the
servers for authentication since the function will always return the same value for the same input.

6057
09:39:58,894 --> 09:40:01,476
密码学已经在实践中应用了几个世纪。
Cryptography has been in practice for centuries.

6058
09:40:02,158 --> 09:40:09,508
Julius Caesar 使用替换移位，将字母移动到字母表中原有位置之后的特定空格。
Julius Caesar used a substitution shift to move alphabets a certain number of spaces beyond their place in the alphabet table.

6059
09:40:09,888 --> 09:40:13,728
间谍乍一看无法破解原始信息。
A spy can't decipher the original message at first glance.

6060
09:40:13,968 --> 09:40:25,220
例如，如果他想向军队传递机密信息，并决定使用加 2
的替换移位，那么 A 变成 C，B 变成 D，以此类推。
For example, if he wanted to pass confidential information to his armies and decides
to use the substitution shift of plus 2, A becomes C, B becomes D, and so on.

6061
09:40:25,678 --> 09:40:32,196
单词 attack 经过加 3 的替换移位后，变成了 DWDFN。
The word attack, when passed through a substitution shift of plus 3, becomes DWDFN.

6062
09:40:32,590 --> 09:40:38,596
这种加密算法被恰当地命名为凯撒密码，它是最广泛使用的算法之一。
This cipher has been appropriately named the Caesar cipher, which is one of the most widely used algorithms.

6063
09:40:40,590 --> 09:40:45,892
Enigma 可能是古代历史上最著名的密码学加密设备。
The Enigma is probably the most famous cryptographic cipher device used in ancient history.

6064
09:40:46,368 --> 09:40:49,636
它在世界大战期间被纳粹德国军队使用。
It was used by the Nazi German armies in the world wars.

6065
09:40:50,094 --> 09:41:02,692
它们被用来保护机密的政治、军事和行政信息，它由三个或更多的转轮组成，
根据机器当时的运行状态来打乱原始信息。
They were used to protect confidential political, military, and administrative information,
and it consisted of three or more rotors that scrambled the original message depending on the machine's state at that time.

6066
09:41:02,928 --> 09:41:12,128
解密过程类似，但它需要两台机器在传递密文前保持在相同状态，
这样我们才能收到相同的明文信息。
The decryption is similar, but it needs both machines to stay in the same state
before passing the ciphertext so that we receive the same plain text message.

6067
09:41:12,654 --> 09:41:17,732
让我们看看由于密码学的作用，我们的数据在浏览互联网时是如何受到保护的。
Let's take a look at how our data is protected while we browse the internet thanks to cryptography.

6068
09:41:18,126 --> 09:41:22,660
这里我们有一个基于 Web 的工具，可以帮助我们理解 RSA 加密的流程。
Here we have a web-based tool that will help us understand the process of RSA encryption.

6069
09:41:22,990 --> 09:41:30,276
我们可以看到整个工作流，从选择要使用的密钥长度，到解密密文以获取明文。
We see the entire workflow from selecting the key size to be used until
the decryption of the ciphertext in order to get the plain text back.

6070
09:41:31,022 --> 09:41:36,484
正如我们已经知道的，RSA 加密算法属于非对称密钥加密的范畴。
As we already know, RSA encryption algorithm falls under the umbrella of asymmetric key cryptography.

6071
09:41:37,262 --> 09:41:42,596
这基本上意味着我们这里有两个密钥：公钥和私钥。
That basically implies that we have two keys at play here: a public key and a private key.

6072
09:41:44,718 --> 09:41:51,716
通常情况下，公钥由发送者用于加密消息，私钥由接收者用于解密消息。
Typically, the public key is used by the sender to encrypt the message
and the private key is used by the receiver to decrypt the message.

6073
09:41:52,302 --> 09:41:56,772
在某些情况下，这种分配是相反的，我们也将一起看看这些情况。
There are some occasions when this allocation is reversed and we will have a look at them as well.

6074
09:41:57,518 --> 09:42:00,196
在 RSA 中，我们可以选择密钥长度。
In RSA we have the choice of key size.

6075
09:42:00,558 --> 09:42:07,332
我们可以选择任何从 512 位到 1024 位，一直到 4096 位的密钥。
We can select any key from a 512-bit to 1024-bit all the way up to a 4096-bit key.

6076
09:42:07,886 --> 09:42:13,700
密钥长度越长，加密过程就越复杂，从而加强了密文的安全性。
The longer the key length, the more complex the encryption process becomes and thereby strengthening the ciphertext.

6077
09:42:14,350 --> 09:42:21,220
虽然安全性增加了，但更复杂的函数在处理相同大小的数据时，执行相同操作所需的时间更长。
Although with added security, more complex functions take longer to perform the same operations on similar size of data.

6078
09:42:21,678 --> 09:42:31,076
我们必须在速度和强度之间保持平衡，因为如果最强的加密
算法无法在世界各地的系统中实际部署，那它们就毫无用处。
We have to keep a balance between both speed and strength because the strongest encryption algorithms are of no use if they cannot be
practically deployed on systems around the world.

6079
09:42:31,854 --> 09:42:34,436
让我们在这里选择一个 1024 位的密钥。
Let's take a 1024-bit key over here.

6080
09:42:35,278 --> 09:42:37,088
现在我们需要生成密钥。
Now we need to generate the keys.

6081
09:42:37,518 --> 09:42:40,951
这种生成是由在 seed phrases 上运行的函数完成的。
This generation is done by functions that operate on pass freezes.

6082
09:42:41,454 --> 09:42:46,340
我们现在使用的工具会生成用于本次演示的伪随机密钥。
The tool we are using right now generates the pseudo-random keys to be used in this explanation.

6083
09:42:46,798 --> 09:42:52,964
一旦我们生成了密钥，你可以看到公钥比私钥要小得多，这几乎总是如此。
Once we generate the keys, you can see the public key is rather smaller than the private key, which is almost always the case.

6084
09:42:53,486 --> 09:42:56,132
这两个密钥在数学上是相互关联的。
These two keys are mathematically linked with each other.

6085
09:42:56,718 --> 09:43:04,708
它们不能被任何其他密钥取代，为了加密原始消息或解密密文，必须将这对密钥保存在一起。
They cannot be substituted with any other key, and in order to encrypt the
original message or decrypt the ciphertext, this pair must be kept together.

6086
09:43:05,038 --> 09:43:09,636
公钥随后发送给发送者，而接收者则保留自己的私钥。
The public key is then sent to the sender and the receiver keeps the private key with himself.

6087
09:43:10,048 --> 09:43:14,340
在这种情况下，让我们试着加密一个词：Simplilearn。
In this scenario, let's try and encrypt a word simply learn.

6088
09:43:16,494 --> 09:43:23,876
我们必须选择用于加密的是私钥还是公钥，因为这会影响信息的混淆过程。
We have to select if the key being used for encryption is either private or public,
since that affects the process of scrambling the information.

6089
09:43:24,128 --> 09:43:29,988
既然我们这里使用的是公钥，那就选择同样的，复制并粘贴到这里。
Since we are using the public key over here, let's select the same and copy it and paste over here.

6090
09:43:33,774 --> 09:43:37,248
我们现在使用的加密算法是标准的 RSA。
The cipher we are using right now is plain RSA.

6091
09:43:37,806 --> 09:43:45,988
还有一些经过修改的密码算法，它们各有优缺点，
也可以根据我们的日常使用习惯和具体用例来选择。
There are some modified ciphers with their own pros and cons that can also be used,
provided we use it on a regular basis and depending on the use case as well.

6092
09:43:46,862 --> 09:43:51,236
一旦我们点击加密，就可以看到这里生成的密文。
Once we click on encrypt, we can see the ciphertext being generated over here.

6093
09:43:53,646 --> 09:44:01,924
伪随机生成函数的设计是，明文中的单个字符变化都会导致完全不同的密文。
The pseudo random generating functions are created in such a way that a single
character change in the plaintext will trigger a completely different ciphertext.

6094
09:44:02,350 --> 09:44:06,148
这是一种安全特性，旨在加强防御暴力破解手段。
This is a security feature to strengthen the process from brute force methods.

6095
09:44:06,766 --> 09:44:10,916
现在加密过程已经完成，让我们来看看解密部分。
Now that we are done with the encryption process, let's take a look at the decryption part.

6096
09:44:15,886 --> 09:44:20,196
接收者从发送者那里获得这个密文，不需要任何其他密钥或补充信息。
The receiver gets this ciphertext from the sender with no other key or supplement.

6097
09:44:20,560 --> 09:44:24,484
他或她必须已经拥有从同一对密钥中生成的私钥。
He or she must already possess the private key generated from the same pair.

6098
09:44:24,880 --> 09:44:29,700
由于它们在数学上是关联的，所以不能使用任何其他私钥来解密消息。
No other private key can be used to decrypt the message since they are mathematically linked.

6099
09:44:30,222 --> 09:44:33,060
我们将私钥粘贴到这里，并选择同样的选项。
We paste the private key here and select the same.

6100
09:44:33,582 --> 09:44:38,020
加密算法必须始终与加密过程中使用的算法一致。
The cipher must always be the same used during the encryption process.

6101
09:44:39,534 --> 09:44:43,716
一旦我们点击解密，你就能看到我们最初决定加密的原始明文。
Once we click decrypt, you can see the original plaintext we had decided to encrypt.

6102
09:44:44,142 --> 09:44:48,004
这就是 RSA 加密和解密的整个过程。
This sums up the entire process of RSA encryption and decryption.

6103
09:44:48,720 --> 09:44:51,108
现在有些人会反过来使用它。
Now some people use it the other way around.

6104
09:44:51,502 --> 09:44:57,124
我们也可以选择使用私钥来加密信息，并使用公钥来解密。
We also have the option of using the private key to encrypt information and the public key to decrypt it.

6105
09:44:57,614 --> 09:45:00,548
这主要是为了验证消息的来源。
This is done mostly to validate the origin of the message.

6106
09:45:00,878 --> 09:45:07,684
由于密钥只能成对工作，如果使用不同的私钥来加密消息，公钥就无法解密它。
Since the keys only work in pairs, if a different private key is used to encrypt the message, the public key cannot decrypt it.

6107
09:45:08,080 --> 09:45:16,260
相反，如果公钥能够解密消息，说明它一定是用正
确的私钥加密的，也就是由合法的所有者加密的。
Conversely, if the public key is able to decrypt the message, it must have
been encrypted with the right private key and hence the rightful owner.

6108
09:45:16,846 --> 09:45:24,720
这里我们只需要获取私钥，用它来加密明文，并在这个复选框中也选择同样的选项。
Here we just have to take the private key and use that to encrypt the plaintext and select the same in this checkbox as well.

6109
09:45:25,166 --> 09:45:28,560
你可以看到我们生成了一个全新的密文。
You can see we have generated a completely new ciphertext.

6110
09:45:29,038 --> 09:45:34,308
这个密文将发送给接收者，这一次我们将使用公钥进行解密。
This ciphertext will be sent to the receiver and this time we will use the public key for decryption.

6111
09:45:35,118 --> 09:45:40,580
让我们勾选正确的复选框并点击解密，我们仍然得到相同的结果。
Let's select the correct checkbox and decrypt, and we still get the same output.

6112
09:45:42,126 --> 09:45:46,756
现在让我们来看看现实世界中加密的实际例子。
Now let's take a look at practical example of encryption in the real world.

6113
09:45:49,678 --> 09:45:55,716
我们每天都在使用互联网，很多人都知道使用不安全网站的后果。
We all use the internet on a daily basis, and many are aware of the implications of using unsafe websites.

6114
09:45:56,206 --> 09:45:57,700
让我们来看看这里的 Wikipedia。
Let's take a look at Wikipedia here.

6115
09:45:58,254 --> 09:46:02,116
这是一个标准的 HTTPS 网站，其中的 H 代表安全。
Pretty standard HTTPS website where the H stands for secured.

6116
09:46:02,734 --> 09:46:05,156
让我们来看看它是如何保护数据的。
Let's take a look at how it secures the data.

6117
09:46:06,414 --> 09:46:11,300
Wireshark 是世界上最领先且应用最广泛的网络协议分析仪。
Wireshark is the world's foremost and most widely used network protocol analyzer.

6118
09:46:11,520 --> 09:46:22,404
它能让你在微观层面看到网络上发生的情况，我们将使用这
个软件来查看从机器发出的流量，并了解它的易受攻击程度。
It lets you see what's happening on your network at a microscopic level, and we are going to use the software to see the traffic that
is leaving a machine and to understand how vulnerable it is.

6119
09:46:24,558 --> 09:46:32,708
由于这台机器上运行着许多应用程序，让我们应用一个过滤器，只显示与 Wikipedia 相关的结果。
Since there are many applications running in this machine, let's apply
a filter that will only show us the results related to Wikipedia.

6120
09:46:41,646 --> 09:46:46,020
让我们搜索一些可以用来浏览网站的内容。
Let's search for something that we can navigate the website with.

6121
09:46:47,406 --> 09:46:52,420
好了，一旦我们进入一点，你就能看到这里显示的一些请求。
Okay, once we get into it a little, you can see some of the requests being populated over here.

6122
09:46:56,718 --> 09:46:58,980
让我们看看具体的请求。
Let's take a look at the specific request.

6123
09:47:00,910 --> 09:47:06,404
这些是基本上负责在我们的机器和互联网之间双向传输数据的数据包。
These are the data packets that basically transport the data from our machine to the internet and vice versa.

6124
09:47:08,046 --> 09:47:13,840
如你所见，这里有一堆乱码数据，并没有透露出我们搜索或观看的任何内容。
As you can see, there's a bunch of gibberish data here that doesn't really reveal anything that we searched or watched.

6125
09:47:14,000 --> 09:47:21,380
同样，其他受保护的网站也以同样的方式运行，通过这
种方式窃听用户数据是非常困难的，甚至根本不可能。
Similarly, other secured websites function the same way, and it is very difficult, if at all possible, to snoop on user data this way.

6126
09:47:22,254 --> 09:47:29,092
为了对比一下，让我们看看另一个网站，这是一个 HTTP 网页。
To put this in perspective, let's take a look at another website which is a HTTP web page.

6127
09:47:35,950 --> 09:47:41,220
它在服务器端没有启用加密，这使得它容易受到攻击。
This has no encryption enabled from the server end, which makes it vulnerable to attacks.

6128
09:47:41,520 --> 09:47:46,596
这里有一个登录表单，需要合法的用户凭据才能获得访问权限。
There is a login form here which needs legitimate user credentials in order to grant access.

6129
09:47:47,150 --> 09:47:49,572
让我们输入一组随机的凭据。
Let's enter a random pair of credentials.

6130
09:47:57,390 --> 09:48:01,444
这些显然行不通，但我们可以看到数据传输的方式。
These obviously won't work, but we can see the manner of data transfer.

6131
09:48:03,278 --> 09:48:05,956
不出所料，我们没能进入平台。
Unsurprisingly, we weren't able to get into the platform.

6132
09:48:06,480 --> 09:48:08,996
相反，我们可以看到数据包。
Instead, we can see the data packets.

6133
09:48:11,150 --> 09:48:17,764
让我们应用类似的过滤器，帮助我们了解这个网站正在发送什么请求。
Let's apply a similar filter that will help us understand what request this website is sending.

6134
09:48:29,088 --> 09:48:33,488
这些是 HTTP 登录表单发送到互联网的请求。
These are the requests being sent by the HTTP login form to the internet.

6135
09:48:33,998 --> 09:48:41,572
如果我们检查这里，看看我们输入的任何用户名和密
码，我们都可以轻松地通过 Wireshark 看到它们。
If we check here, see whatever username and password that we are entering, we can easily see it with the Wireshark.

6136
09:48:42,542 --> 09:48:45,380
现在，我们使用的是一组虚假的凭据。
Now, we used a dummy pair of credentials.

6137
09:48:45,838 --> 09:48:49,252
如果我们选择正确的数据包，我们就能找到正确的凭据。
If we select the right data packet, we can find our correct credentials.

6138
09:48:49,648 --> 09:48:55,876
如果任何网站要求提供支付信息或合法凭据，那么获取这些信息就会变得非常容易。
If any website had asked for a payment information or a legitimate credentials, it would have been really easy to get a hold of these.

6139
09:48:56,368 --> 09:49:04,740
重申一下我们已经学到的内容，我们必须始终避免 HTTP 网站，以及任何未知或不可信的网站。
To reiterate what we have already learned, we must always avoid HTTP websites and just unknown or not trustworthy websites in general.

6140
09:49:04,910 --> 09:49:07,652
因为我们在这里看到的问题只是冰山一角。
Because the problem we saw here is just the tip of the iceberg.

6141
09:49:08,048 --> 09:49:15,620
尽管密码学已经降低了网络攻击的风险，但攻击依然
普遍存在，我们应该始终保持警惕，以确保在线安全。
Even though cryptography has managed to lessen the risk of cyber attacks, it
is still prevalent and we should always be alert to keep ourselves safe online.

6142
09:49:18,126 --> 09:49:20,612
想象一下在新的网站上创建一个账户。
Imagine creating an account on a new website.

6143
09:49:21,326 --> 09:49:26,436
你提供你的电子邮件地址，并设置一个你很有信心且不会忘记的密码。
You provide your email address and set a password that you are confident and you would not forget.

6144
09:49:27,310 --> 09:49:28,772
那网站所有者呢？
What about the website owner?

6145
09:49:29,088 --> 09:49:31,684
他们会如何安全地存储你的密码？
How securely are they going to store your password?

6146
09:49:32,910 --> 09:49:36,004
对于网站管理员来说，他们有三种选择。
For website administrators, they have three alternatives.

6147
09:49:36,526 --> 09:49:46,692
他们既可以以明文格式存储密码，也可以使用加密和解密密钥对密码进行加密，
或者可以将密码以哈希值的形式存储。
They can either store the passwords in a plain text format, they can encrypt the passwords using an encryption and decryption key,
or they can store the passwords in a hash value.

6148
09:49:47,310 --> 09:49:48,708
让我们来看看这其中的每一种。
Let's have a look at each of these.

6149
09:49:49,646 --> 09:49:57,444
当密码以明文格式存储时，这被认为是最不安全的
选项，因为公司里的任何人都可以读取你的密码。
When a password is stored in plain text format, it is considered to be the
most unsafe option since anyone in the company can read your passwords.

6150
09:49:57,838 --> 09:50:03,844
一次黑客攻击或一次数据服务器泄露，就会毫不费力地暴露所有账户的凭据。
A single hack and a data server breach will expose all the account's credentials without needing any extra effort.

6151
09:50:05,294 --> 09:50:10,660
为了应对这种情况，所有者可以选择加密密码并将其保存在服务器中，作为第二种选择。
To counter this, owners can encrypt the passwords and keep them in the servers as a second alternative.

6152
09:50:11,278 --> 09:50:15,140
但这也就意味着他们必须在服务器的某个地方存储解密密钥。
But that would mean they also have to store the decryption key somewhere on their servers.

6153
09:50:15,662 --> 09:50:23,908
一旦发生数据泄露或服务器被黑，解密密钥和加密密码都会被泄露，因此这会变成单点故障。
In the event of a data breach or the server hack, both the decryption key and
encrypted passwords will be leaked, thus making it a single point of failure.

6154
09:50:25,038 --> 09:50:31,168
如果有种选择，能把密码完全打乱，但又没有任何办法可以将其解密呢？
What if there was an option to store the passwords after scrambling them completely but with no way to decrypt them?

6155
09:50:31,534 --> 09:50:33,188
这就是哈希发挥作用的地方。
This is where hashing comes to play.

6156
09:50:33,806 --> 09:50:38,820
由于服务器上只存储哈希值，所以不需要加密。
Since only the hashed values are stored in the server, no encryption is needed.

6157
09:50:39,008 --> 09:50:44,068
既然没有需要保护的明文密码，你的凭据就免受网站管理员的窥探。
With no plain text passwords to protect, your credentials are safe from the website administrators.

6158
09:50:44,654 --> 09:50:50,244
考虑到所有的优点，在当今存储凭据时，哈希密码是行业标准。
Considering all the pros, hashed passwords are the industry standard when it comes to storing credentials nowadays.

6159
09:50:52,142 --> 09:50:57,508
在深入探讨这个话题之前，让我们先简要了解一下哈希的工作原理。
Before getting too deep into the topic, let's get a brief overview of how hashing works.

6160
09:50:59,982 --> 09:51:04,612
哈希是将一段信息或数据打乱到无法识别的进程。
Hashing is the process of scrambling a piece of information or data beyond recognition.

6161
09:51:05,294 --> 09:51:12,804
我们可以通过使用哈希函数来实现这一点，它们本质上是针对主要明文进行数学运算的算法。
We can achieve this by using hash functions, which are essentially
algorithms that perform mathematical operations on the main plain text.

6162
09:51:13,614 --> 09:51:22,884
明文信息通过哈希函数后生成的数值被称为哈希值、摘要，或者通俗地称为原始数据的哈希。
The value generated after passing the plain text information through the hash function is called the hash value,
digest or in general just the hash of the original data.

6163
09:51:23,694 --> 09:51:29,476
虽然这听起来可能和加密相似，但主要的区别是哈希旨在不可逆。
While this may sound similar to encryption, the major difference is hashes are meant to be irreversible.

6164
09:51:29,902 --> 09:51:33,700
没有任何解密密钥能将摘要转换回其原始值。
No decryption key can convert a digest back to its original value.

6165
09:51:34,414 --> 09:51:42,660
然而，由于如今新一代计算机和处理器的计算复杂度增加，一些哈希算法已经被破解。
However, a few hashing algorithms have been broken due to the increase in
computational complexity of today's new generation computers and processors.

6166
09:51:43,088 --> 09:51:51,428
现在有一些能够经受住时间考验的新算法，仍广泛应用于密码存储、身份验证等多个领域。
There are new algorithms that stand the test of time and are still in use
among multiple areas for password storage, identity verification, etc.

6167
09:51:53,134 --> 09:51:57,316
正如我们之前讨论的，网站使用哈希来存储用户的密码。
Like we discussed earlier, websites use hashing to store the user's passwords.

6168
09:51:57,774 --> 09:52:00,228
那么他们是如何利用这些哈希密码的呢？
So how do they make use of these hash passwords?

6169
09:52:01,518 --> 09:52:09,284
当用户注册创建新账户时，密码会通过哈希函数处理，生成的哈希值会被存储在服务器上。
When a user signs up to create a new account, the password is then run through
the hash function and the resulting hash value is stored on the servers.

6170
09:52:09,774 --> 09:52:18,628
所以下次用户登录账户时，他输入的密码会通过相同的哈希函数处理，
并与主服务器上存储的哈希进行对比。
So the next time a user comes to login to the account, the password he enters is passed
through the same hash function and compared to the hash stored on the main server.

6171
09:52:19,502 --> 09:52:28,750
如果新计算出的哈希与网站服务器上存储的哈希相同，那么密码一定是正确的，
因为根据哈希函数的术语，相同的输入总是提供相同的输出。
If the newly calculated hash is the same as the one stored on the website server,
the password must have been correct because according to hash function's terminology,

6172
09:52:28,750 --> 09:52:31,524
如果新计算出的哈希与网站服务器上存储的哈希相同，那么密码一定是正确的，
因为根据哈希函数的术语，相同的输入总是提供相同的输出。
same inputs will always provide the same outputs.

6173
09:52:32,558 --> 09:52:41,252
如果哈希不匹配，那么登录时输入的密码就与注册时输入的密码不一致，因此登录将被拒绝。
If the hashes do not match, then the password entered during login is not the
same as the password entered during the sign out, hence the login will be denied.

6174
09:52:41,568 --> 09:52:52,260
通过这种方式，不会存储任何明文密码，既防止了所有者窥探用户数据，
也保护了用户在不幸发生数据泄露或被黑时的隐私。
This way, no plain text passwords get stored, preventing both the owner from snooping on user data and protecting users' privacy in
the unfortunate event of a data breach or a hack.

6175
09:52:53,454 --> 09:52:57,860
除了密码存储，哈希还可以用于执行完整性检查。
Apart from password storage, hashing can also be used to perform integrity checks.

6176
09:52:58,798 --> 09:53:07,012
当文件上传到互联网时，系统会生成该文件的哈希值，并与原始信息一起上传。
When a file is uploaded on the internet, the file's hash value is generated and it is uploaded along with the original information.

6177
09:53:07,566 --> 09:53:13,604
当新用户下载文件时，他可以使用相同的哈希函数来计算下载文件的摘要。
When a new user downloads the file, he can calculate the digest of the downloaded file using the same hash function.

6178
09:53:14,286 --> 09:53:21,540
当对比哈希值时，如果它们匹配，就说明文件的完整性得到了维护，没有发生数据损坏。
When the hash values are compared, if they match, then file integrity has been maintained and there has been no data corruption.

6179
09:53:23,502 --> 09:53:29,540
由于如此多的重要信息都交给哈希函数处理，我们需要了解它们是如何工作的。
Since so much important information is being passed onto the hash function, we need to understand how they work.

6180
09:53:31,278 --> 09:53:36,068
哈希函数是一套对两块数据进行操作的数学计算。
A hash function is a set of mathematical calculations operated on two blocks of data.

6181
09:53:36,686 --> 09:53:40,036
主要的输入会被分解成两个大小相似的块。
The main input is broken down into two blocks of similar size.

6182
09:53:40,654 --> 09:53:44,036
块大小取决于所使用的算法。
The block size is dependent on the algorithm that is being used.

6183
09:53:45,454 --> 09:53:47,492
哈希函数的设计目标是单向的。
Hash functions are designed to be one way.

6184
09:53:47,758 --> 09:53:50,244
至少从设计上讲，它们不应该是可逆的。
They shouldn't be reversible, at least by design.

6185
09:53:50,862 --> 09:53:59,332
像之前提到的 MD5 这样的某些算法已经被入侵，但现
在人们正在使用更安全的算法，比如 SHA-256 算法。
Some algorithms like the previously mentioned MD5 have been compromised,
but more secure algorithms are being used today, like the SHF MLF algorithms.

6186
09:53:59,982 --> 09:54:03,844
摘要的大小也取决于所使用的相应算法。
The digest size is also dependent on the respective algorithm being used.

6187
09:54:04,398 --> 09:54:10,532
MD5 的摘要是 128 位，而 SHA-256 的摘要是 256 位。
MD5 has a digest of 128 bits while SHE256 has a digest of 256 bits.

6188
09:54:11,310 --> 09:54:18,400
无论进行多少次计算，相同的输入产生的摘要必须始终相同。
This digest must always be the same for the same input, irrespective of how many times the calculations are carried out.

6189
09:54:18,670 --> 09:54:26,884
这是一个非常关键的特性，因为由于函数不可逆，
对比哈希值是检查数据是否未被篡改的唯一方法。
This is a very crucial feature since comparing the hash value is the only
way to check if the data is untouched as the functions are not reversible.

6190
09:54:28,782 --> 09:54:33,380
哈希函数在被接受之前必须满足某些特定要求。
There are certain requirements of a hash function that need to be met before they are accepted.

6191
09:54:34,030 --> 09:54:39,140
虽然其中一些很容易猜到，但其他的是为了长期保持安全性而设置的。
While some of them are easy to guess, others are placed in order to preserve security in the long run.

6192
09:54:41,006 --> 09:54:48,516
哈希函数必须足够快，能够以相对较快的速度加密大量数据，但它也不应该太快。
The hash function must be quick enough to encrypt large amounts of data at a relatively fast pace, but it also shouldn't be very fast.

6193
09:54:49,038 --> 09:54:54,628
如果在所有核心上运行该算法，会使函数容易受到暴力破解，从而成为安全隐患。
Running the algorithm on all cylinders makes the functions easy to brute force and a security liability.

6194
09:54:55,150 --> 09:55:04,740
必须达到一种平衡，既能让哈希函数处理大量数据，又不
会因为遍历所有可能的组合而让暴力破解变得极其简单。
There must be a balance to allow the hash function to handle large amounts of data and not make it ridiculously easy to brute force by
running through all the possible combinations.

6195
09:55:07,310 --> 09:55:10,692
哈希函数必须依赖于输入的每一个比特。
The hash function must be dependent on each bit of the input.

6196
09:55:11,694 --> 09:55:15,780
输入可以是文本、音频、视频或任何其他文件扩展名。
The input can be text, audio, video, or any other file extension.

6197
09:55:16,270 --> 09:55:24,228
如果更改了一个字符，无论这个字符多么微小，整个摘要都必须具有截然不同的哈希值。
If a single character is being changed, it doesn't matter how small that character may be,
the entire digest must have a distinctly different hash value.

6198
09:55:24,750 --> 09:55:29,156
这对于为每个存储的密码创建唯一的摘要至关重要。
This is essential to create unique digests for every password that is being stored.

6199
09:55:29,966 --> 09:55:33,060
但如果两个不同的用户使用相同的密码怎么办？
But what if two different users are using the same password?

6200
09:55:33,646 --> 09:55:37,956
由于所有用户的哈希函数相同，两个摘要也将相同。
Since the hash function is the same for all users, both the digests will be the same.

6201
09:55:38,478 --> 09:55:40,196
这被称为哈希碰撞。
This is called a hash collision.

6202
09:55:40,718 --> 09:55:46,916
你可能认为两个用户拥有完全相同密码的情况非常罕见，但事实并非如此。
You may think this must be a rare occasion where two users have exactly the same password, but that is not the case.

6203
09:55:47,470 --> 09:55:53,572
我们有像加盐这样的技术来减少这些哈希碰撞，我们将在视频稍后讨论这些内容。
We have techniques like salting that can be used to reduce these hash collisions, as we will discuss later in this video.

6204
09:55:56,142 --> 09:55:59,524
看到 2020 年最常用的密码，你会感到震惊。
You would be shocked to see the most used passwords of 2020.

6205
09:56:00,238 --> 09:56:10,276
所有这些密码的安全级别低得离谱，而且由于许多人反复在不同网站上使用相同的密码，
哈希碰撞的风险比预想的要普遍得多。
All of these passwords are laughably insecure, and since many people use the same passwords repeatedly on different websites,
hash collisions risks are more common than one would expect.

6206
09:56:11,406 --> 09:56:14,852
假设哈希函数发现了两个用户拥有相同的密码。
Let's say the hash functions find two users having the same password.

6207
09:56:15,534 --> 09:56:18,884
他们如何在不破坏原始数据的情况下存储这两个哈希值呢？
How can they store both the hashes without messing up the original data?

6208
09:56:19,374 --> 09:56:21,572
这就是加盐和加胡椒派上用场的地方。
This is where salting and peppering come to play.

6209
09:56:23,150 --> 09:56:29,444
加盐是在输入传递给哈希函数之前，在末尾添加一个随机关键词的过程。
Salting is the process of adding a random keyword to the end of the input before it is passed on to the hash function.

6210
09:56:30,126 --> 09:56:36,320
这个随机关键词对系统上的每个用户都是唯一的，它被称为盐值，或者简称为 salt。
This random keyword is unique for each user on the system and it is called the salt value or just the sort.

6211
09:56:36,686 --> 09:56:42,404
所以即使两个密码完全相同，盐值也会不同，因此摘要也会不同。
So even if two passwords are exactly the same, the salt value will differ and so will the digest.

6212
09:56:43,182 --> 09:56:45,540
不过这个过程有一个小问题。
There is a small problem with this process though.

6213
09:56:46,126 --> 09:56:55,780
由于盐是每个用户唯一的，它们需要与密码一起存储在数据
库中，有时甚至以明文形式存储，以加快连续验证的进程。
Since the salt is unique for each user, they need to be stored in the database along with the passwords and sometimes even in plain
text to speed up the process of continuous verification.

6214
09:56:56,302 --> 09:57:01,060
如果服务器被黑，那么就需要对哈希值进行暴力破解，这非常耗时。
If the server is hacked, then the hashes will need to be brute forced, which takes a lot of time.

6215
09:57:01,486 --> 09:57:05,892
但如果他们同时也拿到了盐值，整个过程就会变得非常快。
But if they receive the salts as well, the entire process becomes very fast.

6216
09:57:06,606 --> 09:57:08,804
这就是加胡椒旨在解决的问题。
This is something that peppering aims to solve.

6217
09:57:10,606 --> 09:57:16,420
加胡椒是在输入传递给哈希函数之前，添加一段随机字符串数据的过程。
Peppering is the process of adding a random string of data to the input before passing them to the hash function.

6218
09:57:16,878 --> 09:57:20,068
但这一次，随机字符串对于每个用户来说并不是唯一的。
But this time the random string is not unique for each user.

6219
09:57:20,494 --> 09:57:26,720
它应该是数据库中所有用户共用的，在这种情况下，添加的额外部分被称为胡椒。
It is supposed to be common for all users in the database, and the extra bit added is called the pepper in this case.

6220
09:57:27,246 --> 09:57:29,156
胡椒不会存储在服务器上。
The pepper isn't stored on the servers.

6221
09:57:29,518 --> 09:57:35,108
它主要硬编码在网站源代码中，因为它对所有凭据都是相同的。
It is mostly hard-coded onto the website source code since it's going to be the same for all credentials.

6222
09:57:35,758 --> 09:57:42,052
这样一来，即使服务器被黑，他们也不会拥有破解所有密码所需的正确胡椒。
This way, even if the servers get hacked, they will not have the right pepper needed to crack into all the passwords.

6223
09:57:42,798 --> 09:57:49,220
许多网站结合使用加盐和加胡椒来解决哈希碰撞问题并增强安全性。
Many websites use a combination of salting and peppering to solve the problem of hash collision and bolster security.

6224
09:57:50,094 --> 09:57:54,084
由于暴力破解非常耗时，许多黑客会避免费这个劲。
Since brute force takes such a long time, many hackers avoid taking the effort.

6225
09:57:54,320 --> 09:58:01,444
回报通常不值得，而且同时使用加盐和加胡椒的可能组合是巨大的。
The returns are mostly not worth it, and the possible combinations of using both salting and peppering is humongous.

6226
09:58:04,814 --> 09:58:12,996
随着公众对数字隐私教育的共识，看到人们对加密算法的兴趣日益增加并不奇怪。
With the consensus aiming towards an educated public on digital privacy,
it's no surprise to see an increasing interest in encryption algorithms.

6227
09:58:13,582 --> 09:58:17,888
我们已经涵盖了像 DES 和 AES 算法等主要名称。
We have already covered the major names like the DES and the AES algorithm.

6228
09:58:18,414 --> 09:58:24,928
MD5 算法是作为 MD4 的继任者，最早走向全球舞台的哈希算法之一。
MD5 algorithm was one of the first hashing algorithms to take the global stage as a successor to the MD4.

6229
09:58:25,582 --> 09:58:34,180
尽管在未来遇到了安全漏洞，MD5 仍然是许多环境中数据基础设施的重要组成部分。
Despite the security vulnerabilities encountered in the future, MD5 still
remains a crucial part of data infrastructure in a multitude of environments.

6230
09:58:37,678 --> 09:58:50,436
MD5 哈希算法是一种单向加密函数，它接受任意长度的消息
作为输入，并返回固定长度的摘要值，用于验证原始消息。
The MD5 hashing algorithm is a one-way cryptographic function that accepts a message of any length as input and it returns as output a
fixed-length digest value to be used for authenticating the original messages.

6231
09:58:50,958 --> 09:58:54,980
无论输入是什么，摘要的大小始终是 128 位。
The digest size is always 128 bits, irrespective of the input.

6232
09:58:55,726 --> 09:59:03,396
MD5 哈希函数最初被设计为一种安全的密码学哈希算法，用于验证数字签名。
The MD5 hash function was originally designed for use as a secure cryptographic hash algorithm to authenticate digital signatures.

6233
09:59:04,046 --> 09:59:13,156
MD5 也已被弃用，除了作为非密码学校验和来验证数据完整性和检测无意的数据损坏之外。
MD5 has also been depreciated for uses other than as a non-cryptographic
checksum to verify data integrity and detect unintentional data corruption.

6234
09:59:14,382 --> 09:59:24,804
RSA 数据安全公司的创始人、MIT 教授 Ronald Rivest 设计了 MD5，
作为先前消息摘要算法 MD4 的改进版本。
Ronald Revest, founder of RSA Data Security and Institute professor at MIT, designed
MD5 as an improvement to a prior message digest algorithm, which was the MD4.

6235
09:59:25,648 --> 09:59:29,088
正如之前提到的，这个过程非常简单。
As already iterated before, the process is straightforward.

6236
09:59:29,248 --> 09:59:37,508
我们将明文消息传递给 MD5 哈希函数，它会对明文进行特定的数学运算来打乱数据。
We pass a plain text message to the MD5 hash functions, which in turn perform
certain mathematical operations on the clear text to scramble the data.

6237
09:59:38,222 --> 09:59:43,300
从中获得的 128 位摘要将与原始明文截然不同。
The 128-bit digest received from this is going to be radically different from the plaintext.

6238
09:59:44,270 --> 09:59:49,540
任何消息摘要函数的目标都是生成看起来是随机的摘要。
The goal of any message digest function is to produce digests that appear to be random.

6239
09:59:49,968 --> 09:59:55,364
要被认为是加密安全的，哈希函数应满足两个要求。
To be considered cryptographically secure, the hash function should meet two requirements.

6240
09:59:55,950 --> 10:00:08,068
第一，攻击者不可能生成与特定哈希值匹配的消息；第二，
攻击者不可能创建两个产生相同哈希值的消息。
First, that it is impossible for an attacker to generate a message that matches a specific hash value, and second,
that it is impossible for an attacker to create two messages that produce the same hash value.

6241
10:00:08,654 --> 10:00:13,796
即使明文发生微小的变化，也应引起两个摘要的巨大差异。
Even a slight change in the plain text should trigger a drastic difference in the two digests.

6242
10:00:14,286 --> 10:00:20,740
这在很大程度上防止了哈希碰撞，即两个不同的明文具有相同的摘要。
This goes a long way in preventing hash collisions which take place when two different plain texts have the same digest.

6243
10:00:21,728 --> 10:00:27,140
为了达到这种复杂程度，在获取摘要之前需要遵循一系列步骤。
To achieve this level of intricacy, there are a number of steps to be followed before we receive the digest.

6244
10:00:28,014 --> 10:00:33,284
让我们来看看 MD5 哈希算法工作的详细过程。
Let us take a look at the detailed procedure as to how the MD5 hash algorithm works.

6245
10:00:36,494 --> 10:00:40,288
第一步是使明文与哈希函数兼容。
The first step is to make the plain text compatible with the hash function.

6246
10:00:40,622 --> 10:00:43,268
为此，我们需要对消息中的比特进行填充。
To do this, we need to pad the bits in the message.

6247
10:00:44,014 --> 10:00:50,468
当我们收到输入字符串时，必须确保其大小比 512 的倍数短 64 位。
When we receive the input string, we have to make sure the size is 64 bits short of a multiple of 512.

6248
10:00:51,118 --> 10:00:57,316
在填充比特时，我们必须先添加 1，然后跟上零，以补齐额外的字符。
When it comes to padding the bits, we must add 1 first followed by zeros to round out the extra characters.

6249
10:00:57,838 --> 10:01:03,812
这使得字符串的长度正好比 512 的任何倍数短 64 位。
This prepares the string to have a length of just 64 bits less than any multiple of 512.

6250
10:01:06,766 --> 10:01:11,076
从这里开始，我们可以进行下一步，即填充长度比特。
Here on out, we can proceed on to the next step where we have to pad the length bits.

6251
10:01:11,488 --> 10:01:21,168
最初，在第一步中，我们以这样一种方式附加消息，
使得消息中比特的总长度比 512 的任何倍数短 64 位。
Initially, in the first step, we appended the message in such a way that the
total length of the bits in the message was 64 bits short of any multiple of 512.

6252
10:01:21,518 --> 10:01:28,740
现在我们添加长度比特，使得消息中的比特总数正好是 512 的倍数。
Now we add the length bits in such a way that the total number of bits in the message is perfectly a multiple of 512.

6253
10:01:29,870 --> 10:01:33,572
准确地说，这意味着向消息中添加了 64 位的长度。
That means 64 bit lengths to be precise are added to the message.

6254
10:01:33,998 --> 10:01:38,148
现在我们要哈希的最终字符串是 512 的确切倍数。
Our final string to be hashed is now a definite multiple of 512.

6255
10:01:41,838 --> 10:01:45,488
下一步是初始化消息摘要缓冲区。
The next step would be to initialize the message digest buffer.

6256
10:01:46,030 --> 10:01:51,044
整个哈希明文现在被分解成 512 位的块。
The entire hashing plaintext is now broken down into 512-bit blocks.

6257
10:01:51,598 --> 10:01:57,828
有四个缓冲区或寄存器，每个都是 32 位，分别命名为 A、B、C 和 D。
There are four buffers or registers that are of 32 bits each, named A, B, C and D.

6258
10:01:59,118 --> 10:02:03,716
这些是四个字，它们将存储每个子块的值。
These are the four words that are going to store the values of each of these subblocks.

6259
10:02:04,526 --> 10:02:10,692
遵循这些寄存器的第一次迭代将具有屏幕下方所示的固定十六进制值。
The first iteration to follow these registers will have fixed hexadecimal values as shown on the screen below.

6260
10:02:13,102 --> 10:02:22,692
一旦这些 512 块的值初始化完成，我们可以将每一个划分为 16 个更小的 32 位子块。
Once these values are initialized of these 512 blocks, we can divide each of them into 16 further subblocks of 32 bits each.

6261
10:02:23,342 --> 10:02:30,308
对于每个子块，我们运行 4 轮运算，涉及四个缓冲区变量 A、B、C 和 D。
For each of these subblocks, we run 4 rounds of operations having the four buffer variables A, B, C and D.

6262
10:02:30,768 --> 10:02:36,004
这些轮次还需要其他的常量变量，这些变量在每一轮运算中都会变化。
These rounds require the other constant variables as well, which differ with each round of operation.

6263
10:02:36,718 --> 10:02:40,452
常量值存储在一个包含 64 个元素的随机数组中。
The constant values are stored in a random array of 64 elements.

6264
10:02:41,102 --> 10:02:49,888
由于每个 32 位子块运行四次，16 个这样的子块等于单块迭代所需的 64 个常量值。
Since each 32 bit subblock is run four times, 16 such subblocks equal 64 constant values needed for a single block iteration.

6265
10:02:50,382 --> 10:02:55,876
子块可以用字母 M 表示，常量值可以用字母 T 表示。
The sub blocks can be denoted by the alphabet M and the constant values are denoted by the alphabet T.

6266
10:02:58,286 --> 10:03:04,932
进入实际的操作轮次，我们看到四个缓冲区，它们已经有了第一轮的预初始化值。
Coming to the actual round of operation, we see our four buffers which already have pre-initialized values for the first iteration.

6267
10:03:05,454 --> 10:03:11,876
在最开始，缓冲区 B、C 和 D 的值被传递到一个非线性对数函数中。
At the very beginning, the values of buffers B, C and D are passed on to a nonlinear logarithmic function.

6268
10:03:12,590 --> 10:03:18,624
正如我们稍后在视频中看到的，这个函数的公式会根据当前处理的轮次而变化。
The formula behind this function changes by the particular round being worked on, as we shall see later in this video.

6269
10:03:19,150 --> 10:03:23,460
一旦计算出输出，它就会被添加到存储在缓冲区 A 中的原始值中。
Once the output is calculated, it is added to the raw value stored in buffer A.

6270
10:03:24,174 --> 10:03:30,596
这个加法的结果会被添加到我们运行这四个操作时所使用的特定 32-bit 子块中。
The output of this addition is added to the particular 32-bit subblock using which we are running the four operations.

6271
10:03:32,064 --> 10:03:38,116
然后，这个必要函数的输出需要加上从常量数组 k 中得出的一个常量值。
The output of this requisite function then needs to be added to a constant value derived from the constant array k.

6272
10:03:38,830 --> 10:03:50,704
因为数组中有 64 个不同的元素，所以我们可以为特定块的每一次迭代使用一个不同的元素。
Since we have 64 different elements in the array, repeat Since we have 64 different elements in the array,
we can use a distinct element for each iteration of a particular block.

6273
10:03:51,214 --> 10:04:00,100
下一步涉及循环移位，这增加了哈希算法的复杂度，
并且是为每个独立的输入创建唯一摘要所必需的。
The next step involves a circular shift that increases the complexity of the hash
algorithm and is necessary to create a unique digest for each individual input.

6274
10:04:01,006 --> 10:04:05,028
生成的输出随后会被添加到存储在缓冲区 B 中的值中。
The output generated is later added to the value stored in the buffer B.

6275
10:04:06,158 --> 10:04:11,556
最终的输出现在被存储在输出寄存器的第二个 B 缓冲区中。
The final output is now stored in the second buffer of B of the output register.

6276
10:04:12,398 --> 10:04:26,212
C、D 和 A 的各个值是从迭代开始前的上一个元素中得出的，这意味着 B 的值被存入 C，
C 的值被存入 D，D 的值被存入 A。
Individual values of C, D and A are derived from the preceding element before the iteration started,
meaning the value of B gets stored in C, value of C gets stored in D, and the value of D in A.

6277
10:04:27,278 --> 10:04:34,372
现在我们已经为这个子块准备好了完整的寄存器，A、B、C、D 的值作为输入传递到下一个子块。
Now that we have a full register ready for this sub block, the values of A, B, C, D are moved on as input to the next subblock.

6278
10:04:34,830 --> 10:04:41,892
一旦所有 16 个子块完成，最终的寄存器值就会被保存，接着开始下一个 512-bit 块。
Once all 16 subblocks are completed, the final register value is saved and the next 512-bit block begins.

6279
10:04:42,510 --> 10:04:46,660
在所有这些块结束时，我们得到了 MD5 算法的最终摘要。
At the end of all these blocks, we get a final digest of the MD5 algorithm.

6280
10:04:48,878 --> 10:04:54,784
关于第一步提到的非线性过程，公式在每一轮运行时都会发生变化。
Regarding the nonlinear process mentioned in the first step, the formula changes for each round it's being run on.

6281
10:04:55,086 --> 10:05:01,184
这样做是为了保持算法的计算复杂度，并增加程序的随机性。
This is done to maintain the computational complexity of the algorithm and to increase randomness of the procedure.

6282
10:05:01,614 --> 10:05:08,772
四个轮次中的每一个公式都使用相同的参数，即 B、C 和 D，来生成单个输出。
The formula for each of the four rounds uses the same parameters, that is B, C and D, to generate a single output.

6283
10:05:09,166 --> 10:05:11,556
目前屏幕上显示的正是所使用的公式。
The formulas being used are shown on the screen right now.

6284
10:05:14,222 --> 10:05:21,444
与最新的哈希算法家族不同，32-bit 摘要在验证摘要时相对更容易比较。
Unlike the latest hash algorithm families, a 32-bit digest is relatively easier to compare when verifying the digests.

6285
10:05:22,286 --> 10:05:28,484
它们不会占用明显的磁盘存储空间，而且相对更容易记忆和重复。
They don't consume a noticeable amount of disk storage and are comparatively easier to remember and reiterate.

6286
10:05:30,798 --> 10:05:36,784
密码不需要以明文格式存储，否则黑客和恶意行为者就可以获取它们。
Passwords need not be stored in plain text format, making them accessible for hackers and malicious actors.

6287
10:05:37,198 --> 10:05:44,004
使用摘要时，数据库安全性也会得到提升，因为所有哈希值的大小都是相同的。
When using digest, the database security also gets a boost since the sizes of all the hash values will be the same.

6288
10:05:45,038 --> 10:05:50,224
一旦发生黑客攻击或数据泄露，恶意行为者只能获取到哈希值。
In the event of a hack or a breach, the malicious actor will only receive the hashed values.

6289
10:05:50,414 --> 10:05:55,236
因此，没有任何办法可以还原出明文，在这种情况下就是用户的密码。
So there is no way to regenerate the plain text, which would be the user passwords in this case.

6290
10:05:55,598 --> 10:06:02,820
由于这些函数在设计上是不可逆的，因此如今在服务
器上存储用户凭据时，哈希处理已成为一种强制要求。
Since the functions are irreversible by design, hashing has become a compulsion when storing user credentials on the server nowadays.

6291
10:06:05,486 --> 10:06:14,064
当要把多个服务集成到同一个框架中且不产生 CPU 开销时，需要相对较低的内存占用。
A relatively low memory footprint is necessary when it comes to integrating
multiple services into the same framework without a CPU overhead.

6292
10:06:14,542 --> 10:06:21,504
无论输入字符串的大小如何，摘要大小都是相同的，且获取哈希值所运行的步骤也是相同的。
The digest size is the same and the same steps are run to get the hash value, irrespective of the size of the input string.

6293
10:06:21,838 --> 10:06:31,184
这有助于降低对计算能力的要求，并且更容易在旧硬件上运行，
而这些硬件在全球范围内的服务器集群中非常常见。
This helps in creating a low requirement for computational power and is much easier to run on older hardware,
which is pretty common in server farms around the world.

6294
10:06:33,934 --> 10:06:38,788
我们可以通过比较传输前后的哈希值来监控文件损坏情况。
We can monitor file corruption by comparing hash values before and after transit.

6295
10:06:39,566 --> 10:06:45,508
一旦哈希值匹配，文件完整性检查就有效，我们可以避免数据损坏。
Once the hashes match, file integrity checks are valid and we can avoid data corruption.

6296
10:06:46,158 --> 10:06:52,228
无论迭代参数如何，哈希函数对于相同的输入始终会给出相同的输出。
Hash functions will always give the same output for the similar input, irrespective of the iteration parameters.

6297
10:06:52,686 --> 10:06:58,628
它还有助于确保数据在传输到消息接收人的途中没有被篡改。
It also helps in ensuring that the data hasn't been tampered with on route to the receiver of the message.

6298
10:07:01,774 --> 10:07:07,204
我们每天都用 Wi-Fi 工作，用互联网进行娱乐和交流。
We use our Wi-Fi every day for work and we use the internet for entertainment and communication.

6299
10:07:07,600 --> 10:07:15,044
由于过去二十年来的巨大发展和创新，人类对技术的依赖达到了历史新高。
The dependency on technology is at an all-time high thanks to the radical developments and innovation in these last two decades.

6300
10:07:15,758 --> 10:07:21,092
其中很大一部分是确保通信和数据传输渠道的安全。
A big portion of this belongs to ensuring secure channels of communication and data transmission.

6301
10:07:23,760 --> 10:07:34,080
安全哈希算法是一系列加密哈希函数，由美国国家标准技术研究院与 NSA 共同发布。
The secure hash algorithm are a family of cryptographic hash functions that are
published by the National Institute of Standards and Technology along with the NSA.

6302
10:07:34,720 --> 10:07:39,748
它作为联邦信息处理标准通过，也被称为 FIPS。
It was passed as a federal information processing standard, also known as FIPS.

6303
10:07:40,000 --> 10:07:42,720
它包含四个不同的哈希函数家族。
It has four different families of hash functions.

6304
10:07:43,118 --> 10:07:52,100
SSJ0 是 1993 年发布的 160-bit 哈希函数，后来因一个未公开的重大缺陷而被停止使用。
SSJ0 is a 160-bit hash function published in 1993 and it was closed down later after an undisclosed significant flaw.

6305
10:07:52,846 --> 10:07:58,560
SHA1 也是一个 160-bit 哈希函数，与早期的 MD5 算法相似。
SHA1 is also a 160-bit hash function which resembles the earlier MD5 algorithm.

6306
10:07:58,862 --> 10:08:03,012
这是由 NSA 设计的，作为数字签名算法的一部分。
This was designed by the NSA to be a part of the digital signature algorithm.

6307
10:08:03,840 --> 10:08:12,320
SHA2 是一个包含两个相似哈希函数的家族，它们具
有不同的块大小，分别称为 SHA 256 和 SHA512。
SHA2 is a family of two similar hash functions with different block sizes known as the SHA 256 and the SHA512.

6308
10:08:12,910 --> 10:08:14,400
它们在字大小上有所不同。
They differ in the word size.

6309
10:08:14,798 --> 10:08:20,420
SHA 256 使用 32-bit 字，而 SHA 512 使用 64-bit 字。
SHA 256 uses 32-bit words while SHA 512 uses 64-bit words.

6310
10:08:21,422 --> 10:08:25,120
SHA3 是一个被称为 KCAC 的哈希函数。
SHA3 is a hash function properly known as KCAC.

6311
10:08:25,360 --> 10:08:30,160
它是在 2012 年通过非 NSA 设计的公开竞赛选出的。
It was chosen in 2012 after a public competition among non-NSA designs.

6312
10:08:30,766 --> 10:08:37,860
它支持与 SHA2 相同的哈希长度，其内部结构与其他 SHA 家族显著不同。
It supports the same hash lens as SHA2 and its internal structure differs significantly from the rest of the SHA family.

6313
10:08:38,734 --> 10:08:42,160
正如我们之前迭代过的那样，这个过程非常简单。
As we have already iterated, the process is straightforward.

6314
10:08:42,542 --> 10:08:50,564
我们将明文消息传递给 SHA 哈希函数，它会对明文执行特定的数学运算来打乱数据。
We pass a plain text message to the SHA hash function, which in turn performs
certain mathematical operations on the clear text to scramble the data.

6315
10:08:51,214 --> 10:08:56,004
从中获得的 160-bit 摘要将与明文完全不同。
The 160-bit digest received from this is going to be radically different from the plain text.

6316
10:08:56,526 --> 10:09:00,708
任何哈希函数的目标都是生成看起来是随机的摘要。
The goal of any hash function is to produce digests that appear to be random.

6317
10:09:01,422 --> 10:09:06,500
要被认为是加密安全的，哈希函数应满足两个要求。
To be considered cryptographically secure, the hash function should meet two requirements.

6318
10:09:06,958 --> 10:09:13,040
第一，攻击者不可能生成与特定哈希值相匹配的消息。
First, that it is impossible for an attacker to generate a message that matches a specific hash value.

6319
10:09:13,200 --> 10:09:19,840
第二，攻击者不可能创建两条产生完全相同哈希值的消息。
And second, it should be impossible for an attacker to create two messages producing the exactly same hash value.

6320
10:09:20,014 --> 10:09:24,868
即使明文发生微小的变化，也应引起两个摘要的巨大差异。
Even a slight change in the plaintext should trigger a drastic difference in the two digest.

6321
10:09:25,486 --> 10:09:31,780
这在很大程度上防止了哈希碰撞，即两个不同的明文具有相同的摘要。
This goes a long way in preventing hash collisions, which takes place when two different plaintext have the same digest.

6322
10:09:33,198 --> 10:09:38,560
SHA 家族函数在生成摘要时需要遵循一些特性。
The SHA family functions have some characteristics that they need to follow while generating the digests.

6323
10:09:39,022 --> 10:09:40,548
让我们来看看其中的几个。
Let's go through a few of them.

6324
10:09:44,846 --> 10:09:51,840
在 SHA 1 和 SHA256 的情况下，明文的长度应小于 2 的 64 次方位。
The length of the clear text should be less than 2 to the power 64 bits in the case of SHA 1 and SH256.

6325
10:09:52,240 --> 10:10:01,508
这对于保持明文与哈希函数的兼容性至关重要，且
大小需要处于对比范围内，以使摘要尽可能随机。
This is essential to keep the plain text compatible with the hash function, and
the size needs to be in comparison area to keep the digest as random as possible.

6326
10:10:04,398 --> 10:10:13,440
在 SHA 256 算法中，哈希摘要的长度应为 256 位，在 SHA 512 算法中应为 512 位，以此类推。
The length of the hash digest should be 256 bits in the SHA 256 algorithm, 512 bits in the SHA 512 algorithm, and so on.

6327
10:10:13,934 --> 10:10:19,908
更大的摘要通常意味着更多的计算量，代价是牺牲速度和空间。
Bigger digest usually suggests significantly more calculations at the cost of speed and space.

6328
10:10:20,462 --> 10:10:28,804
我们通常选择最长的摘要来增强安全性，但哈希函数的速度和安全性之间必须达到一定的平衡。
We typically go for the longest digest to bolster security, but there must
be a definite balance between the speed and security of a hash function.

6329
10:10:32,654 --> 10:10:39,140
从设计上讲，所有的 SHA 512 和 SHA 256 哈希函数都是不可逆的。
By design, all hash functions of the SHA 512 SHA 256 are irreversible.

6330
10:10:39,856 --> 10:10:49,764
你既不能在已知摘要的情况下获取明文，也不应该
在将摘要再次输入到相同的哈希函数时得到原始值。
You should neither get a plaintext when you have the digest beforehand, nor should the
digest provide the original value when you pass it to the same hash function again.

6331
10:10:50,318 --> 10:10:59,588
另一种保护机制是，当哈希摘要第二次输入到 SHA 函数时，
我们应该得到与第一次完全不同的摘要。
Another case of protection is that when the hash digest is passed into the SHA function for a second time,
we should get a completely different digest from the first instance.

6332
10:11:00,016 --> 10:11:03,076
这样做是为了降低暴力破解攻击的概率。
This is done to reduce the chance of brute force attacks.

6333
10:11:04,718 --> 10:11:09,956
为了达到这种复杂程度，在获取摘要之前需要遵循一系列步骤。
To achieve this level of intricacy, there are a number of steps to be followed before we receive the digest.

6334
10:11:10,382 --> 10:11:15,300
让我们来看看 SHA 算法工作的详细过程。
Let us take a look at the detailed procedure as to how the SHA algorithm works.

6335
10:11:16,686 --> 10:11:20,292
第一步是使明文与哈希函数兼容。
The first step is to make the plaintext compatible with the hash function.

6336
10:11:21,134 --> 10:11:23,684
为此，我们需要对消息中的比特进行填充。
To do this, we need to pad the bits in the message.

6337
10:11:24,270 --> 10:11:30,436
当你收到输入字符串时，必须确保其大小比 512 的倍数少 64 位。
When you receive the input string, you have to make sure the size is 64 bits short of a multiple of 512.

6338
10:11:31,150 --> 10:11:37,924
在填充比特时，你必须先添加 1，然后添加剩余的 0 来补齐额外的字符。
When it comes to padding the bits, you must add 1 first followed by the remaining zeros to round out the extra characters.

6339
10:11:38,606 --> 10:11:44,356
这能让我们的字符串长度正好比 512 的任何倍数少 64 位。
This prepares our string to have a length just 64 bits less than any multiple of 512.

6340
10:11:45,582 --> 10:11:49,860
从这里开始，我们可以进入下一步，即填充长度比特。
Here on out, we can proceed to the next step where we have to pad the length bits.

6341
10:11:50,176 --> 10:11:59,748
最初，在第一步中，我们以一种方式附加消息，使得消息的总比特数比 512 的倍数少 64 位。
Initially, in the first step, we appended the message in such a way that the total
number of bits in the message was 64 bits short from becoming a multiple of 512.

6342
10:12:00,398 --> 10:12:07,268
现在我们添加长度比特，使得消息的总比特数正好是 512 的倍数。
Now we add the length of bits in such a way that the total number of bits in the message is a perfect multiple of 512.

6343
10:12:08,046 --> 10:12:13,892
这意味着 64 位加上原始消息的长度将成为 512 的倍数。
That means 64 bits plus the length of the original message becomes a multiple of 512.

6344
10:12:14,286 --> 10:12:17,124
这将变成最终需要进行哈希处理的字符串。
This becomes a final string that needs to be hashed.

6345
10:12:19,694 --> 10:12:22,756
在下一步中，我们需要初始化这些链式变量。
In the next step we have to initialize these chaining variables.

6346
10:12:23,822 --> 10:12:29,188
现在整个明文消息可以分解为每块 512 位的区块。
The entire plain text message can now be broken down into blocks of 512 bits each.

6347
10:12:30,158 --> 10:12:38,660
与使用四个寄存器或缓冲区的其他哈希算法（如 MD5）不同，
SHA 系列使用五个每个 32 位的缓冲区。
Unlike other hash algorithms like MD5, which use four registers or buffers, SHA family use five buffers of 32 bits each.

6348
10:12:39,086 --> 10:12:42,244
它们被命名为 A、B、C、D 和 E。
They are named A, B, C, D, and E.

6349
10:12:42,496 --> 10:12:50,052
这些寄存器会经过多轮操作，其中第一轮具有屏幕上显示的固定十六进制值。
These registers go through multiple rounds of operation, where the first
iteration has fixed hecedecimal values as can be seen in the screen.

6350
10:12:51,374 --> 10:12:59,300
接下来，我们必须处理每个 512 位块，将每个块分解为 16 个每个 32 位的子块。
Moving on, we have to process each of the 512-bit blocks by breaking each of them into 16 sub-blocks of 32 bits each.

6351
10:13:00,078 --> 10:13:08,324
每一个子块都会经过四轮操作，这些操作使用整个寄存器、512 位块以及常量数组。
Each of them goes through four rounds of operation that use the entire
register and have the 512-bit block along with the constant array.

6352
10:13:08,656 --> 10:13:12,176
在这四轮操作中，每一轮包含 20 次迭代。
Out of those four rounds, each round has 20 iterations.

6353
10:13:12,416 --> 10:13:15,140
所以总共通常有 80 轮。
So in general we have 80 rounds sum total.

6354
10:13:16,782 --> 10:13:20,356
常数 k 的值是一个包含 80 个元素的数组。
The constant value of k is an array of 80 elements.

6355
10:13:21,198 --> 10:13:28,068
在这 80 个元素中，每轮使用 16 个元素，所以每个元素对应 80 轮。
Of those 80, 16 elements are being used each round, so that comes out to 80 rounds for each of those elements.

6356
10:13:29,166 --> 10:13:33,252
正如下面的表格所示，t 的值随轮数而变化。
The value of t differs by the number of rounds as can be seen in the table below.

6357
10:13:35,726 --> 10:13:40,816
需要一个单一公式来计算每一轮和每次迭代的输出。
A single formula is necessary to calculate the output of each round and iteration.

6358
10:13:41,198 --> 10:13:51,748
