其他任务还包括由信息系统和业务管理制定的运营流程，参与灾难恢复计划（灾难恢复计划）测
试，以及促进故障排除和事件处理。
Others include the operations procedures as established by IS and Business Management,
participating in Test of disaster recovery plans, DRPs, and facilitating troubleshooting and incident handling.

8085
13:34:24,832 --> 13:34:29,764
我们将在接下来的屏幕继续介绍信息系统运营。
We shall continue with information system operations in the following screen.

8086
13:34:30,574 --> 13:34:40,432
详细说明操作任务和流程的程序，配合适当的信息系统管理监督，
是信息系统控制的必要组成部分。
Procedures detailing instructions for operational tasks and procedures coupled
with appropriate IS management oversight are necessary parts of IS control.

8087
13:34:41,392 --> 13:34:53,870
这些文档应包括运营程序、监控系统和应用、检测系统和应用错误及问题、备份与恢复、
处理 IT 问题和未解决问题等程序。
This documentation should include procedures for operations, monitoring systems and applications,
detecting systems and applications errors and problems, backup and recovery,

8088
13:34:53,870 --> 13:34:58,660
这些文档应包括运营程序、监控系统和应用、检测系统和应用错误及问题、备份与恢复、
处理 IT 问题和未解决问题等程序。
handling IT problems and unresolved issues, among other procedures.

8089
13:34:59,054 --> 13:35:02,788
让我们在下一个屏幕看看作业调度软件。
Let us look at job scheduling software in the next screen.

8090
13:35:04,014 --> 13:35:08,000
调度就是在无需人工干预的情况下实现操作自动化。
Scheduling is making operations automated without any attendance.

8091
13:35:08,366 --> 13:35:19,172
调度包括必须运行的作业、必须运行的作业顺序、作业执行顺序，以及导致问题执行的条件。
The schedule includes the job that must be run, the sequence of the jobs that must be run, the sequence of job execution,
and the conditions that cause problem execution.

8092
13:35:19,680 --> 13:35:22,692
作业应根据服务水平协议进行调度。
Job should be scheduled according to SLA.

8093
13:35:23,374 --> 13:35:35,268
高优先级作业应获得最佳资源可用性，而备份和系统重
组等维护功能，如果可能的话，应在非高峰时段进行。
High priority jobs should be given optimal resource availability, while maintenance functions such as backup and system reorganization
should, if possible, be performed during non-peak hours.

8094
13:35:35,950 --> 13:35:42,692
作业调度软件是用于处理大量批处理程序的机构所使用的软件。
Job scheduling software is software used by installations that process large number of batch routines.

8095
13:35:43,040 --> 13:35:48,964
它负责设置每日工作计划，并自动确定哪些作业需要提交处理。
It sets up daily work schedules and automatically determines which jobs to be submitted for processing.

8096
13:35:49,520 --> 13:36:03,108
作业调度的优点包括信息只需设置一次，降低出错概率，并定义作业依赖关系，
这样如果某个作业失败，依赖其输出的后续作业就不会被处理。
Advantages of job scheduling includes that information is set up only once, reducing chance of error,
job dependencies are defined so that if a job fails, subsequent jobs relying on its output will not be processed.

8097
13:36:03,520 --> 13:36:12,240
此外，此类软件还能确保记录所有作业的成功和失败，并减少对人工操作的依赖。
In addition, such software will ensure records are maintained of all
job successes and failures and there is less reliance on operations.

8098
13:36:13,134 --> 13:36:23,588
CISA 考生需要了解与硬件和网络组件、系统软件以及数据库管理系统相关的技术概念。
A CISA candidate is expected to have knowledge of the technology concepts related to
hardware and network components, system software, and database management systems.

8099
13:36:24,014 --> 13:36:30,724
信息系统审计师必须熟悉信息系统硬件及其网络组件的功能。
The IS auditor must be familiar with the functionality of information system hardware and its network components.

8100
13:36:31,200 --> 13:36:43,492
这包括理解支持组织目标和目标的 IS IT 解决方案中物理部分的重要性，
以及涉及系统软件的关键控制和风险。
This includes understanding the importance of the physical part of IS IT solutions that support the organizational objectives and
goals, as well as key control and risks involving system software.

8101
13:36:43,950 --> 13:36:56,548
虽然 CISA 考试不测试单个组件运行的技术知识，但
要求理解与每个组件相关的风险以及可能的控制功能。
Although the CISA exam does not test technical knowledge of the working of individual components,
an understanding of the risks associated with and possible control functions of each component is expected.

8102
13:36:56,960 --> 13:37:08,548
例如，了解路由器访问密码可能被共享的风险，但如果程序编写正确，
密码可以为网络弹性做出重大贡献。
An example of this is knowledge of the risk that router access passwords may be shared, but that if properly programmed,
passwords can make a major contribution to network resilience.

8103
13:37:09,070 --> 13:37:13,732
下一屏幕列出了此知识声明的主要覆盖领域。
The following screen lists the main areas of coverage in this knowledge statement.

8104
13:37:14,606 --> 13:37:28,900
主要覆盖领域包括 IS 网络基础设施、硬件审查、网络基础
设施和实施审查、操作系统、实用程序以及操作系统审查。
Main areas of coverage are IS network infrastructure, hardware reviews, network infrastructure and implementation reviews,
operating systems, utility programs, and operating system reviews.

8105
13:37:29,326 --> 13:37:33,572
让我们在下一屏幕看看企业网络架构。
Let us look at enterprise network architectures in the next screen.

8106
13:37:34,254 --> 13:37:38,160
了解企业网络架构非常重要。
Knowledge of enterprise network architectures is important.

8107
13:37:38,894 --> 13:37:50,372
这是因为今天的网络是组织内高速局域网和广域计算机网络的大型、
集中管理的互联网络架构解决方案的一部分。
This is because today's networks are part of a large, centrally managed inter-networked architecture solution of high-speed local and
wide area computer network in an organization.

8108
13:37:50,800 --> 13:38:04,100
此类网络可能包括网络分段或区块，其中可能包含基于 Web 的前端应用服务器（公共或私有）、
应用和数据库服务器，以及大型机服务器。
Such networks might include network segments or blocks which may include web-based front-end application servers, public or private,
application and database servers, and mainframe servers.

8109
13:38:04,640 --> 13:38:20,160
组织可能会实施面向服务的架构（SOA），并使用简单的对象访
问协议（SOAP）和可扩展标记语言（XML）的 Web 软件组件。
Organizations may implement service-oriented architectures, SOA, with web software
components using Simple Object Access Protocol, SOAP, and Extensible Markup Language, XML.

8110
13:38:20,640 --> 13:38:28,772
在这样的环境中，信息高度可访问，随时随地可用，并集中存储。
Within such an environment, information is highly accessible and available anytime, everywhere, and stored centrally.

8111
13:38:29,294 --> 13:38:34,404
让我们在下一页学习关于互联网和相关术语的内容。
Let us learn about the Internet and related terms in our next slide.

8112
13:38:35,438 --> 13:38:43,268
理解互联网的一个简单方法是看它由什么组成，以及与互联网相关的一些关键术语。
A simple way to understand the Internet is to look at what it is comprised of and some key terms used in relation to the Internet.

8113
13:38:43,822 --> 13:38:47,456
首先，互联网是一个巨大的全球网络，NW。
First, the Internet is a vast global network, NW.

8114
13:38:47,696 --> 13:38:51,012
全球网络由相互连接的网络组成。
The global network is comprised of interconnected networks.

8115
13:38:51,376 --> 13:38:55,524
这些互联网络的目的是交换信息。
The purpose of these interconnected networks is to exchange information.

8116
13:38:56,016 --> 13:38:59,588
网络中还有路由器用于引导流量。
There are also routers to direct traffic within the networks.

8117
13:38:59,936 --> 13:39:04,516
路由器使用路由表通过最有效的路线引导流量。
Routers use routing tables to direct traffic through the most efficient routes.

8118
13:39:05,134 --> 13:39:10,052
互联网服务提供商（ISP）让用户能够连接到互联网。
Internet service providers, ISPs, enable users to connect to Internet.

8119
13:39:10,446 --> 13:39:22,596
网络通过各种线路连接，包括 ISDN、光纤、卫星和区域网络，
这些网络通过网络接入点（NAP）连接。
Networks are connected via least lines, integrated service for digital networks, ISDN, fiber, satellite,
and regional networks are connected through Network Access Points, NAP.

8120
13:39:23,136 --> 13:39:26,340
没有单一的人或组织在运行互联网。
No single person or organization runs the Internet.

8121
13:39:26,656 --> 13:39:33,764
可以说它是一个电子无政府状态，使用 TCP IP 协议族作为事实上的标准。
It can be said to be an electronic anarchy that uses TCP IP protocol suite as the de facto standard.

8122
13:39:34,256 --> 13:39:39,460
让我们在接下来的屏幕中看看与互联网相关的常用术语。
Let us look at the common terms used in relation to the Internet in the following screen.

8123
13:39:40,174 --> 13:39:57,924
你可能会遇到的互联网常用术语包括 ISP，即互联网服务提供商；NAP，
即连接区域网络的网络访问点；以及流量集中点，指多个 ISP 的汇聚点。
Common terms that you will come across in relation to the Internet include ISP, which stands for Internet Service Provider, NAP,
Network Access Point that connects regional networks, traffic concentration point that refers to a point of convergence for many ISPs.

8124
13:39:58,416 --> 13:40:01,508
Telnet 是一种远程终端控制协议。
Telnet is a remote terminal control protocol.

8125
13:40:02,126 --> 13:40:08,772
DNS 代表域名系统，它负责将主机名转换为 IP 地址，反之亦然。
DNS stands for domain name service that translates host names into IP addresses and vice versa.

8126
13:40:09,296 --> 13:40:12,016
DNS 服务器提供这种转换服务。
DNS servers offer the translation service.

8127
13:40:12,336 --> 13:40:19,460
连接到互联网的 LAN 或大型机，提供完整的互联网访问，被称为直连。
LAN or mainframes connected to the Internet, providing full access to the Internet is referred to as a direct connection.

8128
13:40:19,950 --> 13:40:23,588
让我们在下一个屏幕中看看常见的互联网术语。
Let us look at common internet terms in the next screen.

8129
13:40:24,366 --> 13:40:28,484
在线服务允许用户充分利用互联网的全部力量。
Online services allow users to tap the full power of the Internet.

8130
13:40:28,910 --> 13:40:32,176
互联网的常见用途是下载或上传文件。
Popular use of Internet is to download or upload files.

8131
13:40:32,336 --> 13:40:36,096
这是通过文件传输协议 FTP 实现的。
This is enabled through the File Transfer Protocol, FTP.

8132
13:40:36,496 --> 13:40:46,212
通过匿名 FTP，任何人都可以通过用户标识 ID 和密码获得访问权限，尽管这被认为是有风险的。
With anonymous FTP, anyone can get access with user identification, ID, and password, BW, although this is considered risky.

8133
13:40:46,736 --> 13:40:54,116
简单邮件传输协议 SMTP 与互联网上的电子邮件交换相关或有助于电子邮件交换。
Simple Mail Transfer Protocol, SMTP, relates to or facilitates email exchange on the Internet.

8134
13:40:54,702 --> 13:41:05,380
简单网络管理协议 SNMP 是监控和控制网络设备、管理配置、性能和互联网安全的一种手段。
Simple Network Management Protocol, SNMP, is a means to monitor and control
network devices, manage configurations, performance, and Internet security.

8135
13:41:05,870 --> 13:41:09,604
现在让我们在下一个屏幕中讨论万维网。
Let us now discuss the World Wide Web in the next screen.

8136
13:41:10,574 --> 13:41:24,100
万维网或 WWW 是一种客户端服务器模型，其中客户端使用浏览器（例如 Internet Explorer）来
访问可能运行在 NT 或 Unix 操作系统上的 Web服务器。
World Wide Web or WWW is a client server model where the client uses a browser, for example, Internet Explorer,
to access a web server that could be running on NT or Unix operating system.

8137
13:41:24,576 --> 13:41:29,188
万维网是互联网中增长最快、最具创新性的部分。
The World Wide Web is the fastest growing and most innovative part of the Internet.

8138
13:41:29,696 --> 13:41:38,212
浏览万维网是通过输入网站的 URL，并使用超文本链接跳转到其他网站来实现的。
Navigation of the WWW is done through typing URL of the site and use of hypertext links to jump to other sites.

8139
13:41:38,656 --> 13:41:50,756
万维网使用超文本标记语言 HTML 来制作网页，并使用
超文本传输协议 HTTP 进行 Web服务器与浏览器的通信。
World Wide Web uses Hypertext Markup Language, HTML, for web pages, and
hypertext transfer protocol, HTTP, for web server browser communication.

8140
13:41:51,216 --> 13:41:57,508
让我们在接下来的屏幕中继续看与万维网相关的常用术语。
Let us continue to look at common terms in relation to the World Wide Web in the following screen.

8141
13:41:58,030 --> 13:42:04,580
你可能会遇到的万维网术语包括通用网关接口 CGI 脚本。
World Wide Web terms that you will come across include Common Gateway Interface, CGI scripts.

8142
13:42:05,136 --> 13:42:13,540
这是一种可执行的、机器无关软件程序，可以通过网页访问来执行特定任务。
This is an executable, machine-independent software program that can be accessed by a web page to perform specific tasks.

8143
13:42:13,936 --> 13:42:17,220
Cookies 帮助网页记住用户的偏好。
Cookies help a web page to remember preferences.

8144
13:42:17,536 --> 13:42:25,092
Cookie 是从 Web服务器发送到浏览器的消息，用于识别用户并准备定制页面。
A cookie is a message sent from a web server to a browser to identify users and prepare customized pages.

8145
13:42:25,536 --> 13:42:32,356
Applets 从 Web服务器下载到浏览器中执行，例如用于生成输入表单。
Applets are downloaded from web servers to execute in browsers, for example, to generate input forms.

8146
13:42:32,974 --> 13:42:37,860
在接下来的屏幕中，我们来看看客户端服务器模型及其相关术语。
In the following screen, we look at the client server model and its related terms.

8147
13:42:38,574 --> 13:42:46,084
在客户端服务器架构中，应用程序被拆分到不同的
计算机上运行，有些在客户端上，有些在服务器上。
In a client server architecture, an application is split to run on different computers, some on the client and some on the server.

8148
13:42:46,496 --> 13:42:48,804
这些任务是相互依赖的。
These tasks are mutually dependent.

8149
13:42:49,136 --> 13:42:53,668
在客户端端，图形用户界面可以是瘦客户端或胖客户端。
On the client side, the graphic user interface can be thin or thick.

8150
13:42:54,016 --> 13:43:00,900
服务器通常是多用户系统，例如大型机、小型机或个人电脑。
The server is usually a multi-user system, such as mainframe, mini computer, or personal computer.

8151
13:43:01,326 --> 13:43:07,296
服务器的一些功能包括文件、打印、数据库通信、传真等。
Some of the server functions include file, print, database communication, facsimile, etc.

8152
13:43:07,856 --> 13:43:15,684
客户端服务器架构的优势包括在计算机之间分配工作，以及共享系统和数据资源。
Advantages if client server architecture includes distributing work among computers and sharing of system and data resources.

8153
13:43:16,096 --> 13:43:21,796
在接下来的屏幕中，我们将讨论不同层级的客户端服务器架构和中间件。
In the following screen, we will discuss different tiers of client server architectures and middleware.

8154
13:43:22,830 --> 13:43:33,476
多层架构可以展示任务如何在图形用户界面、业务规
则和应用逻辑以及数据库层级之间在计算机中共享。
A multi-tiered architecture can be used to show how tasks are shared among computers at the graphic user interface through business
rules and application logic and database levels.

8155
13:43:33,808 --> 13:43:36,452
存在不同的客户端服务器架构。
There are different client-server architectures.

8156
13:43:36,768 --> 13:43:41,803
这些包括两层、三层和多层架构，即超过两层。
These include two-tier, three-tier, and multi-tiered, more than two tiers.

8157
13:43:42,446 --> 13:43:45,968
让我们在接下来的屏幕中看看两层架构。
Let us look at two-tier architecture in the following screen.

8158
13:43:46,350 --> 13:43:58,308
在两层客户端服务器架构中，客户端（例如图形用户界
面和业务规则）构成前端，而数据库服务器构成后端。
In a two-tier client-server architecture, there is a client, for example, graphic user interface and business rules,
which forms the front end and the database server, which forms the back end.

8159
13:43:58,688 --> 13:44:11,088
这种架构的局限性包括胖客户端综合征，例如大型复杂程
序需要更多的内存和 CPU，且这种架构的可扩展性不高。
Limitations of this architecture include a fat client syndrome, for example, big complex programs requiring more memory and CPU,
and this architecture is not highly scalable.

8160
13:44:11,248 --> 13:44:14,980
例如，当增加更多用户时就会出现问题。
For example, problems arise when more users are added.

8161
13:44:15,408 --> 13:44:19,172
让我们在接下来的屏幕中看看三层架构。
Let us look at three-tiered architecture in the following screen.

8162
13:44:20,206 --> 13:44:30,724
在三层客户端服务器架构中，前端由图形用户界面
表示，而后端由应用服务器和数据库服务器组成。
In a three-tiered client server architecture, the front end is represented by a graphic user interface,
while the back end is comprised of the application and database servers.

8163
13:44:31,088 --> 13:44:38,596
与两层架构相比，这种架构的优势包括瘦客户端且更具可扩展性。
Advantages of this architecture compared to a two-tiered include a thin client and it's more scalable.

8164
13:44:38,798 --> 13:44:41,732
例如，它可以支持成千上万的用户。
For example, can support thousands of users.

8165
13:44:42,128 --> 13:44:45,380
让我们在接下来的屏幕中讨论中间件。
Let us discuss middleware in the following screen.

8166
13:44:46,158 --> 13:44:56,100
中间件通过提供身份识别、安全、授权和目录服务，来管理图形用户界面与服务器之间的交互。
Middleware manages interaction between the graphic user interface and servers
by offering identification, security, authorization, and directory services.

8167
13:44:56,528 --> 13:45:04,708
这反过来支持客户端与服务器之间的通信、负载均衡、故障转移、组件管理和队列管理。
This in turn supports communication between clients and servers, load balancing, failover, component management, and queue management.

8168
13:45:05,102 --> 13:45:08,260
在下一个屏幕中，我们将介绍中间件的用途。
In the next screen we cover uses of middleware.

8169
13:45:09,166 --> 13:45:17,092
在用于处理和监控数据库事务的事务处理监控器中间件中，主要执行负载均衡。
In the Transaction Processing Monitors Middleware, used to handle and monitor database transaction mainly does load balancing.

8170
13:45:17,568 --> 13:45:26,756
对象请求代理 ORB 技术中的中间件支持在分布式环境中利用共享、可重用的业务对象。
Middleware in Object Request Broker ORB technology enables use of shared, reusable business objects in a distributed environment.

8171
13:45:27,086 --> 13:45:30,928
例如，Korba 和 Microsoft 的 COMDCom。
For example, Korba and Microsoft's COMDCom.

8172
13:45:31,408 --> 13:45:40,612
在远程过程调用中，RPC 中间件是允许客户端在远程计算机（服务器）上执行程序的协议。
In a remote procedure call, RPC Middleware is the protocol that enables client to execute a program on the remote computer, server.

8173
13:45:41,008 --> 13:45:50,084
最后，在消息服务器中，中间件程序异步地对消息进
行优先级排序、入队，并使用专用服务器处理消息。
Lastly, in messaging servers, middleware programs asynchronously prioritize, queue, process messages using dedicated servers.

8174
13:45:50,448 --> 13:45:54,724
让我们在接下来的屏幕中看看中间件的风险和控制措施。
Let us look at risks and controls of middleware in the following screen.

8175
13:45:55,822 --> 13:46:03,248
中间件的主要风险是来自多个操作系统环境的系统完整性丢失以及缺乏变更控制。
The major risk of middleware is loss of system integrity from multiple operating environments and lack of change control.

8176
13:46:03,728 --> 13:46:11,588
然而，可用于管理这些问题的控制措施包括充分测试系统、管理修改和版本。
However, controls that can be used to manage this include testing systems adequately, managing modifications, and versions.

8177
13:46:11,968 --> 13:46:15,844
在下一个屏幕中，我们进入计算机硬件部分。
In the next screen, we move on to our computer hardware.

8178
13:46:16,686 --> 13:46:27,268
屏幕上的图表展示了计算机硬件组件的广泛分类，以及计算机输入、处理和输出组件之间的通信。
The diagram on the screen shows a broad classification of computer hardware components and the communication between the input,
processing, and output components of a computer.

8179
13:46:27,648 --> 13:46:34,628
输入设备用于将数据和信息捕获到计算机的中央处理器中。
Input devices are used to capture data and information into the central processing unit of the computer.

8180
13:46:35,088 --> 13:46:42,180
中央处理器由算术逻辑单元、寄存器和主内存组成。
The central processing unit comprises of the arithmetic logic unit, registers, and the main memory.

8181
13:46:42,528 --> 13:46:53,092
图表还显示中央处理器连接到输出设备，通过这些设备将处理后的数据和信息传递给用户。
The diagram also shows that the central processing unit is connected to the output
devices through which processed data and information is communicated to the user.

8182
13:46:53,568 --> 13:46:58,756
辅助存储也连接到主机的中央处理器上。
A secondary storage is also connected to the main computer central processing unit.

8183
13:46:59,248 --> 13:47:03,780
接下来的屏幕将进一步解释这些组件中的每一个。
Each of these components is explained further in the following screens.

8184
13:47:04,686 --> 13:47:09,316
中央处理器构成了计算机的处理组件。
The central processing unit forms the processing components of a computer.

8185
13:47:09,648 --> 13:47:20,388
它包含一个执行数学和逻辑运算的算术逻辑单元、一个控制单元，以及用于处理事务的内部内存。
There is an arithmetic logic unit which performs mathematical and logical operations, a control unit,
and internal memory used for processing transactions.

8186
13:47:20,910 --> 13:47:28,996
输入和输出组件将事务信息传递给计算机，并显示或记录由计算机生成的输出。
Input and output components pass transaction information to the computer and display or record the output generated by the computer.

8187
13:47:29,408 --> 13:47:37,220
键盘和鼠标等计算机外设是仅输入设备，而打印机是仅输出设备。
Computer peripherals such as the keyboard and mouse are input only devices, whereas printers form output only devices.

8188
13:47:37,728 --> 13:47:45,728
计算机的其他组件包括主板、随机存取内存、RAM 和只读内存 只读内存。
Other components of a computer include motherboard, random access memory, RAM, and read only memory, ROM.

8189
13:47:46,128 --> 13:47:50,468
现在让我们在接下来的几个屏幕中看看计算机的类型。
Let us now look at types of computers in the following few screens.

8190
13:47:51,470 --> 13:47:58,340
计算机可以根据多个标准进行分类，主要是处理能力、尺寸和架构。
Computers can be categorized based on several criteria, mainly processing power, size, and architecture.

8191
13:47:58,704 --> 13:48:17,104
不同的类别包括超级计算机、高端和中端服务器、大型机、小型机、个人电脑（PC 或微型计算机）、
笔记本电脑、智能手机和个人数字助理 PDA。
The different categories include supercomputers, high-end and mid-range servers, mainframe, mini computer, personal computers,
PCs or microcomputer, notebook, laptop computers, smartphones, and personal digital assistants, PDAs.

8192
13:48:17,664 --> 13:48:28,864
超级计算机是体积巨大且价格昂贵的计算机，具有最高
的处理速度，用于特殊用途，如复杂的数学或逻辑计算。
Supercomputers are very large and expensive computers with the highest processing speed used for specialized purposes,
use complex mathematical or logical calculations.

8193
13:48:29,024 --> 13:48:38,116
例如，巨大的计算能力被用于确定天气模式，例如特定地点发生海啸或地震的概率。
For example, huge computing power is used to determine weather patterns,
such as probability of tsunami or earthquake occurring in a given location.

8194
13:48:38,446 --> 13:48:46,020
高端和中端服务器是多处理计算机系统，能够支持数千名同时在线的用户。
High-end and mid-range servers are multiprocessing computer systems capable of supporting thousands of simultaneous users.

8195
13:48:46,384 --> 13:48:50,884
这些计算机与大型机的区别在于价格更低廉。
These computers differ from mainframes by virtue of being less expensive.

8196
13:48:51,264 --> 13:49:04,196
高端的运行 Uni Operating System OS 并可作为数据库服务器使用，
而低端的运行 Windows OS 并可作为应用程序打印服务器使用。
The higher end ones utilize Uni Operating System OS and may be used as database servers,
while the lower end ones utilize Windows OS and may be used as application print servers.

8197
13:49:04,878 --> 13:49:15,492
大型机是大型通用计算机，在多用户、多处理环境中运行，
通常为成千上万的内部和外部用户提供服务。
Mainframe computers are large, general purpose computers operating in a multi-user,
multiprocessing environment and usually serves thousands of internal external users.

8198
13:49:15,904 --> 13:49:23,236
许多计算机被中型机构使用，并在多用户、多处理环境中运行。
Many computers are used by mid-sized organizations and operate in a multi-user, multi-processing environment.

8199
13:49:23,598 --> 13:49:34,884
个人电脑（PC），也称为微型计算机，是小型、廉价
的计算机，被称为 PC 或工作站，专为个人用户设计。
Personal computers, PCs, also known as microcomputers, are small, inexpensive
computers referred to as PCs or workstations and designed for individual users.

8200
13:49:35,118 --> 13:49:39,044
它们价格低廉并使用微处理器技术。
They are inexpensive and use microprocessor technology.

8201
13:49:39,504 --> 13:49:50,116
笔记本电脑是轻便的，重量在 10 磅（5 公斤）以下，
是依靠普通交流电连接或可充电电池组供电的个人电脑。
Notebooks, laptop computers are lightweight, under 10 pounds, 5 kilograms,
personal computers powered by normal AC connection or rechargeable battery pack.

8202
13:49:50,464 --> 13:49:52,996
它们因其可移植性而受到青睐。
They are preferred because of their portability.

8203
13:49:53,264 --> 13:50:01,584
然而，由于它们是便携式的，在 LAN 无线连接等情况下，它们容易受到盗窃或连接劫持的攻击。
However, local area network by being portable, they are vulnerable
to theft or connectivity hijacked in a LAN wireless connection, etc.

8204
13:50:02,222 --> 13:50:09,508
智能手机和个人数字助理 PDA 是小型手持式数字设备，尺寸与计算器相当。
Smartphones and personal digital assistance PDAs are small handheld digital devices the size of a calculator.

8205
13:50:09,824 --> 13:50:23,716
它们也被称为 Palm Tops，用作个人管理器、计划表、电话、传真，具有网络技术能力，
并可与个人电脑进行接口连接，用于现场数据采集和通信。
Also known as Palm Tops, used as a personal organizer and planners, telephone, fax have networking capabilities and can interface with
personal computers and are used for field data collection and for communication.

8206
13:50:24,064 --> 13:50:27,076
它们使用基于笔的电磁笔代替键盘。
They use pen-based stylus instead of keyboard.

8207
13:50:27,344 --> 13:50:36,324
它们还可以作为调度器、电话、通讯录、待办事项列表，以
及用于办公自动化、电子表格、文本编辑器，例如 MS Word。
They can also be used as schedulers, phone, address book, to-do list, and
for office automation, spreadsheets, text editor, for example, MS Word.

8208
13:50:36,624 --> 13:50:39,332
有些具备手写识别能力。
Some have handwriting recognition capability.

8209
13:50:39,744 --> 13:50:47,140
在下一个屏幕中，我们将继续讨论计算机硬件和架构，并了解外设。
In the next screen, we will continue our discussion of computer hardware and architectures and learn about peripheral devices.

8210
13:50:47,918 --> 13:51:00,708
计算机外设包括输入输出设备、音频视频卡、CD-ROMs、只读内存、DVDs、磁带驱动器、
磁盘驱动器、打印机和调制解调器。
Computer peripheral devices include input-output devices, audio video cards,
CD-ROMs, read-only memory, DVDs, tape drives, disk drives, printers, and modems.

8211
13:51:01,166 --> 13:51:04,676
一些常用的计算机术语包括以下内容。
Some commonly used computer terminologies include the following.

8212
13:51:05,104 --> 13:51:12,708
多任务处理是指通过为每个任务分配时间片，同时运行两个或更多任务。
Multitasking, which refers to running of two or more tasks concurrently by allocating time slots slices to each task.

8213
13:51:13,184 --> 13:51:18,148
另一方面，多道程序设计是指同时运行两个或更多程序。
Multiprogramming, on the other hand, refers to running two or more programs concurrently.

8214
13:51:18,574 --> 13:51:26,276
多处理是另一个术语，指两个或更多处理器共享内存并同时执行程序。
Multiprocessing is another term used when two or more processors share memory and execute programs simultaneously.

8215
13:51:26,624 --> 13:51:35,268
在多用户或时间共享环境中，多个用户同时访问并使用计算机和操作系统。
In multi-user or time-sharing environments, multiple users access and use computer and the operating system simultaneously.

8216
13:51:35,664 --> 13:51:43,428
多线程描述了一个过程，即在程序执行时，多个子活动同时发生。
Multi threading is describes a process in which several sub activities take place when a program is being executed.

8217
13:51:43,824 --> 13:51:50,500
随着时间的推移，计算机硬件经历了许多发展，我们将在下一屏看到。
There are numerous computer hardware developments that have occurred over time, as we shall see in the next screen.

8218
13:51:51,726 --> 13:52:04,868
计算机硬件的一些发展包括内存卡、闪存盘、U盘、一次写
入多次读取、蠕虫、内存卡、闪存以及通用串行总线USB。
Some of the developments in computer hardware include memory cards, flash drives, pen drive, write once and read many, Worm,
Memory Cards, Flash Memory, and Universal Serial Bus, USB.

8219
13:52:05,408 --> 13:52:13,636
内存卡、闪存盘、U盘是USB和内存卡技术的结合，非常适合用于存储信息。
Memory cards, flash drives, pen drive are a combination of USB and memory card technology that is useful in storing information.

8220
13:52:14,062 --> 13:52:22,724
然而，如果它们丢失或被盗，会对存储的数据构成非常严重的安全风险，
并且可能被用来绕过可启动的安全检查。
However, they pose very serious security risks to the stored data if they
are lost or stolen and can be used to bypass bootable security checks.

8221
13:52:23,168 --> 13:52:28,448
大量的数据和信息可以非常快速地传输到闪存中。
Large amounts of data and information can be transferred to flash memory very fast.

8222
13:52:29,008 --> 13:52:38,692
一次写入多次读取的蠕虫包括紧凑型光盘，比如用于音乐的CD，最高可达80分钟，
以及用于数据文件的700MB光盘。
Write once and read many worm includes compact disks, CDs, like the ones
used for music, up to 80 minutes, and for data files, 700 megabytes.

8223
13:52:39,008 --> 13:52:44,932
可记录、可重写的紧凑型光盘，即CDR、CDRW，在技术上不属于蠕虫。
Compact Disc recordable, rewritable, CDR, CDRW, are technically not a worm.

8224
13:52:45,168 --> 13:52:52,964
另一个例子是数字视频光盘DVD，它使用大容量的光学存储技术，容量可达GB级别。
Another example is digital video disc DVD that uses optical storage technology with large capacity, gigabytes.

8225
13:52:53,328 --> 13:52:56,324
让我们在下一屏看看其他的进展。
Let us look at other developments in the following screen.

8226
13:52:56,974 --> 13:53:01,220
内存卡和闪存是存储信息的替代设备。
Memory cards, flash memory are alternative devices to store information.

8227
13:53:01,488 --> 13:53:11,972
它们体积小、非易失性、可拆卸，且易于擦除和存储数据信息，还可以与相机、
个人数字助理等其他外设配合使用。
They are small, non-volatile, removable, and easy to erase and store data information
in and can be used with other peripherals like cameras, personal digital assistants.

8228
13:53:12,448 --> 13:53:19,236
通用串行总线USB是一种串行总线标准，用于将设备与主机连接。
Universal Serial Bus USB is a serial bus standard that interfaces devices with a host.

8229
13:53:19,568 --> 13:53:29,188
它的设计目的是允许将许多外设连接到单一的标准接口插座上，
并通过支持热插拔来提高即插即用的能力。
It was designed to allow connection of many peripherals to a single standardized
interface sockets and improve the plug and play capabilities by allowing hot swapping.

8230
13:53:29,728 --> 13:53:33,796
在下一屏，我们来看看常见的企业后端设备。
In the next screen, we look at common enterprise backend devices.

8231
13:53:34,670 --> 13:53:50,780
打印服务器用于整合打印资源以节省成本；文件服务器用于管理全组织对文件和程序的访问；
应用程序服务器用于托管应用程序，允许用户访问集中式程序；以及Web服务器，
Print servers which consolidate printing resources for cost saving, file servers that manage organization-wide access to files and
program, application program servers that host applications, and allow users or access to centralized programs, and web servers,

8232
13:53:50,780 --> 13:53:52,070
打印服务器用于整合打印资源以节省成本；文件服务器用于管理全组织对文件和程序的访问；
应用程序服务器用于托管应用程序，允许用户访问集中式程序；以及Web服务器，
which provide information and services to internal employees or external public customers through web pages.

8233
13:53:52,070 --> 13:53:57,540
通过网页向内部员工或外部公众客户提供信息和服务。
which provide information and services to internal employees or external public customers through web pages.

8234
13:53:57,968 --> 13:54:06,564
访问Web服务器是使用统一资源定位符URL，例如www.google.com。
A web server is accessed using a Universal Resource Locator, URL, for example, www.google.com.

8235
13:54:06,848 --> 13:54:09,380
它还利用DNS服务。
It also utilizes DNS services.

8236
13:54:09,888 --> 13:54:16,420
代理服务器提供用户与资源之间的中间环节，而不是直接访问。
Proxy servers provide an intermediate link between users and resources as opposed to direct access.

8237
13:54:16,848 --> 13:54:21,700
数据库服务器是包含原始数据和应用程序的仓库。
Database server is a repository containing raw data and applications.

8238
13:54:22,048 --> 13:54:25,284
Web服务器为用户消费处理数据。
Web servers process data for user consumption.

8239
13:54:25,728 --> 13:54:36,448
专用设备是像防火墙、IDS、交换机、路由器等特殊设备，可用于支持虚拟专用网络、负载均衡等。
Appliances are specialized devices like firewall, IDS, switches, routers
that could be used to support virtual private networks, load balancing, etc.

8240
13:54:37,134 --> 13:54:40,772
现在让我们在下一屏考虑硬件风险。
Now let us consider hardware risks in the next screen.

8241
13:54:41,486 --> 13:54:55,940
计算机硬件面临以下风险：数据和介质丢失、闪存盘丢失（可能导致未经授权的访问）、
数据损坏（可能仅仅是因为USB驱动器拔插不当引起的）。
Computer hardware is exposed to the following risks data and media loss, loss of flash drives,
which may lead to unauthorized access to data, corruption of data, which can simply be caused by improper unplugging of USB drives.

8242
13:54:56,462 --> 13:55:03,108
病毒和其他恶意软件包含感染文档，并可以通过闪存盘传播。
Viruses and other malicious software contain ininfected documents and which can spread via flash disks.

8243
13:55:03,488 --> 13:55:18,250
恶意代码包括用于捕捉黑客密码的键盘记录器、数据窃取（黑客、企业间谍、
不满的员工可能窃取数据）、利用社会工程学获取对个人电脑的物理访问，
Malicious code include key loggers to capture passwords for hackers, data theft, where hackers, corporate spies,
disgruntled employees may steal data, use of social engineering to gain physical access to personal computers,

8244
13:55:18,250 --> 13:55:18,770
恶意代码包括用于捕捉黑客密码的键盘记录器、数据窃取（黑客、企业间谍、
不满的员工可能窃取数据）、利用社会工程学获取对个人电脑的物理访问，
losses of confidentiality that may come as a result of losing a memory stick with confidential data.

8245
13:55:18,770 --> 13:55:24,708
以及由于丢失包含机密数据的内存棒而导致的机密性损失。
losses of confidentiality that may come as a result of losing a memory stick with confidential data.

8246
13:55:25,166 --> 13:55:27,300
这可能会导致法律责任。
This may lead to legal liability.

8247
13:55:27,728 --> 13:55:30,756
医疗信息的 HIPAA 要求。
HIPAA requirements for health information.

8248
13:55:31,168 --> 13:55:35,364
让我们在下一屏看看保护硬件的控制措施。
Let us look at controls to safeguard hardware in the following screen.

8249
13:55:36,238 --> 13:55:41,956
为了保护计算机硬件免受这些风险的影响，可以采取以下控制措施。
In order to safeguard computer hardware against these risks, the following controls can be put in place.

8250
13:55:42,510 --> 13:55:44,964
加密内容在域 5 中有完整涵盖。
Encryption fully covered in domain 5.

8251
13:55:45,248 --> 13:55:49,316
教育安全人员，让他们意识到环境中的风险。
Educating security personnel to be aware of the risk in their environment.

8252
13:55:49,648 --> 13:55:54,596
执行桌面锁定策略，时长根据环境风险而定。
To enforce the lock desktop policy, duration based on risk of environment.

8253
13:55:55,008 --> 13:56:00,548
更新杀毒软件策略，并强制对 USB 闪存盘进行扫描。
Update the antivirus policy and enforce mandatory scanning of USB flash drive.

8254
13:56:01,038 --> 13:56:06,436
使用 Microsoft Active Directory 组策略来实现细粒度的控制。
Granular control using Microsoft Active Directory Group policy to implement controls.

8255
13:56:06,768 --> 13:56:09,888
开展用户意识计划，以改变文化行为。
User awareness programs for culture behavior change.

8256
13:56:10,128 --> 13:56:15,236
购买时仅使用集成了安全功能的安全设备。
Use only secure devices which have security integrated into devices when buying them.

8257
13:56:15,408 --> 13:56:25,252
包含退还信息，包含包含联系详情的文本文件，但排除公司名称，
以便捡到闪存盘的人能将其归还给所有者。
Include return information, include text file with contact details, excluding company name,
to allow whoever collects the flash drive to return it to the owner.

8258
13:56:25,648 --> 13:56:31,568
在下一屏，我们来看看射频识别，通常称为 RFID。
In the next screen, we look at radio frequency identification, commonly known as RFID.

8259
13:56:32,686 --> 13:56:38,372
RFID 利用无线电波来识别限定半径内的带标签物体。
RFID uses radio waves to identify tagged objects within a limited radius.

8260
13:56:38,656 --> 13:56:49,924
它使用一个包含产品标识信息的微芯片标签，以及一个将信息传输到射频识别读头的天线。
It uses a tag which is a microchip to store information with the identification of the product and an antenna that transmits
information to the radio frequency identification reader.

8261
13:56:50,336 --> 13:56:52,804
标签有两种供电模式。
There are two modes of powering the tags.

8262
13:56:53,198 --> 13:57:03,460
主动标签由自带电池供电，利用更高频率，通信半
径更广，数据容量更大，可重复使用，但价格更贵。
Active tags that are powered by own batteries utilize higher frequencies, wider
communication radius, have more data capacity, are reusable, but are more expensive.

8263
13:57:03,776 --> 13:57:09,092
被动标签则从射频识别读头的辐射中获取能量。
And passive tags that draw power from the radio frequency identification reader radiation.

8264
13:57:09,376 --> 13:57:20,292
它包含基础信息，容量为 2 KB，使用较低频率，通信半
径较小，数据容量较少，不可重复使用，但价格更便宜。
It has basic information, 2 kilobytes, uses lower frequencies, smaller
communication radius, less data capacity, is not reusable, but it is less expensive.

8265
13:57:20,814 --> 13:57:25,316
让我们在下一屏看看 RFID 的应用。
Let us look at the applications of RFID in the following screen.

8266
13:57:26,190 --> 13:57:30,308
射频识别可用于以下领域。
Radio frequency identification can be used in the following areas.

8267
13:57:30,670 --> 13:57:36,932
资产管理，例如在图书馆，因为它不需要视距。
Asset management, for example, in the library because it does not require optical line of sight.

