You have to customize it to your own company.

11094
18:41:04,096 --> 18:41:12,740
然后他基本上整合了缓解控制措施，我的意思是，为了检测并应对每一个步骤。
And then he basically puts together mitigating Concepts, mitigating controls, I mean, to detect and respond to each of the steps.

11095
18:41:13,102 --> 18:41:14,660
这就是威胁猎人做的事情。
This is what a threat hunter does.

11096
18:41:14,990 --> 18:41:19,236
这就是那些真正从事风险管理的人整天在做的事情。
This is what people who are really doing risk management do all day long.

11097
18:41:19,726 --> 18:41:21,776
他们不会只是说，好，哪些是重要的控制措施？
They don't just say, okay, what are the important controls?

11098
18:41:21,936 --> 18:41:23,616
软件供应商卖给我什么？
What are the software vendors selling me?

11099
18:41:23,696 --> 18:41:27,012
或者什么技术很酷，或者我在街上听到什么消息？
Or what is it cool to implement, or what am I hearing about in the street?

11100
18:41:27,758 --> 18:41:32,356
你必须找出你公司自己的问题，然后正确地应用控制措施。
You have to figure out your own company's problems and then apply the controls correctly.

11101
18:41:33,296 --> 18:41:35,696
你可以使用各种网络安全框架。
You can use all sorts of cybersecurity frameworks.

11102
18:41:35,776 --> 18:41:37,476
外面有几十个，实际上有几百个。
There are dozens of them out there, hundreds really.

11103
18:41:37,710 --> 18:41:43,246
有来自 United States 的 NIST 相关内容，有 COSO，还有很多，还有 ISO，这些都是全球标准。
There's the NIST stuff from the United States, there's COSO, there's many, there's ISO, Worldwide standards.

11104
18:41:43,696 --> 18:41:48,736
你必须根据自己的公司来定制这些内容，因为每家公司都不一样。
You have to customize these things to your own company because each company is different.

11105
18:41:48,816 --> 18:41:51,524
如果你只是套用通用的规则，那你就会陷入麻烦。
And if you just apply a generic rule, you're going to be in trouble.

11106
18:41:51,856 --> 18:41:53,572
那么这部分该怎么放呢？
So where does this fit in?

11107
18:41:54,446 --> 18:41:58,496
我已经讲过了 Lockheed Martin 原则，现在我要加快一点速度了。
I already talked about Lockheed's Exchange principle, and I'm going to move a bit faster now.

11108
18:42:00,494 --> 18:42:01,136
这是什么意思？
What does this mean?

11109
18:42:01,296 --> 18:42:05,456
你必须应用并映射你的控制措施。
You have to apply and map your controls.

11110
18:42:05,646 --> 18:42:11,876
我说的控制措施，比如明显的例子就是防火墙，或者入侵检测系统，或者是 SIMS，对吧？
By controls, I mean, let's say an obvious one is a firewall or intrusion detection systems or SIMS, right?

11111
18:42:12,336 --> 18:42:15,216
安全、信息和事件监控软件。
Security, information, and event monitoring software.

11112
18:42:15,296 --> 18:42:18,468
你必须将这些资源应用于你的核心资源上。
And you have to apply these resources to your essential resources.

11113
18:42:18,736 --> 18:42:21,572
这些核心资源在不同公司之间是不同的。
Those essential resources are different from company to company.

11114
18:42:21,856 --> 18:42:29,028
它可能是 SharePoint 服务器，可能是 WordPress 服务器，
也可能是 E-commerce 相关的东西、数据库，或者任何东西。
It might be that SharePoint server, might be that WordPress server, could be e-commerce stuff, database, whatever.

11115
18:42:29,616 --> 18:42:32,356
然后你必须正确地应用流程。
And then you have to apply processes properly.

11116
18:42:33,294 --> 18:42:41,136
这意味着作为风险经理，作为威胁猎人，你不再是像克林特·伊斯特伍德那样闯进来的一匹野马。
This means that as you are a risk manager, as you're a threat hunter,
you no longer are just that cowboy coming in like Clint Eastwood.

11117
18:42:41,216 --> 18:42:45,136
我喜欢克林特·伊斯特伍德的电影，但你不再是以电影里的牛仔身份出现的。
I love Clint Eastwood movies, but you're not coming in as a movie cowboy anymore.

11118
18:42:45,296 --> 18:42:48,096
你不再仅仅是巫师甘道夫或者所谓的专家。
You're not just Gandalf the wizard or the guru.

11119
18:42:48,496 --> 18:42:50,256
你现在是网络侦探。
You are now the cyber detective.

11120
18:42:50,446 --> 18:42:52,816
随着我与行业内更多人的交流，我发现……
More and more as I talk to people in the industry.

11121
18:42:53,134 --> 18:42:54,496
你就是网络侦探。
You're the cyber detective.

11122
18:42:54,816 --> 18:42:58,308
你通过推断来发现问题。
You deduce and find problems.

11123
18:42:58,638 --> 18:43:04,016
如果要用一个西方中心的类比，你有点像福尔摩斯。
You're kind of to use a western centric metaphor, you're kind of Sherlock Holmes.

11124
18:43:04,176 --> 18:43:05,376
或者你就是向导。
Or you are the guide.

11125
18:43:05,616 --> 18:43:09,296
想象一下我在 UK 的斯诺登山攀登。
Imagine that's me climbing Mount Snowden in in the UK.

11126
18:43:09,774 --> 18:43:18,692
你是在遵循一条路径，并帮助人们使用正确的工具，以便他们能爬上山或者沿着小径前行。
You're uh you're following a path and you're helping people use the right tools so you can get up the mountain or go along the trail.

11127
18:43:19,216 --> 18:43:20,576
你是团队队长，对吧？
the team captain, right?

11128
18:43:20,718 --> 18:43:25,604
对于那些踢足球、橄榄球或者板球的观众来说。
For all you footballers out there, or rugby or for that matter, cricket.

11129
18:43:26,606 --> 18:43:29,956
你是团队队长，负责协调和切换资源。
You're the team captain where you coordinate and pivot resources.

11130
18:43:30,222 --> 18:43:33,616
这些是威胁猎人更现代的心态。
Those are the newer mindsets of the threat hunter.

11131
18:43:33,696 --> 18:43:36,324
威胁猎人随后要学习企业是如何运作的。
The threat hunter then learns how a business works.

11132
18:43:37,870 --> 18:43:39,856
这一点我再怎么强调都不为过。
and I can't emphasize that more.

11133
18:43:40,016 --> 18:43:43,776
你要学习并清晰地了解系统上的端点。
You learn and you gain a clear understanding of the endpoints on the system.

11134
18:43:43,856 --> 18:43:50,176
这意味着所有的物联网设备、所有的手机、所有的 IT 设备，还有所有的台式机等等。
That means all the IoT devices, all the phones, all of the IT, uh, all the desktops, et cetera.

11135
18:43:50,798 --> 18:43:53,696
你会学习构成网络的网络技术最佳实践。
You learn networking best practices that constitute a network.

11136
18:43:53,776 --> 18:43:57,616
所以你会学习网络如何运作，包括端点和网络基础设施。
So you then learn about how the network works, endpoints and also network infrastructure.

11137
18:43:57,776 --> 18:44:04,132
更重要的是，你会学习信息如何在网络中的一个系统流向另一个系统。
More importantly, you learn how information flows from one system in that network to another.

11138
18:44:04,462 --> 18:44:05,856
因为这就是黑客对你所做的事情。
Because that's what hackers are doing to you.

11139
18:44:05,936 --> 18:44:07,696
然后你会发现到底发生了什么。
And you find out what's going on.

11140
18:44:07,854 --> 18:44:22,256
所以你基本上是在建立假设，并进入一种思维循环，然后
你观察并调查网络系统或端点，寻找模式并寻找入侵指标。
So you're basically creating hypotheses and you're engaging in a kind of loop of thought,
and then you look and you investigate network systems or endpoints to look for patterns and you look for indicators of compromise.

11141
18:44:22,478 --> 18:44:23,676
有些人称之为 TTPs。
Some people call it TTPs.

11142
18:44:23,790 --> 18:44:25,696
我称之为入侵指标。
I call it indicators of compromise.

11143
18:44:26,094 --> 18:44:32,964
然后你进行一些分析，然后重新开始，查看你系统的基础设施，查看开发人员。
And then you do some analytics and you start over again and you look
through the infrastructure of your system, you look into the developers.

11144
18:44:33,358 --> 18:44:41,156
如果你的公司专注于代码开发，那么你需要确保那些代码开发人员的工作方式是安全的。
If you have a company that is focusing on code development, then you need to make sure how those code developers are working.

11145
18:44:41,486 --> 18:44:44,096
所以你要在你的数据上实施安全措施。
So you implement security on your data.

11146
18:44:44,256 --> 18:44:58,976
所以随着信息的流动，当你关注允许信息流动和存储的那些技术元素时，
你就会了解到这些信息如何被中断，更重要的是，如何被篡改。
So you as that information flows, and then as you focus on the technical elements that allow that information to flow and where it is
stored, you then learn how that information can be interrupted and more importantly, manipulated.

11147
18:44:59,216 --> 18:45:04,096
然后你寻找新的网络流量，寻找系统上的新进程，以及被丢弃的文件。
Then you look for new network traffic, you look for new processes on the system, dropped files.

11148
18:45:04,176 --> 18:45:06,468
这些都是入侵指标的例子。
These are all examples of indicators of compromise.

11149
18:45:07,534 --> 18:45:12,704
在奇怪的时间连接到奇怪的地方，或者在正常时间连接到奇怪的地方。
Connections to strange places at strange times or strange places at normal times.

11150
18:45:13,424 --> 18:45:22,144
如果威胁猎人觉得这是安全问题，他或她就会把这些问题报告给安全运营中心。
The threat hunter then reports these types of issues if he or she feels it's a problem to the security or secure operations center.

11151
18:45:22,304 --> 18:45:23,364
这就是 SOC。
That's what a SOC is.

11152
18:45:23,790 --> 18:45:25,220
安全运营中心。
Secure Operations Center.

11153
18:45:25,742 --> 18:45:30,692
你会与 Blue Team 和 Red Team 合作，那是 Red Team，不是 red team，抱歉之前的拼写错误。
You work with Blue Team and Red Team, that's supposed to be red team, not read team, sorry about the typo there.

11154
18:45:31,664 --> 18:45:35,620
你会与管理层和董事会合作，并提出解决方案。
You work with management and the board and you suggest solutions.

11155
18:45:36,750 --> 18:45:39,904
最重要的是，威胁猎人寻找我称之为「间隙」的东西。
Most importantly, a threat hunter looks for what I call interstices.

11156
18:45:40,144 --> 18:45:41,924
这是一个用来形容「漏洞」的华丽词汇。
That's a fancy word for gaps.

11157
18:45:42,464 --> 18:45:48,964
你会寻找那些一种技术与另一种技术连接的中间地带。
You look where in between places where where one technology and another connect.

11158
18:45:49,390 --> 18:45:51,104
这里我给你举几个简单的例子。
Here you give you a couple quick examples.

11159
18:45:51,344 --> 18:46:00,932
最明显的例子是即时通讯和/或电子邮件，还有人，
这就是我所说的中间空间，你知道，就是我们，对吧？
Most obvious examples, instant messaging and or email and people, where people, that's what I mean by neat space, you know, us, right?

11160
18:46:01,326 --> 18:46:02,948
而且网络空间正在融合。
And cyberspace converge.

11161
18:46:03,374 --> 18:46:18,624
比如商业邮件攻击，有人钓鱼攻击 CEO，或者更准确地说，是 CEO 的助理，
获取信息或能够进行转账，或者类似的任何事情。
So a a business email compromise where somebody fishes the CEO, or more relevantly, the CEO's assistant,
and gets information or is able to conduct a wire transfer, any of those sort of things.

11162
18:46:18,784 --> 18:46:31,984
这就是互联网控制、工业控制系统和控制物理设备（如工厂、炼油厂、
公用事业）的 SCADA 系统与网络工具或计算机相互连接的地方。
It's where ICE internet control industrial control systems and SCADA systems that control physical devices factories, refineries,
utilities, interconnect with cyber tools or with computers.

11163
18:46:32,144 --> 18:46:33,796
这就是黑客进入并发起攻击的地方。
That's where hackers go and attack.

11164
18:46:34,766 --> 18:46:44,964
物理进入建筑，也就是人们走进建筑的地方，那是可能产生间隙的地方，
这就是为什么我们要部署生物识别或其他手段来尝试控制这些间隙。
Physical access to a building where people walk into a building, that's where there's gaps can form,
and that's why we put biometrics in place or whatever to try to control those gaps.

11165
18:46:45,326 --> 18:46:55,780
还有很多不同的例子我不会一一展开，但这种间隙安全的概念，也就是在中间地带的概念，
对于威胁猎人管理风险来说非常重要。
There are many different examples that I won't go into, but this concept of interstitial security, of in-between places,
very important thing for where the threat hunter manages risk.

11166
18:46:56,366 --> 18:46:57,584
所以我想听听你们的看法。
So I want to hear it.

11167
18:46:57,744 --> 18:47:02,724
你认为威胁狩猎对你来说只是个流行词，还是一个真实的职位或活动？
Do you think that threat hunting is kind of a buzz phrase to you, or is it a real job role or activity?

11168
18:47:03,406 --> 18:47:04,868
只是好奇你们的观点。
just curious about your opinion.

11169
18:47:05,582 --> 18:47:15,010
告诉我们你的看法，给我你的意见，然后在这次演示结束后，
花点时间在你们知道的招聘公告板上查一下威胁狩猎这
Give us your opinion, give me your opinion, and then take some time after this presentation and look up that concept of threat hunting
in the job bulletin boards that you know of, in the states here it's DICE and Monster and Indeed.com.

11170
18:47:15,010 --> 18:47:19,364
个概念，在美国这里是 DICE、Monster 和 Indeed.com。
Give us your opinion, give me your opinion, and then take some time after this presentation and look up that concept of threat hunting
in the job bulletin boards that you know of, in the states here it's DICE and Monster and Indeed.com.

11171
18:47:19,584 --> 18:47:20,228
到处都能看到相关信息。
It's all around.

11172
18:47:21,678 --> 18:47:34,436
所以关键的安全技能是识别模式的能力，模式识别、数据
分析，也就是你分析和枚举网络，或者你分析和枚举问题。
So critical security skills are the ability to identify patterns, pattern recognition, data analytics,
where you analyze and enumerate networks, or you analyze and enumerate issues.

11173
18:47:35,022 --> 18:47:36,784
你会进行漏洞分析。
You do vulnerability analysis.

11174
18:47:36,864 --> 18:47:41,828
比如，你会使用 Nessus 这样的工具，或者我最喜欢的 OpenVAS，也就是 OpenVAS。
So you use a tool like Nessus, for example, or my favorite Open VAS, OpenVOS.

11175
18:47:42,318 --> 18:47:47,460
嗯，有很多各种工具可以用来进行漏洞分析和渗透测试。
Um there are various tools that you can do to conduct vulnerability analysis and pen tests.

11176
18:47:48,064 --> 18:47:50,304
然后这就是威胁狩猎发挥作用的地方。
And then this is where threat hunting comes in.

11177
18:47:50,414 --> 18:47:54,660
这就是你将 Red Team 渗透测试与 Blue Team 分析结合在一起的地方。
It's where you're combining red team pen testing with blue team analytics.

11178
18:47:54,864 --> 18:47:56,196
这就会让你成为一名威胁猎人。
That makes you a threat hunter.

11179
18:47:56,782 --> 18:47:58,624
这里面包含一点数据取证。
There's a little bit of data forensics there.

11180
18:47:58,704 --> 18:48:03,588
你不会成为数据取证专家，但你确实需要查看文件内部。
You don't become a data forensics specialist, but you do take a look inside of files.

11181
18:48:03,982 --> 18:48:07,104
例如，Netstat 命令，我就拿这个作为例子。
For example, the Netstat command, I'll just use that as an example.

11182
18:48:07,374 --> 18:48:16,384
Linux 系统上的木马经常会接管该命令和其他命令，
看起来它们运行正常，但实际上它们正在破坏安全。
A Trojan on a Linux system will often take over that command and others where
it looks like it's behaving normally, but it's actually compromising security.

11183
18:48:16,464 --> 18:48:23,744
它里面包含一个木马，可能是一个非法服务器，允
许黑客进入并攻击特定系统，然后接管并窃取数据。
It has a Trojan in it, might be an illicit server that allows hackers to
come in and attack a particular system and take it over and steal data.

11184
18:48:24,078 --> 18:48:32,676
这些就是你需要在 Linux 上，不只是在 Linux 系
统上，而且是在你的网络上能够执行的取证示例。
These are examples of the kind of forensics that you're going to need to
be able to do on a Linux, not on a Linux system, but on your networks.

11185
18:48:33,550 --> 18:48:37,604
所以你会深入了解你的环境中系统是如何协同工作的。
So you get a deep understanding of how systems work together in your environment.

11186
18:48:38,414 --> 18:48:42,084
这不是理论上的理解，它必须是基于你自己的公司的实践。
this is not a theoretical understanding, it has to be practical based on your own company.

11187
18:48:42,862 --> 18:48:45,892
例如，会计和人力资源部门。
So, for example, accounting and human resources.

11188
18:48:46,190 --> 18:48:50,948
你基本上要查看他们在做什么，它是如何运作的，以及可能会出什么问题。
You basically look into what they're doing and how it's working and what could go wrong.

11189
18:48:51,584 --> 18:49:05,412
你会查看安装的系统，特别是 SCADA 系统，这是让自动化系
统（例如工厂生产线上的机器人）能够协同工作的技术之一。
you look at installed systems, especially SCADA systems, which are one of the technologies that makes it possible for automated
systems like robots, for example, that are on a factory line to work together.

11190
18:49:06,064 --> 18:49:09,904
所以你要理解你的业务流程是如何运作的。
So you you you understand how the process of your business works.

11191
18:49:09,984 --> 18:49:13,104
你也要带来你自己的专业贡献。
And you also bring something to the table yourself.

11192
18:49:13,358 --> 18:49:15,556
你需要了解如何处理事件。
You need to understand how to resolve incidents.

11193
18:49:15,664 --> 18:49:19,984
你需要了解如何去观察，就像我说的，去观察问题的拐角。
You need to understand how to look what I say, look around the corner of a problem.

11194
18:49:20,144 --> 18:49:26,864
换句话说，你看一个情况，然后你会说，嗯，我能预见到明天那里会变成一个问题。
In other words, you look at a situation and you say, hmm, tomorrow I can see where that's going to become a problem.

11195
18:49:27,024 --> 18:49:30,948
如果你所在的团队已经有现成的 Blue Team 或 Red Team，你也可以协助他们工作。
And you assist teams if there are already existing blue teams or red teams.

11196
18:49:31,424 --> 18:49:35,984
我接触过很多小企业，那里可能只有一两个人，需要身兼数职。
I work with a lot of small businesses where it's one or two people wear a lot of different hats.

11197
18:49:36,144 --> 18:49:47,104
一两个人有时得当渗透测试人员，有时又得当分析
师，有时甚至得独自承担整个安全运营中心的工作。
One or two people have to sometimes become the pen testers, sometimes the other that same person has to become the analyst,
sometimes that person is a one person security operations center.

11198
18:49:47,264 --> 18:49:50,052
如果你在大型公司工作，那显然会有不同的团队。
If you work for a larger company, then obviously you have different teams.

11199
18:49:50,816 --> 18:49:56,132
但核心逻辑是，你要学会与团队协作并提供支持，以帮助提升安全性。
But it's the understanding that you coordinate and assist with teams to help improve security.

11200
18:49:56,576 --> 18:49:59,076
所以，威胁猎人默认你已经被黑客入侵了。
So a threat hunter already assumes you've been hacked.

11201
18:49:59,536 --> 18:50:03,936
它把网络视为狩猎场，并想要获取整个环境的全貌。
It sees the network as a hunting ground and it wants a picture of the whole environment.

11202
18:50:04,334 --> 18:50:07,456
威胁猎人并不相信现有的安全措施就足够了。
A threat hunter does not believe that security is good enough.

11203
18:50:07,662 --> 18:50:09,124
这是我们做的一项小调查。
This is a little survey we did.

11204
18:50:09,454 --> 18:50:12,836
有很多 IT 工作人员会想，嘿，我们搞定了，现在很安全。
There are a lot of IT workers out there who kind of think, hey, we're done, we're fine.

11205
18:50:13,376 --> 18:50:13,936
其实不然。
You're not.

11206
18:50:14,126 --> 18:50:16,256
如果你有这种态度，那你可能就麻烦了。
If you have that attitude, you're probably in trouble.

11207
18:50:16,686 --> 18:50:20,336
所以你必须采取这种观察、定位并做出决定的做法。
So you have to take along this observe and orient yourself and decide.

11208
18:50:20,496 --> 18:50:31,940
基本上，你必须采取这种不断思考、观察和定位的方法，
判断哪些有效、哪些无效，然后采取行动来运用你的技能。
You have to take this basically approach where you're constantly thinking, observing and orienting yourself,
and you decide what's working and what's not, and then you take actions to apply skills.

11209
18:50:32,176 --> 18:50:35,396
你必须非常清楚你所处的环境。
You have to be very aware of your world.

11210
18:50:35,616 --> 18:50:41,456
呃，我不知道你们屏幕的分辨率能不能看清，但这些潜水员对周围环境缺乏警觉。
Uh, this is I don't know if you can see this through the resolution on your screen,
but these scuba divers are not situationally aware.

11211
18:50:41,536 --> 18:50:44,336
他们说，嘿，一切都很棒，但你看到他们身后是什么了吗？
They're saying, hey, everything's great, and do you see what's behind them?

11212
18:50:44,816 --> 18:50:46,372
一只非常、非常大的鲨鱼。
a very, very large shark.

11213
18:50:46,894 --> 18:50:48,976
这可能是 Photoshop 处理过的，没关系。
This could be Photoshop, doesn't matter.

11214
18:50:49,216 --> 18:50:54,340
重点是，作为一名 IT 工作者，你对周围环境警觉吗？
The point is, as you are an IT worker, are you situationally aware?

11215
18:50:54,766 --> 18:51:02,660
你对风险的管理是否达到了你认为一切安全的状态，
还是说深海中其实潜伏着巨大的黑客或巨大的鲨鱼？
Have you managed your risk to where you think everything's fine and you really are,
or is there a big hacker or a big shark behind you lurking in the deep?

11216
18:51:03,438 --> 18:51:08,004
所以你必须找到上下文并理解你的业务运营。
So you have to find the context and understand your operations.

11217
18:51:08,336 --> 18:51:10,372
因此，你要参与威胁情报工作。
And so you engage in threat intelligence.

11218
18:51:10,496 --> 18:51:23,876
简单来说，就是你要去调查你网络中的系统，找出最明显的——我不说“明显”这个词——找出最危险
的威胁，以及你该如何应对它们。
That simply means, in a sense, you go out there and find out for the systems you have in your network,
what are the most obvious I won't say the word obvious, what are the most dangerous threats and how can you counter them?

11219
18:51:24,896 --> 18:51:27,556
通过应对这些威胁，你可以应用安全控制。
And by countering them, you can apply controls.

11220
18:51:28,016 --> 18:51:39,172
或者你可以说，我们要买网络保险，所以基本上你可以说，我们认为那件事会发生，
我接受那个责任，并把它转交给保险公司。
Or you can say, Well, we're going to do cyber insurance instead of um so you can basically say, Well,
we think that's gonna be that's gonna happen, and I'll take that liability and I'll defer it to insurance.

11221
18:51:39,376 --> 18:51:45,476
或者如果那里存在责任或问题，我们将实施安全控制来降低那个风险。
Or if there's a liability or a problem there, we're going to implement a security control to make that risk go down.

11222
18:51:45,696 --> 18:51:48,292
你可以参与行为分析。
You can engage in behavioral analytics.

11223
18:51:49,006 --> 18:51:56,416
这些年来我们注意到，我交流过的所有人都发现，终端
用户显然是主要的，或者说，他们是主要的攻击目标。
We have noticed over the years, all the people that I talk with, that
end users obviously are a major if well, they're the major target.

11224
18:51:56,878 --> 18:52:06,256
所以你需要在公司中开展用户行为分析，以确保能够识别出攻击最常从哪里发起。
So you need to engage in user behavior analytics in your company to
make sure that to identify where those attacks are coming in the most.

11225
18:52:06,382 --> 18:52:14,016
然后你可以对用户进行教育，改变业务流程，从而降低问题，降低风险。
And then you can educate users, you can change processes, business processes, so that that problem is lowered, that risk is lowered.

11226
18:52:14,382 --> 18:52:24,896
所以你要利用有根据的直觉，并保持一种天生的好奇心，因为你不想再次被坑，
不想有人像「抢镜」一样突然出现在你身后。
So you use informed hunches and you get you have an innate sense of curiosity because you don't want to get again,
you don't want to have somebody come up behind you like a photo bomb.

11227
18:52:24,976 --> 18:52:28,336
这是一个术语，指有人闯入你的照片并在你身后做点什么。
That's a term where somebody gets into your picture and does something behind your back.

11228
18:52:28,416 --> 18:52:30,416
你肯定不想在黑客攻击的层面上发生这种情况。
You don't want to have that happen in a hacker sense.

11229
18:52:30,576 --> 18:52:31,524
再举个例子。
Here's another example.

11230
18:52:32,942 --> 18:52:36,336
有几个足球运动员在拍照，英国女王突然出现在他们身后抢镜。
a couple of footballers were taking a picture and the Queen of England photo bomb them.

11231
18:52:36,496 --> 18:52:37,028
我觉得这是一个很好的例子。
I think that's a good.

11232
18:52:38,816 --> 18:52:46,496
当你参与威胁狩猎时，基本上会接触到一些有趣的术语。
As you engage in threat hunting, you basically engage in some interesting terminology.

11233
18:52:46,670 --> 18:52:49,156
客户是攻击的受益人。
The customer is the beneficiary of the attack.

11234
18:52:49,774 --> 18:52:57,776
如果你的公司正遭受攻击，而且有人想要让攻击发生，那个客户可能甚至不是技术人员。
If there's an attack going on on your company and somebody wants it
to happen, that customer might be somebody who's not even technical.

11235
18:52:57,936 --> 18:53:01,220
他们可能会雇佣一群人来攻击你的公司。
They might employ a gang of people to attack your company.

11236
18:53:02,094 --> 18:53:03,776
所以对手就是操作者。
So the adversary is the operator.

11237
18:53:03,936 --> 18:53:07,936
那个人可能是内部员工，一个不满的、不高兴的内部员工。
That person could be an internal worker, a disgruntled, unhappy internal worker.

11238
18:53:08,096 --> 18:53:10,308
也可能是外部的一群人。
It could be a gang of outside workers.

11239
18:53:11,054 --> 18:53:20,228
所以他们要做的是，他们将使用某种形式的基础设施，可能是你们公司自己的基础设施，
或者他们自己的基础设施来发动攻击。
And so what they're going to do is they're going to use some form of infrastructure, maybe your own company infrastructure,
they're going to use their own to wage the attack.

11240
18:53:20,462 --> 18:53:26,016
然后他们将使用某种能力，也就是一些工具来发动攻击。
Then they are going to use a capability, some tools to wage the attack.

11241
18:53:26,414 --> 18:53:28,452
然后还有受害者，也就是你。
And then there's a victim that would be you.

11242
18:53:28,782 --> 18:53:31,376
所以那个客户就是攻击的受益人。
So that customer is the beneficiary of the attack.

11243
18:53:31,456 --> 18:53:34,500
受益人可能和对手是同一个人，但通常他们是分开的。
It might be the same as the adversary, but oftentimes they're separate.

11244
18:53:34,830 --> 18:53:38,628
这些都是威胁狩猎概念中使用的术语。
These are the kinds of terms that are used in the concept of threat hunting.

11245
18:53:39,246 --> 18:53:44,096
有些公司在威胁狩猎方面的成熟度比其他公司更高。
There are companies that are more mature than others in threat hunting.

11246
18:53:45,056 --> 18:53:49,456
这是我从 SANS 那里借鉴过来的。
this is something I I stole from uh I use from uh SANS.

11247
18:53:49,696 --> 18:53:52,452
他们有一些关于什么是威胁狩猎的非常好的文章。
They have some very good articles about what threat hunting is.

11248
18:53:52,816 --> 18:53:55,216
SANS 是一个安全组织。
SANS is a security organization.

11249
18:53:55,616 --> 18:54:00,644
他们基本上把等级从 0 一直划分到 4。
And they basically put together levels from zero all the way to four.

11250
18:54:01,296 --> 18:54:04,996
我认为大多数公司还在 0 或 1 级别。
I would argue that most companies are at the zero or one level.

11251
18:54:05,296 --> 18:54:09,156
如果你运气真的很好，你可能处于 HMM2 流程级别。
If you're really lucky, you might be at the HMM2 procedural level.

11252
18:54:09,806 --> 18:54:10,096
好吗？
Okay?

11253
18:54:10,656 --> 18:54:17,412
嗯，大多数公司只要有自动警报就很开心了，而且大多数公司其实并没有太多的常规流程。
Um most companies are happy if they have automated alerting, uh, and most companies really don't have much of a routine.

11254
18:54:17,550 --> 18:54:21,732
而且我认为越来越多的公司正在达到 HMM1 级别，对吧？
And I I would argue that more and more companies are getting up to HMM1, right?

11255
18:54:21,936 --> 18:54:26,212
他们加入了一点威胁情报，并且有一点常规流程。
Where they incorporate a little bit of threat intelligence and they have a little bit of routine.

11256
18:54:26,896 --> 18:54:29,892
目标是尽可能达到更高的水平，但这成本非常高。
the goal is to get as high as possible, but it's very costly.

11257
18:54:30,606 --> 18:54:30,896
好吗？
Okay?

11258
18:54:32,590 --> 18:54:34,244
所以这就是威胁狩猎成熟度模型。
so it's the hunting maturity model.

11259
18:54:34,510 --> 18:54:48,868
各位，核心思想基本上是建立架构，从被动防御转向主动防
御，并获得获取情报的能力，以及针对黑客采取进攻能力。
And the whole idea, folks, is that you basically move To create an architecture and move from a passive defense to an active defense,
and the ability to gain intelligence and take on an offensive capability against the hackers.

11260
18:54:49,536 --> 18:54:52,256
各位，目前有各种类型的威胁狩猎。
There are various types of threat hunting out there, folks.

11261
18:54:52,416 --> 18:55:04,964
以用户为中心，也就是查看人员的工作职责，然后你会发现，职责越重要，
遭受攻击的可能性就越大，或者成功的攻击就越可能让公司倒闭。
User-centered, which is where you look at the job responsibility of people, then you see, well, the more important the responsibility,
the more likely that there's an attack, or the more likely that a successful attack could bring the company down.

11262
18:55:05,230 --> 18:55:11,300
所以你专注于有问题的用户或有问题的进程，专注于用户，然后尝试解决问题。
So you focus on problem users or problem processes, focused on users, and then you try to solve the problem.

11263
18:55:11,536 --> 18:55:14,052
另一种做法是专注于能力。
The other way to do it is you focus on capability.

11264
18:55:14,574 --> 18:55:16,176
系统的业务功能是什么？
What's the business function of a system?

11265
18:55:16,336 --> 18:55:18,496
它的业务用途是什么，然后你尝试去解决它？
What's the business use and then you try to solve it?

11266
18:55:18,670 --> 18:55:21,348
还有基础设施，也就是你专注于设备。
There's infrastructure where you focus on the equipment.

11267
18:55:21,696 --> 18:55:24,420
我发现能力和用户一样，也非常有用。
I find capability is very useful as well as user.

11268
18:55:25,136 --> 18:55:35,856
呃，选择这三种方法中的任何一种——用户、能力或基础设施——都有各种原因，
但我发现以用户为中心在很多时候是最有用的。
Uh and there are various reasons why you would approach any one of these three, user capability or infrastructure,
but I find that the user-centered is the most useful at many times.

11269
18:55:35,950 --> 18:55:38,980
我的时间快到了，所以我打算稍微快点过一下这里。
I'm running out of time, so I'm gonna move on here a little bit.

11270
18:55:39,438 --> 18:55:40,656
黑客在追求什么？
What are the hackers after?

11271
18:55:40,816 --> 18:55:42,020
嗯，这取决于你的公司。
Well, it depends on your company.

11272
18:55:42,736 --> 18:55:43,056
对吧？
Right?

11273
18:55:43,216 --> 18:55:50,016
如果你的公司专注于某些有价值的东西，他们就会去攻击那个，
或者至少是支持那个有价值东西的进程。
If your company is focusing on a certain thing of value, they're gonna go after that,
or at least the processes that support that thing of value.

11274
