Now that we have a basic understanding of cybersecurity, let's dive deeper into the unique cybersecurity challenges faced by
healthcare organizations, understanding the threat landscape, unique cybersecurity challenges in healthcare.

12727
21:29:49,774 --> 21:29:57,232
由于医疗机构处理的数据具有敏感性和机密性，它们面临着一套独特的网络安全挑战。
Healthcare organizations face a unique set of cybersecurity challenges
due to the sensitive and confidential nature of the data they handle.

12728
21:29:57,486 --> 21:30:05,392
与传统行业不同，医疗行业在严格的监管下运行，要求对患者信息提供最高的隐私保护和安全性。
Unlike traditional industries, healthcare operates under strict regulations
which demand the utmost privacy and security for patient information.

12729
21:30:05,710 --> 21:30:12,432
医疗机构面临的挑战包括但不限于 IT 基础设施日益增长的复杂性。
The challenges healthcare organizations face include, but are not limited to, rising complexity of IT infrastructure.

12730
21:30:12,718 --> 21:30:23,712
医疗设施拥有复杂的 IT 基础设施，集成了众多系统，
包括电子健康档案、EHR、医院管理系统和联网医疗设备。
Healthcare facilities have complex IT infrastructures that integrate numerous systems, including electronic health records, EHR,
hospital management systems, and connected medical devices.

12731
21:30:23,982 --> 21:30:29,632
这种复杂性往往会导致漏洞，以及 IoT 和医疗设备的集成。
This complexity often leads to vulnerabilities, integration of IoT and medical devices.

12732
21:30:29,872 --> 21:30:39,632
物联网设备（如智能输液泵、可穿戴设备和其他联
网医疗设备）的日益普及，增加了更多的攻击面。
The growing adoption of Internet of Things devices, such as smart infusion pumps,
wearables, and other connected medical equipment, adds more attack surfaces.

12733
21:30:39,872 --> 21:30:46,352
这些设备往往缺乏其他领域中常见的强大安全协议，使它们容易受到漏洞利用。
These devices often lack the robust security protocols found in other sectors, making them vulnerable to exploitation.

12734
21:30:46,702 --> 21:30:49,072
多样化的利益相关者和访问点。
Diverse stakeholders and access points.

12735
21:30:49,358 --> 21:30:57,232
医疗生态系统涉及多个利益相关者，如医疗提供者、保险公司、供应商和监管机构。
Healthcare ecosystems involve multiple stakeholders, such as healthcare providers, insurers, vendors, and regulatory bodies.

12736
21:30:57,472 --> 21:31:03,552
这导致敏感数据存在多个访问点，增加了未经授权的访问风险。
This results in several access points to sensitive data, increasing the risks of unauthorized access.

12737
21:31:04,048 --> 21:31:06,288
遗留系统和补丁管理。
Legacy systems and patch management.

12738
21:31:06,528 --> 21:31:13,728
许多医疗机构仍在使用遗留系统，这些系统可能无法获得定期的安全更新或补丁。
Many healthcare organizations still operate legacy systems that may not receive regular security updates or patches.

12739
21:31:13,998 --> 21:31:19,428
这些过时的系统通常存在已知漏洞，网络犯罪分子可以利用这些漏洞。
These outdated systems often have known vulnerabilities, which cyber criminals can exploit.

12740
21:31:19,888 --> 21:31:21,168
运营压力。
Operational pressure.

12741
21:31:21,454 --> 21:31:25,168
医疗专业人员往往面临提供服务的压力。
Healthcare professionals are often under time pressure to provide care.

12742
21:31:25,408 --> 21:31:32,768
这可能导致安全协议被绕过，尤其是在高压环境下需要做出紧急决策时。
This can lead to security protocols being bypassed, particularly when urgent decisions need to be made in high stress environments.

12743
21:31:33,102 --> 21:31:41,568
既然我们了解了医疗机构面临的挑战，现在让我们继
续探讨医疗数据的类型及其对网络犯罪分子的价值。
Now that we understand the challenges healthcare organizations face, let's move
forward and explore the types of healthcare data and their value to cybercriminals.

12744
21:31:41,838 --> 21:31:45,008
医疗数据的类型及其对网络犯罪分子的价值。
Types of healthcare data and their value to cybercriminals.

12745
21:31:45,262 --> 21:31:54,288
医疗数据是网络犯罪分子的重要目标，因为它包含关键的个人信息，可用于各种恶意目的。
Healthcare data is a valuable target for cybercriminals because it contains
critical personal information that can be used for a variety of malicious purposes.

12746
21:31:54,542 --> 21:31:58,768
让我们讨论一些主要的医疗数据类型以及它们对攻击者的吸引力。
Let's discuss some key types of healthcare data and their appeal to attackers.

12747
21:31:59,088 --> 21:32:01,648
电子健康档案，EHR。
Electronic health records, EHR.

12748
21:32:01,888 --> 21:32:08,928
这些记录包含敏感的患者信息，包括病史、诊断、治疗方案和处方。
These records contain sensitive patient information, including medical history, diagnoses, treatments, and prescriptions.

12749
21:32:09,230 --> 21:32:14,368
EHR 可以被用于身份盗窃、保险欺诈，或者在黑市上出售。
EHRs can be used for identity theft, insurance fraud, or sold on the black market.

12750
21:32:14,688 --> 21:32:22,368
财务信息、账单信息、保险详情和支付记录对于从事欺诈活动的网络犯罪分子来说至关重要。
Financial information, billing information, insurance details, and payment history are critical for cybercriminals engaging in fraud.

12751
21:32:22,608 --> 21:32:26,528
这些数据可以被利用来盗取患者或保险公司的钱。
This data can be exploited to steal money from patients or insurers.

12752
21:32:26,768 --> 21:32:28,048
医疗设备数据。
Medical device data.

12753
21:32:28,302 --> 21:32:35,248
联网的医疗设备会产生持续的数据流，这些数据可能被劫持或篡改来伤害患者。
Connected medical devices generate continuous streams of data that can be hijacked or manipulated to harm patients.

12754
21:32:35,502 --> 21:32:40,448
攻击者可以利用这些数据进行勒索软件攻击，或者篡改医疗方案。
Attackers can leverage this data for ransomware attacks or tampering with medical treatments.

12755
21:32:40,688 --> 21:32:43,328
个人健康信息，PHI。
Personal health information, PHI.

12756
21:32:43,568 --> 21:32:54,448
除了临床记录，PHI 还包括任何与健康相关的个人身
份信息，PII，例如社会安全号码、地址和电话号码。
Beyond clinical records, PHI includes any personally identifiable information, PII, related to health,
such as social security numbers, addresses, and phone numbers.

12757
21:32:54,608 --> 21:32:58,448
这些信息可被用于身份盗窃、欺诈甚至勒索。
This can be used for identity theft, fraud, or even extortion.

12758
21:32:58,688 --> 21:32:59,808
基因组数据。
Genomic data.

12759
21:32:59,982 --> 21:33:04,928
随着个性化医疗的兴起，基因数据变得越来越有价值。
With the rise of personalized medicine, genetic data has become increasingly valuable.

12760
21:33:05,168 --> 21:33:11,488
这些数据可被用来利用保险政策中的漏洞，或用于生物技术勒索。
This data can be used to exploit vulnerabilities in insurance policies or for biotechnological blackmail.

12761
21:33:11,694 --> 21:33:17,088
由于医疗数据的敏感性，近些年针对这些数据的黑市交易呈爆炸式增长。
Due to the sensitive nature of healthcare data, the black market for it has exploded in recent years.

12762
21:33:17,328 --> 21:33:21,968
这反过来使得医疗机构成为了网络攻击的首要目标。
This in turn has made healthcare organizations prime targets for cyber attacks.

12763
21:33:22,254 --> 21:33:30,368
既然我们已经审查了面临风险的数据类型，现在让
我们继续探讨医疗机构面临的一些常见威胁和漏洞。
Now that we've examined the types of data at risk, let's move forward and explore
some of the common threats and vulnerabilities healthcare organizations face.

12764
21:33:30,670 --> 21:33:32,528
常见威胁和漏洞。
Common threats and vulnerabilities.

12765
21:33:32,814 --> 21:33:37,008
医疗系统经常受到各种类型的网络威胁的攻击。
Healthcare systems are frequently attacked by various types of cyber threats.

12766
21:33:37,198 --> 21:33:39,248
这里有一些最常见的威胁。
There are some of the most common threats.

12767
21:33:39,488 --> 21:33:41,248
第一个是勒索软件。
The first one is ransomware.

12768
21:33:41,408 --> 21:33:46,528
这类恶意软件会锁定关键系统的访问权限，并要求支付费用以解锁。
This type of malware locks access to critical systems and demands payment for their release.

12769
21:33:46,798 --> 21:33:54,980
医疗机构经常成为目标，因为它们无法承受运营中的停机时间，比如患者护理或访问 EHR。
Healthcare organizations are often targeted because they cannot afford downtime in operations, such as patient care or access to EHRs.

12770
21:33:55,342 --> 21:33:56,448
内部威胁。
Insider threats.

12771
21:33:56,654 --> 21:34:06,368
医疗机构不仅面临外部黑客的风险，还面临内部人员的风
险，包括拥有敏感数据访问权限的员工、承包商或供应商。
Healthcare organizations are at risk not only from external hackers, but also
from insiders, employees, contractors, or vendors with access to sensitive data.

12772
21:34:06,638 --> 21:34:11,808
内部威胁可能是故意造成的，也可能是意外发生的，但它们通常是最难检测到的。
Insider threats can be intentional or accidental, but they are often the hardest to detect.

12773
21:34:12,110 --> 21:34:13,888
网络钓鱼和社会工程学。
Phishing and social engineering.

12774
21:34:14,128 --> 21:34:23,568
攻击者经常欺骗医疗机构员工去点击恶意链接或泄露敏感信息，
这些信息随后可被用于获取系统的未经授权的访问。
Attackers often trick healthcare employees into clicking malicious links or revealing sensitive information,
which can then be used to gain unauthorized access to systems.

12775
21:34:23,854 --> 21:34:24,848
数据泄露。
Data breaches.

12776
21:34:25,070 --> 21:34:33,648
网络犯罪分子可以利用医疗系统中的漏洞来窃取大
量的个人健康信息，这些信息经常在黑市上出售。
Cybercriminals can exploit vulnerabilities in healthcare systems to steal vast
amounts of personal health information, which is often sold on the black market.

12777
21:34:33,934 --> 21:34:39,008
这些泄露可能会损害医疗机构的声誉，并导致高额罚款。
These breaches can damage a healthcare organization's reputation and lead to costly fines.

12778
21:34:39,248 --> 21:34:45,648
分布式拒绝服务，也就是 DDoS 攻击，会压垮服务器，导致其无法访问。
Distributed denial of service, DDoS, attacks overwhelm servers, causing them to become inaccessible.

12779
21:34:45,902 --> 21:34:53,648
虽然这些攻击通常用于中断服务，但攻击者也可能
利用 DDoS 攻击作为掩护，同时进行其他恶意活动。
While these are typically used to disrupt services, attackers may use
DDoS attacks as a diversion while conducting other malicious activities.

12780
21:34:53,968 --> 21:34:55,808
医疗设备漏洞。
Medical device vulnerabilities.

12781
21:34:56,048 --> 21:35:03,408
许多联网的医疗设备存在固有漏洞，例如未加密的通信或薄弱的身份验证方法。
Many connected medical devices have inherent vulnerabilities, such as unencrypted communications or weak authentication methods.

12782
21:35:03,662 --> 21:35:08,528
这些漏洞可以被利用来操纵设备功能或窃取数据。
These vulnerabilities can be exploited to manipulate device functionality or steal data.

12783
21:35:08,814 --> 21:35:16,048
既然我们已经涵盖了常见的威胁，现在让我们继续前
进，回顾一些近期备受关注的医疗网络攻击及其影响。
Now that we've covered the common threats, let's move forward and review
some of the recent high-profile healthcare cyberattacks and their impacts.

12784
21:35:16,368 --> 21:35:20,208
近期备受关注的医疗网络攻击及其影响。
Recent high-profile healthcare cyberattacks and their impact.

12785
21:35:20,462 --> 21:35:26,848
近期的重大网络攻击凸显了医疗领域对强大网络安全能力的迫切需求。
Recent high-profile cyberattacks have underscored the critical need for robust cybersecurity in healthcare.

12786
21:35:27,008 --> 21:35:37,808
2017 年的 WannaCry 勒索软件攻击，这次攻击影响了分布
在 150 个国家的 20 多万台电脑，其中包括许多医疗机构。
The WannaCry ransomware attack, 2017, this attack affected more than 200,000
computers across 150 countries, including many healthcare institutions.

12787
21:35:38,094 --> 21:35:45,968
英国的国家医疗服务体系 NHS 受到了严重影响，一些医院被迫取消手术和预约。
The UK's National Health Service, NHS, was severely impacted, with some hospitals forced to cancel surgeries and appointments.

12788
21:35:46,254 --> 21:35:51,248
WannaCry 攻击利用了 Windows 操作系统的未修复的漏洞。
The WannaCry attack exploited unpatched vulnerabilities in Windows operating systems.

12789
21:35:51,790 --> 21:35:57,392
2018 年 Lab Corp 数据泄露，它是 U.S. 最大的实验室检测公司之一。
The Lab Corp Data Breach, 2018, one of the largest laboratory testing companies in the U.S.

12790
21:35:57,712 --> 21:36:03,152
遭受了数据泄露，导致超过 770 万人的个人数据遭到泄露。
suffered a data breach, compromising the personal data of over 7.7 million individuals.

12791
21:36:03,406 --> 21:36:09,220
这次泄露涉及对敏感患者信息的未经授权的访问，包括实验室检测结果。
This breach involved unauthorized access to sensitive patient information, including lab test results.

12792
21:36:09,614 --> 21:36:20,592
2020 年的 Universal Health Services 攻击，一起重大的勒索软件攻击袭击了 Universal
Health Services，简称 UHS，导致其医疗业务在全国范围内陷入中断。
The Universal Health Services Attack, 2020, a significant ransomware attack hit Universal Health Services, UHS,
causing a nationwide disruption to its healthcare operations.

12793
21:36:20,846 --> 21:36:26,992
这次攻击迫使医院退回到基于纸质的系统，延误了患者的护理，并危及生命。
The attack forced hospitals to revert to paper-based systems, delaying patient care and putting lives at risk.

12794
21:36:27,232 --> 21:36:36,352
这些事件展示了医疗网络攻击的广泛影响，它们可
能导致患者护理中断、经济损失以及损害公众信任。
These incidents demonstrate the widespread impact of healthcare cyberattacks, which
can cause disruptions to patient care, financial losses, and harm to public trust.

12795
21:36:36,622 --> 21:36:43,472
考虑到这些例子，了解监管医疗数据保护的法律和监管框架非常重要。
With these examples in mind, it's important to understand the legal and regulatory framework that governs healthcare data protection.

12796
21:36:43,662 --> 21:36:45,028
现在让我们深入了解一下。
Let's dive into that now.

12797
21:36:45,486 --> 21:36:47,392
法律和监管框架。
Legal and regulatory framework.

12798
21:36:47,726 --> 21:36:50,672
HIPAA，保护患者隐私和安全。
HIPAA, protecting patient privacy and security.

12799
21:36:50,912 --> 21:36:58,112
《健康保险流通和责任法案》，简称 HIPAA，是 United States 医疗数据保护的基石。
The Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act, HIPAA, is the cornerstone of healthcare data protection in the United States.

12800
21:36:58,350 --> 21:37:04,352
它为保护患者健康信息提供了严格的指南，重点关注隐私和安全。
It provides strict guidelines for the protection of patient health information focusing on privacy and security.

12801
21:37:04,592 --> 21:37:07,232
HIPAA 由几个关键组成部分组成。
HIPAA is comprised of several key components.

12802
21:37:07,502 --> 21:37:08,272
隐私规则。
Privacy Rule.

12803
21:37:08,592 --> 21:37:16,272
隐私规则规定了医疗保健提供者和其他实体如何处理受保护的健康信息 PHI 的标准。
The privacy rule establishes standards for how healthcare providers and other entities handle protected health information, PHI.

12804
21:37:16,526 --> 21:37:23,872
它为患者同意、健康信息共享，以及个人访问和修改其健康记录的权利制定了指南。
It sets guidelines for patient consent, the sharing of health information,
and the rights of individuals to access and amend their health records.

12805
21:37:24,142 --> 21:37:25,072
安全规则。
Security rule.

12806
21:37:25,312 --> 21:37:34,832
安全规则概述了医疗保健组织必须实施的技术、行政和物理防护措施，以保护电子 PHI，即 EPHI。
The security rule outlines the technical, administrative, and physical safeguards
healthcare organizations must implement to protect electronic PHI, EPHI.

12807
21:37:35,054 --> 21:37:44,388
它要求实体建立政策和流程，以防止未经授权的访
问，确保数据完整性，并提供安全的 e-PHI 访问。
It requires entities to establish policies and procedures to prevent
unauthorized access, ensure data integrity, and provide secure access to e-PHI.

12808
21:37:44,718 --> 21:37:46,192
泄露通知规则。
Breach notification rule.

12809
21:37:46,432 --> 21:37:59,952
泄露通知规则要求医疗保健组织在涉及未受保护的 PHI 发生数据泄露时，通知受影响的个人、
卫生与公众服务部 HHS，并在某些情况下通知媒体。
The breach notification rule mandates that healthcare organizations inform affected individuals,
the Department of Health and Human Services, HHS, and, in some cases, the media, if a breach occurs involving unsecured PHI.

12810
21:38:00,112 --> 21:38:05,348
这一规则对于确保医疗保健网络安全中的透明度和可追责性至关重要。
This rule is vital in ensuring transparency and accountability in healthcare cybersecurity.

12811
21:38:05,742 --> 21:38:11,952
医疗保健组织必须遵守 HIPAA 法规，以避免高昂的罚款和声誉损失。
Healthcare organizations must comply with HIPAA regulations to avoid costly penalties and reputational damage.

12812
21:38:12,174 --> 21:38:19,524
违反 HIPAA 可能导致每项违规处以 100 美元到 50,000 美元的罚款，具体取决于严重程度。
Violations of HIPAA can result in fines ranging from $100 to $50,000 per violation, depending on the severity.

12813
21:38:19,792 --> 21:38:24,032
深入了解 HIPAA 是必不可少的，但还有更多内容需要探索。
Having a solid understanding of HIPAA is essential, but there's more to explore.

12814
21:38:24,192 --> 21:38:28,164
现在让我们来看看 HITECH Act 以及它在医疗保健网络安全中的作用。
Let's now look at the Hightech Act and its role in healthcare cybersecurity.

12815
21:38:28,432 --> 21:38:30,512
HITECH Act，强化 HIPAA。
High Tech Act, strengthening HIPAA.

12816
21:38:31,022 --> 21:38:44,912
2009 年通过的《经济和临床健康健康信息技术法》，即 HITECH Act，
通过促进健康信息技术的应用，特别是采用电子健康记录 电子健康记录，来补充 HIPAA。
The Health Information Technology for Economic and Clinical Health, HITECH Act, passed in 2009,
complements HIPAA by promoting the use of health information technology, particularly the adoption of electronic health records, EHRs.

12817
21:38:45,166 --> 21:38:53,028
它强化了 HIPAA 的执行机制，确保医疗保健组织采取强有力的网络安全措施来保护 EPHI。
It strengthens HIPAA's enforcement mechanisms, ensuring that healthcare
organizations adopt robust cybersecurity measures to protect EPHI.

12818
21:38:53,422 --> 21:38:57,072
HITECH Act 的关键条款包括加强执法。
Key provisions of the HighTech Act include increased enforcement.

12819
21:38:57,326 --> 21:39:05,924
HITECH Act 加大了违反 HIPAA 的处罚，特别是对于未能及时处理安全泄露的医疗保健组织。
The HighTech Act increased penalties for non-compliance with HIPAA, particularly for
healthcare organizations that fail to address security breaches in a timely manner.

12820
21:39:06,286 --> 21:39:07,792
有意义的使用激励措施。
Meaningful use incentives.

12821
21:39:08,046 --> 21:39:14,672
HITECH Act 还为医疗保健提供者采用并有意义地使用 电子健康记录 提供财政激励。
The HighTech Act also provides financial incentives for healthcare providers to adopt and meaningfully use EHRs.

12822
21:39:14,862 --> 21:39:22,500
然而，这些激励措施与安全 IT 系统的实施挂钩，强调了对强有力网络安全措施的需求。
However, these incentives are tied to the implementation of secure IT systems, emphasizing the need for strong cybersecurity measures.

12823
21:39:22,752 --> 21:39:31,552
在了解了 HIPAA 和 HITECH 之后，了解其他有助于构建
全面医疗保健网络安全策略的相关法律和标准也很重要。
Having explored HIPAA and high-tech, it's important to understand other relevant laws
and standards that contribute to a comprehensive healthcare cybersecurity strategy.

12824
21:39:31,726 --> 21:39:32,832
现在让我们来看看这些。
Let's look at that now.

12825
21:39:33,072 --> 21:39:35,312
其他相关法律和标准。
Other relevant laws and standards.

12826
21:39:35,662 --> 21:39:42,192
除了 HIPAA 和 HITECH，还有其他几项法律和法规有助于管理医疗保健网络安全。
In addition to HIPAA and HITECH, several other laws and regulations help govern healthcare cybersecurity.

12827
21:39:42,478 --> 21:39:46,032
通用数据保护条例，GDPR。
The General Data Protection Regulation, GDPR.

12828
21:39:46,318 --> 21:39:54,672
这项欧盟法规为在欧盟内保护个人数据（包括医疗数据）提供了一个全面的框架。
This European Union regulation provides a comprehensive framework for the
protection of personal data, including healthcare data, within the EU.

12829
21:39:55,246 --> 21:40:03,908
处理欧盟公民数据的医疗保健组织必须遵守 GDPR 关于数据隐私和安全的严格要求。
Healthcare organizations dealing with EU citizens' data must comply with GDPR's strict requirements for data privacy and security.

12830
21:40:04,526 --> 21:40:09,424
联邦信息安全现代化法案，FISMA，这是 U.S. 的
The Federal Information Security Modernization Act, FISMA, this U.S.

12831
21:40:09,584 --> 21:40:16,704
法律适用于联邦机构及其承包商，包括为政府提供服务的医疗保健组织。
law applies to federal agencies and their contractors, including healthcare organizations that provide services to the government.

12832
21:40:17,166 --> 21:40:23,140
FISMA 要求机构实施信息安全计划以保护敏感数据。
FISMA requires agencies to implement information security programs to protect sensitive data.

12833
21:40:23,726 --> 21:40:29,060
美国国家标准技术研究院，NIST，网络安全框架。
The National Institute of Standards and Technology, NIST, Cybersecurity Framework.

12834
21:40:29,344 --> 21:40:35,300
这个框架提供了一套用于改善网络安全态势的最佳实践和指南。
This framework offers a set of best practices and guidelines for improving cybersecurity posture.

12835
21:40:35,694 --> 21:40:41,348
虽然不是强制性的，但它为医疗机构提供了一种实用的风险管理方法。
While not mandatory, it provides healthcare organizations with a practical approach to risk management.

12836
21:40:41,824 --> 21:40:52,132
既然监管要求已经讲过了，现在让我们继续深入探讨
指导医疗机构保护其系统和数据的核心网络安全原则。
With the regulatory landscape now covered, let's move on and dive into the core cybersecurity principles that guide healthcare
organizations in protecting their systems and data.

12837
21:40:52,782 --> 21:40:55,332
医疗领域的核心网络安全原则。
Core cybersecurity principles in healthcare.

12838
21:40:55,630 --> 21:41:00,548
CIA 三要素：机密性、完整性和可用性。
The CIA triad, confidentiality, integrity, and availability.

12839
21:41:01,102 --> 21:41:14,784
指导医疗网络安全工作的基本安全原则是基于 CIA 三要素的：
机密性，确保患者数据保持私密，且仅供授权人员访问。
The fundamental security principles that guide healthcare cybersecurity efforts are based on the CIA triad, confidentiality,
ensuring that patient data is kept private and only accessible to authorized individuals.

12840
21:41:15,024 --> 21:41:21,956
这包括使用加密、访问控制和强身份验证方法来保护敏感的健康信息。
This involves encryption, access controls, and strong authentication methods to protect sensitive health information.

12841
21:41:22,510 --> 21:41:26,704
完整性，维护患者数据的准确性和完整性。
Integrity, maintaining the accuracy and completeness of patient data.

12842
21:41:27,022 --> 21:41:36,356
医疗机构必须确保数据不会被未经授权的第三方篡
改，可以通过数据校验和审计追踪等措施来实现。
Healthcare organizations must ensure that data is not altered or tampered with
by unauthorized parties using measures like data validation and audit trails.

12843
21:41:36,814 --> 21:41:43,024
可用性，确保患者数据和系统在需要时可以访问，且不会中断。
Availability, ensuring that patient data and systems are accessible when needed, without disruptions.

12844
21:41:43,310 --> 21:41:51,364
这包括实施冗余系统、备份和灾难恢复计划，以防止可能影响患者护理的停机时间。
This involves implementing redundant systems, backups, and disaster recovery plans to prevent downtime, which can affect patient care.

12845
21:41:51,854 --> 21:41:59,104
在讨论了 CIA 三要素之后，医疗机构实施适当的风险管理策略至关重要。
Having discussed the CIA triad, it is crucial for healthcare organizations to implement proper risk management strategies.

12846
21:41:59,374 --> 21:42:03,504
现在让我们来探讨医疗环境下的风险评估和管理。
Let's now explore risk assessment and management in a healthcare context.

12847
21:42:03,822 --> 21:42:12,144
医疗机构必须定期评估和管理网络安全风险，以保护其资产并符合监管标准。
Healthcare organizations must regularly assess and manage cybersecurity
risks to protect their assets and comply with regulatory standards.

12848
21:42:12,494 --> 21:42:25,700
风险管理的关键组成部分包括风险识别，即识别潜在的网络安全风险，包括软件、
硬件或进程中可能被攻击者利用的漏洞。
Key components of risk management include risk identification, identifying potential cybersecurity risks,
including vulnerabilities in software, hardware, or processes that could be exploited by attackers.

12849
21:42:26,064 --> 21:42:34,692
风险分析，分析每种风险的可能性和潜在影响，并根据后果的严重程度来确定优先级。
Risk analysis, analyzing the likelihood and potential impact of each
risk, prioritizing them based on the severity of their consequences.

12850
21:42:35,024 --> 21:42:44,356
风险缓解，实施安全控制以最大限度地降低网络攻击的可能性，例如防火墙、加密和员工培训。
Risk mitigation, implementing security controls to minimize the likelihood
of a cyberattack, such as firewalls, encryption, and employee training.

12851
21:42:44,878 --> 21:42:53,184
事件响应，制定并测试事件响应计划，以便快速检测、遏制并从数据泄露中恢复。
Incident response, developing and testing incident response plans to quickly detect, contain, and recover from security breaches.

12852
21:42:53,454 --> 21:43:00,196
这确保了组织能够最大限度地减少攻击的影响，并符合数据泄露通知要求。
This ensures that organizations can minimize the impact of attacks and comply with breach notification requirements.

12853
21:43:00,750 --> 21:43:01,572
总结。
Conclusion.

12854
21:43:01,824 --> 21:43:13,156
医疗网络安全的基础是理解该行业面临的独特挑战，以及保护敏感患者数据的法律和监管框架。
The foundation of healthcare cybersecurity is built on understanding the unique challenges that the sector faces,
as well as the legal and regulatory frameworks that protect sensitive patient data.

12855
21:43:13,518 --> 21:43:26,384
通过遵循机密性、完整性和可用性等核心网络安全原则，医疗机构可以有效缓解风险，
并保护其系统免受新兴网络威胁的侵害。
By adhering to core cybersecurity principles like confidentiality, integrity, and availability,
healthcare organizations can effectively mitigate risks and safeguard their systems against emerging cyber threats.

12856
21:43:26,638 --> 21:43:40,464
随着医疗行业不断数字化，组织保持警惕、主动并致力于维护强大的网络安全态势至关重要，
以保护患者数据并维护医疗系统的完整性。
As healthcare continues to digitize, it is crucial for organizations to remain vigilant, proactive,
and committed to maintaining a strong cybersecurity posture to protect patient data and uphold the integrity of the healthcare system.

12857
21:43:40,750 --> 21:43:43,824
保障医疗技术和身份验证。
Securing healthcare technology and authentication.

12858
21:44:04,366 --> 21:44:19,268
在本模块中，我们将探讨用于保障医疗技术的关键策略和技术，重点是保护电子健康记录、
实施强身份验证机制以及医疗物联网，医疗物联网。
In this module, we will explore key strategies and technologies used to secure healthcare technology, focusing on protecting EHRs,
implementing strong authentication mechanisms, and the Internet of Medical Things, IOMT.

12859
21:44:19,790 --> 21:44:22,992
保护电子健康记录，电子健康记录。
Protecting electronic health records, EHRs.

12860
21:44:23,278 --> 21:44:29,232
电子健康记录，电子健康记录，是现代医疗系统的支柱。
EHRs, electronic health records, EHRs, are the backbone of modern healthcare systems.

12861
21:44:29,454 --> 21:44:34,192
它们包含对患者护理至关重要的敏感个人和医疗信息。
They contain sensitive personal and medical information that is vital for patient care.

12862
21:44:34,446 --> 21:44:41,792
随着医疗机构越来越多地依赖数字记录，保护这些数据免受网络威胁是至关重要的。
As healthcare organizations increasingly rely on digital records, it is essential to secure this data against cyber threats.

12863
21:44:42,030 --> 21:44:49,924
让我们首先看看保护 EHR 的主要方法，以及医疗机构必须采取的关键措施。
Let's begin by looking at the primary methods for protecting EHRs and the critical measures that healthcare institutions must adopt.

12864
21:44:50,382 --> 21:44:53,232
传输中和静态存储的数据加密。
Data encryption, in transit and at rest.

12865
21:44:53,806 --> 21:45:02,832
保护 EHR 最有效的方法之一就是数据加密，它能确保患者数据对未经授权的人员不可读。
One of the most effective ways to protect EHRs is through data encryption,
which ensures that patient data is unreadable to unauthorized individuals.

12866
21:45:03,118 --> 21:45:08,132
数据加密既可以应用于传输中的数据，也可以应用于静态存储的数据。
Data encryption can be applied both when data is in transit and when it is at rest.

12867
21:45:08,590 --> 21:45:15,872
在传输过程中，当患者数据在系统之间或跨网络传输时，很容易被拦截。
In transit, when patient data is being transmitted between systems or across networks, it is vulnerable to interception.

12868
21:45:16,238 --> 21:45:26,596
为了保护这些数据，医疗机构必须使用安全的通信
协议，如传输层安全协议 TLS 或安全套接层 SSL。
To protect this data, healthcare organizations must use secure communication
protocols like transport layer security, TLS, or secure socket layer, SSL.

12869
21:45:26,990 --> 21:45:36,272
这些加密方法确保数据在传输过程中保持加密，防止黑客在数据在系统间移动时访问敏感信息。
These encryption methods ensure that data remains encrypted during transmission, preventing hackers from accessing sensitive
information while it is moving between systems.

12870
21:45:36,590 --> 21:45:42,512
在静态存储时，存储在数据库或服务器上的 EHR 也容易受到攻击。
At rest, EHRs stored in databases or on servers are also vulnerable to attacks.

12871
21:45:42,766 --> 21:45:52,164
对于静态存储的数据，加密同样至关重要，它能确保即使攻
击者获得了存储系统的访问权限，也无法读取或篡改数据。
Encryption is equally essential for data at rest, ensuring that even if an
attacker gains access to storage systems, they cannot read or manipulate the data.

12872
21:45:52,526 --> 21:46:02,832
医疗机构应使用强大的加密算法，如高级加密标准 AES-256，来保护 EHR 免受未经授权的访问。
Healthcare organizations should use strong encryption algorithms like AES-256,
Advanced Encryption Standard, to protect EHRs from unauthorized access.

12873
21:46:03,150 --> 21:46:11,472
一旦 EHR 被加密，下一步的关键步骤就是确保数据得到安全备份，并在发生攻击时能够快速恢复。
Once EHRs are encrypted, the next key step is ensuring that the data
is backed up securely and can be restored quickly in case of an attack.

12874
21:46:11,758 --> 21:46:15,940
接下来让我们来看看安全数据备份和灾难恢复规划。
Let's explore secure data backup and disaster recovery planning next.

12875
21:46:16,462 --> 21:46:19,472
安全数据备份和灾难恢复规划。
Secure data backup and disaster recovery planning.

12876
21:46:19,726 --> 21:46:24,032
EHR 的完整性和可用性对于患者护理至关重要。
The integrity and availability of EHRs are crucial for patient care.

12877
21:46:24,334 --> 21:46:34,432
在发生网络攻击、自然灾害或系统故障时，医疗机构必须准
备好在没有重大停机时间或数据丢失的情况下恢复关键数据。
In the event of a cyber attack, natural disaster, or system failure, healthcare
organizations must be prepared to recover critical data without significant downtime or loss.

12878
21:46:34,734 --> 21:46:35,712
数据备份。
Data backup.

12879
21:46:35,886 --> 21:46:42,032
应定期对 EHR 进行备份，并安全地存储在异地或云端。
Regular backups of EHRs should be performed and stored securely in off-site locations or in the cloud.

12880
21:46:42,286 --> 21:46:48,996
这些备份必须经过加密，以确保即使原始数据被入侵，备份依然是安全的。
These backups must be encrypted to ensure that even if the original data is compromised, the backup remains secure.

12881
21:46:49,390 --> 21:46:50,912
灾难恢复规划。
Disaster recovery planning.

12882
21:46:51,214 --> 21:46:57,392
除了拥有安全的备份，医疗机构还必须制定全面的灾难恢复计划。
In addition to having secure backups, healthcare organizations must have a comprehensive disaster recovery plan.

12883
21:46:57,712 --> 21:47:05,872
该计划应概述在发生数据泄露或技术故障时，恢复 EHR 系统正常功能的步骤。
This plan should outline the steps to be taken to restore EHR systems
to normal functionality in the event of a breach or technical failure.

12884
21:47:06,190 --> 21:47:14,832
有效的灾难恢复规划可以最大限度地减少停机时间，
确保患者护理不中断，并保护敏感数据免受丢失。
Effective disaster recovery planning minimizes downtime, ensuring that patient
care is not interrupted and that sensitive data is protected from loss.

12885
21:47:15,086 --> 21:47:21,872
通过为 EHR 采取这些保护措施，医疗机构可以显著降低数据泄露的风险。
With these protective measures in place for EHRs, healthcare organizations can significantly reduce the risks of data breaches.

12886
21:47:22,094 --> 21:47:29,072
既然我们讨论了如何保护 EHR，现在让我们来看看验证用户身份的不同机制。
Now that we've discussed how to protect EHRs, let's move on to explore the different mechanisms for verifying user identity.

12887
21:47:29,390 --> 21:47:30,992
身份验证机制。
Authenticating mechanisms.

12888
21:47:31,232 --> 21:47:35,552
身份验证是保障医疗系统访问安全的关键环节。
Authentication is a critical aspect of securing access to healthcare systems.

12889
21:47:35,854 --> 21:47:45,560
通过在授予访问敏感数据或系统之前验证用户身份，医疗机构可以防止未经授权的访问，
并确保只有受信任的人员才能与 EHR 和医疗设备交互。
By verifying the identity of users before granting access to sensitive data or systems,
healthcare organizations can prevent unauthorized access and ensure that

12890
21:47:45,560 --> 21:47:49,712
通过在授予访问敏感数据或系统之前验证用户身份，医疗机构可以防止未经授权的访问，
并确保只有受信任的人员才能与 EHR 和医疗设备交互。
only trusted individuals can interact with EHRs and medical devices.

12891
21:47:50,030 --> 21:47:55,152
下面，我们将探讨医疗环境中常用的各种身份验证方法。
Below, we will explore various types of authentication methods commonly used in healthcare settings.

12892
21:47:55,584 --> 21:47:57,344
你知道的东西，也就是密码。
Something you know, passwords.

12893
21:47:57,614 --> 21:48:02,544
最基本的身份验证形式是用户已知的东西，通常是密码。
The most basic form of authentication is something the user knows, typically a password.

12894
21:48:02,798 --> 21:48:07,424
虽然密码是常见的身份验证方法，但它们也有一定的弱点。
While passwords are a common method of verifying identity, they have certain weaknesses.

12895
21:48:07,694 --> 21:48:12,292
让我们来看看一些加强密码政策并有效管理密码的策略。
Let's look at some strategies for strengthening password policies and managing them effectively.

12896
21:48:12,544 --> 21:48:13,824
密码复杂度。
Password complexity.

12897
21:48:14,062 --> 21:48:19,184
医疗机构应要求使用复杂的密码，让攻击者难以猜出。
Healthcare organizations should require complex passwords that are difficult for attackers to guess.

12898
21:48:19,438 --> 21:48:25,424
复杂密码应包含大小写字母、数字和特殊字符的组合。
Complex passwords should include a combination of upper and lower case letters, numbers, and special characters.

12899
21:48:25,710 --> 21:48:30,544
密码长度也很重要，通常至少需要 12 个字符。
It's important that passwords be sufficiently long, typically at least 12 characters.

12900
21:48:30,798 --> 21:48:31,904
密码管理。
Password management.

12901
21:48:32,174 --> 21:48:40,144
为了进一步增强安全性，医疗机构应实施密码管理工具，用于存储并自动生成强密码。
To further enhance security, healthcare organizations should implement password
management tools that store and automatically generate strong passwords.

12902
21:48:40,398 --> 21:48:44,772
这些工具可以帮助降低用户选择弱密码或重复使用密码的风险。
These tools can help reduce the risk of users choosing weak or reused passwords.

12903
21:48:45,024 --> 21:48:47,504
密码过期和更新。
Password expiration and renewal.

12904
21:48:47,744 --> 21:48:57,824
实施要求用户定期更改密码的政策，例如每 60 或
90 天更改一次，有助于限制被入侵密码的影响。
Implementing policies that require users to change their passwords periodically, e.g. every 60 or 90 days,
helps limit the impact of compromised passwords.

12905
21:48:57,998 --> 21:49:07,904
然而，必须平衡用户便利性，因为频繁更改可能导致糟糕的密码习惯，
比如使用简单或重复使用的密码。
However, it is essential to balance this with user convenience, as frequent
changes can lead to poor password practices, like using simple or reused passwords.

12906
21:49:08,174 --> 21:49:19,424
既然讨论了密码安全，现在让我们来看看你拥有的东西，物理令牌和多因素身份验证，MFA，
也就是你拥有的东西，FOB，MFA。
Now that we've discussed password security, let's explore something you own,
physical tokens and multi-factor authentication, MFA, something you own, FOB, MFA.

12907
21:49:19,726 --> 21:49:29,104
为了进一步增强安全性，医疗机构可以使用物理令
牌，例如 FOB 设备，并结合多因素身份验证，MFA。
To further enhance security, healthcare organizations can use physical
tokens, such as FOB devices, along with multi-factor authentication, MFA.

12908
21:49:29,424 --> 21:49:35,824
MFA 要求用户提供两种或多种验证形式来访问系统或数据。
MFA requires users to provide two or more forms of verification to access systems or data.

12909
21:49:36,064 --> 21:49:41,664
即使密码被入侵，这也能显著降低未经授权的访问风险。
This significantly reduces the risk of unauthorized access, even if a password is compromised.

12910
21:49:41,966 --> 21:49:50,464
FOB 令牌是物理设备，可生成有时效性的一次性密码，用户必须在输入密码的同时输入这些代码。
FOB tokens, these are physical devices that generate time-sensitive
one-time passcodes that users must enter along with their passwords.

12911
21:49:50,670 --> 21:49:57,824
它们作为额外的安全层，确保只有持有物理令牌的人才能访问系统。
They serve as an additional layer of security, ensuring that only individuals with the physical token can access the system.

12912
21:49:58,094 --> 21:50:00,624
多因素身份验证，MFA。
Multifactor authentication, MFA.

12913
21:50:00,910 --> 21:50:06,944
MFA 被广泛用于通过要求多种验证形式来加强身份验证。
MFA is widely used to strengthen authentication by requiring multiple forms of verification.

12914
21:50:07,184 --> 21:50:20,304
这可能包括用户知道的东西（密码）、用户拥有的东西（手机或 FOB 设备）以及用户本身的东西
（生物识别数据，如指纹识别或人脸识别）。
This may include a combination of something the user knows, a password, something the user has, a mobile phone or a FOB device,
something the user is, biometric data, like fingerprints or facial recognition.

12915
21:50:20,622 --> 21:50:27,104
通过实施 MFA，医疗机构可以显著降低未经授权的访问机会。
By implementing MFA, healthcare organizations significantly reduce the chances of unauthorized access.

12916
21:50:27,278 --> 21:50:34,224
接下来，让我们看看你本身的东西，生物识别身份验证方法，也就是你本身的东西，生物识别。
Next, let's explore something you are, biometric authentication methods, something you are, biometrics.

12917
21:50:34,414 --> 21:50:40,304
生物识别是一种基于每个个体独特的物理特征的身份验证形式。
Biometrics is a form of authentication based on physical characteristics unique to each individual.

12918
21:50:40,622 --> 21:50:47,424
在医疗领域，生物识别身份验证越来越多地用于加强访问控制并改善患者护理。
In healthcare, biometric authentication is increasingly used to enhance access control and improve patient care.

12919
21:50:47,662 --> 21:50:51,104
常见的生物识别方法包括指纹识别。
Common biometric methods include fingerprint recognition.

12920
21:50:51,438 --> 21:50:57,584
指纹扫描仪常用于医疗环境，提供快速且安全的系统和数据访问。
Fingerprint scanners are commonly used in healthcare settings, providing quick and secure access to systems and data.

12921
21:50:57,934 --> 21:51:02,784
指纹是每个人的独特特征，很难被复制或伪造。
Fingerprints are unique to each individual, making them difficult to replicate or forge.

12922
21:51:03,086 --> 21:51:04,144
人脸识别。
Facial recognition.

12923
21:51:04,430 --> 21:51:10,304
人脸识别技术使用算法来分析个人面部的独特特征。
Facial recognition technology uses algorithms to analyze the unique features of an individual's face.

12924
21:51:10,574 --> 21:51:20,224
这种身份验证方式是非侵入式的，可用于非接触式访问控制，
在卫生要求极高的医疗环境中特别有用。
This form of authentication is non-intrusive and can be used for contactless access control,
which is particularly useful in healthcare environments where hygiene is critical.

12925
21:51:20,464 --> 21:51:22,144
视网膜或虹膜扫描。
Retina or iris scanning.

12926
21:51:22,384 --> 21:51:27,424
视网膜和虹膜扫描在识别个人方面具有极高的准确性。
Retina and iris scans offer a high level of accuracy for identifying individuals.

12927
21:51:27,664 --> 21:51:34,784
这些技术可以捕捉眼睛中的独特特征，使其在高度风险区域的安全性访问控制中非常有效。
These technologies capture unique patterns in the eyes, making them effective for secure access control in high-risk areas.

12928
21:51:35,086 --> 21:51:39,984
生物识别在用户便利性和安全性方面具有显著优势。
Biometrics offer significant advantages in terms of user convenience and security.

12929
21:51:40,224 --> 21:51:49,584
然而，与所有身份验证方法一样，医疗机构必须正确实施这些技术，确保符合隐私法律和法规。
However, like all authentication methods, it is essential that healthcare organizations implement them properly,
ensuring they comply with privacy laws and regulations.

12930
21:51:49,934 --> 21:51:55,984
在生物识别身份验证之后，让我们来看看 FIDO，这是一种现代的无密码身份验证标准。
After biometric authentication, let's look at FIDO, a modern standard for passwordless authentication.

12931
21:51:56,206 --> 21:51:58,224
身份验证访问，FIDO。
Authenticating access, FIDO.

12932
21:51:58,544 --> 21:52:05,744
FAST Identity Online FIDO 标准旨在为用户提供安全的无密码身份验证。
The FAST Identity Online FIDO, standard is designed to enable secure passwordless authentication for users.

12933
21:52:06,126 --> 21:52:14,544
FIDO 允许用户使用生物识别数据、PIN 码或硬件安全密钥进行身份验证，从而无需传统密码。
FIDO allows users to authenticate using biometric data, pins, or hardware security keys,
eliminating the need for traditional passwords.

12934
21:52:14,766 --> 21:52:20,640
FIDO 得到了广泛采用，因为它在提供强大安全性的同时提高了用户便利性。
FIDO has gained widespread adoption because it offers robust security while improving user convenience.

12935
21:52:20,942 --> 21:52:22,480
无密码身份验证。
Passwordless authentication.

12936
21:52:22,766 --> 21:52:28,720
通过 FIDO，用户可以通过安全流程进行身份验证，而无需记住复杂的密码。
With FIDO, users can authenticate through a secure process without needing to remember complex passwords.

12937
21:52:29,102 --> 21:52:36,480
FIDO 使用公钥加密来验证用户身份，比传统的基于密码的系统更安全。
FIDO uses public key cryptography to verify users' identities, making it more secure than traditional password-based systems.

12938
21:52:36,846 --> 21:52:37,760
安全密钥。
Security keys.

12939
21:52:38,094 --> 21:52:44,720
FIDO 支持使用硬件安全密钥，例如 USB 设备或 Bluetooth 令牌来验证用户身份。
FIDO supports the use of hardware security keys, such as USB devices or Bluetooth tokens to authenticate users.

12940
21:52:44,960 --> 21:52:55,200
这些密钥存储密码学数据，且必须物理存在才能验证系统访问权限，
使它们成为防御网络钓鱼和其他类型网络攻击的有效手段。
These keys store cryptographic data and must be physically present to authenticate access to systems,
making them an effective defense against phishing and other types of cyber attacks.

12941
21:52:55,440 --> 21:52:56,880
多平台支持。
Multi-platform support.

12942
21:52:57,166 --> 21:53:07,760
FIDO 可用于多种平台，包括移动设备、桌面电脑和 Web 应用程序，
确保用户无论使用何种设备都能安全地进行身份验证。
FIDO can be used across a variety of platforms, including mobile devices, desktops, and web applications,
ensuring that users can securely authenticate regardless of their device.

12943
21:53:08,014 --> 21:53:16,320
通过采用 FIDO 标准，医疗机构可以为用户提供一
种无缝且安全的身份验证方式，而无需依赖密码。
By adopting the FIDO standard, healthcare organizations can offer users
a seamless and secure way to authenticate without relying on passwords.

12944
21:53:16,590 --> 21:53:24,388
既然我们已经涵盖了身份验证，现在让我们转向探索医疗设备和医疗物联网 医疗物联网 的安全。
Now that we've covered authentication, let's move on to explore securing medical devices and the Internet of Medical Things, IOMT.

12945
21:53:24,686 --> 21:53:27,108
保障医疗设备和 IoT 的安全。
Securing Medical Devices and IOT.

12946
21:53:27,440 --> 21:53:37,520
随着医疗领域对联网设备依赖的增加，保障医疗设备
和医疗物联网 IMT 的安全已成为关注的重点领域。
With the increasing reliance on connected devices in healthcare, securing medical
devices and the Internet of Medical Things, IMT, has become a critical area of focus.

12947
21:53:37,760 --> 21:53:44,420
这些设备的增长扩大了攻击面，产生了网络犯罪分子可以利用的新漏洞。
The growth of these devices has expanded the attack surface, creating new vulnerabilities that cyber criminals can exploit.

12948
21:53:44,720 --> 21:53:50,692
让我们来看看保障医疗设备和 IoT 设备的安全所面临的挑战和策略。
Let's examine the security challenges and strategies for securing medical devices and IoT devices.

12949
21:53:51,040 --> 21:53:53,252
医疗设备中的漏洞。
Vulnerabilities in medical devices.

12950
21:53:53,520 --> 21:54:00,228
心脏起搏器、输液泵和成像机器等医疗设备是医疗环境中的核心工具。
Medical devices such as pacemakers, infusion pumps, and imaging machines, are essential tools in healthcare settings.

12951
21:54:00,480 --> 21:54:06,084
然而，其中许多设备存在已知漏洞，使其成为攻击者的理想目标。
However, many of these devices have known vulnerabilities that make them attractive targets for attackers.

12952
21:54:06,320 --> 21:54:11,364
医疗设备中一些常见的安全弱点包括弱身份验证。
Some common security weaknesses in medical devices include weak authentication.

12953
21:54:11,680 --> 21:54:21,440
许多医疗设备使用弱或过时的身份验证方法，例如默认密码或未加密的通信，
这使它们容易受到未经授权的访问。
Many medical devices use weak or outdated authentication methods, such as default passwords or unencrypted communications,
making them vulnerable to unauthorized access.

12954
21:54:21,806 --> 21:54:23,108
未打补丁的软件。
Unpatched software.

12955
21:54:23,360 --> 21:54:28,388
一些医疗设备运行在不再受制造商支持的旧版软件上。
Some medical devices run on legacy software that is no longer supported by the manufacturer.

12956
21:54:28,640 --> 21:54:34,948
这些设备可能无法获得定期的安全更新或补丁，导致它们暴露在已知的漏洞中。
These devices may not receive regular security updates or patches, leaving them exposed to known vulnerabilities.

12957
21:54:35,310 --> 21:54:36,772
不安全的通信。
Insecure communication.

12958
21:54:37,040 --> 21:54:44,804
医疗设备经常在不安全的网络上传输敏感数据，增加了被攻击者拦截或篡改的风险。
Medical devices often transmit sensitive data across unsecured networks,
increasing the risk of interception or tampering by attackers.

12959
21:54:45,120 --> 21:54:46,852
缺乏监控和日志记录。
Lack of monitoring and logging.

12960
21:54:47,120 --> 21:54:55,520
许多医疗设备缺乏足够的监控或日志记录能力，导致难以实时检测和响应安全事件。
Many medical devices do not have sufficient monitoring or logging capabilities,
making it difficult to detect and respond to security incidents in real time.

12961
21:54:55,760 --> 21:55:07,556
为了缓解这些漏洞，医疗机构应实施强有力的安全协议，包括网络分段、定期更新软件，
以及针对医疗设备的强认证措施。
To mitigate these vulnerabilities, healthcare organizations should implement strong security protocols,
including network segmentation, regular software updates, and robust authentication measures for medical devices.

12962
21:55:07,840 --> 21:55:11,716
医疗物联网，IoT 的安全考量。
Security considerations for the Internet of Medical Things, IoT.

12963
21:55:12,000 --> 21:55:21,680
医疗物联网，即 IoT，是指医疗保健中连接设备的
网络，包括可穿戴设备、诊断机器和远程监控工具。
The Internet of Medical Things, IoT, refers to the network of connected devices in healthcare, including wearable devices,
diagnostic machines, and remote monitoring tools.

12964
21:55:21,920 --> 21:55:29,988
虽然 IoT 带来了显著的益处，如改善患者护理和提高运营效率，但它也带来了新的安全挑战。
While IoT offers significant benefits, such as improved patient care
and operational efficiency, it also presents new security challenges.

12965
21:55:30,320 --> 21:55:32,676
设备身份验证和授权。
Device authentication and authorization.

12966
21:55:32,960 --> 21:55:43,120
为了确保只有授权用户才能访问 IoT 设备，医疗机构必须实施强身份验证措施，
例如 MFA 和生物识别访问控制。
To ensure only authorized users can access IoT devices, healthcare organizations must
implement strong authentication measures, such as MFA and biometric access control.

12967
21:55:43,600 --> 21:55:44,800
数据加密。
Data encryption.

12968
21:55:45,040 --> 21:55:50,560
IoT 设备传输敏感数据，例如患者的生命体征或药物剂量。
IoT devices transmit sensitive data, such as patient vital signs or medication dosages.

12969
21:55:50,800 --> 21:55:55,920
对这些数据在传输中和静态存储时进行加密，对于保护患者隐私至关重要。
Encrypting this data both in transit and at rest is crucial to protecting patient privacy.

12970
21:55:56,368 --> 21:55:57,728
网络分段。
Network segmentation.

12971
21:55:57,968 --> 21:56:07,716
医疗机构应将 IoT 设备与网络上的其他关键系统进行分段，
以防止在某个设备被入侵时，攻击者在网络内横向移动。
Healthcare organizations should segment IoT devices from other critical systems on their networks to prevent attackers from moving
laterally within the network if one device is compromised.

12972
21:56:08,048 --> 21:56:09,648
定期的安全审计。
Regular security audits.

12973
21:56:09,888 --> 21:56:16,932
为了确保 IoT 设备保持安全，医疗机构应定期进行安全审计和渗透测试。
To ensure IoT devices remain secure, healthcare organizations should conduct regular security audits and penetration testing.

12974
21:56:17,168 --> 21:56:22,048
这有助于识别漏洞，并在攻击发生前主动解决它们。
This helps identify vulnerabilities and address them proactively before an attack occurs.

12975
21:56:22,288 --> 21:56:31,844
随着联网医疗设备使用的不断增加，保护 IoT 将是保护患者数据和维护医疗系统完整性的关键。
As the use of connected medical devices continues to rise, securing the IoT will be essential to protecting patient data and
maintaining the integrity of healthcare systems.

12976
21:56:32,208 --> 21:56:40,676
结论：保护医疗技术和身份验证系统对于保护患者数据和确保医疗服务的连续性至关重要。
Conclusion: Securing healthcare technology and authentication systems is
crucial to safeguarding patient data and ensuring the continuity of care.

12977
21:56:41,008 --> 21:56:51,050
通过加密和安全数据备份来保护电子健康记录 EHR，实施强有力的用户身份验证机制，
并保护医疗设备和 IoT 设备，是稳健的医疗网络安全策略的核心组成部分。
Protecting electronic health records, EHRs, through encryption and secure data backup,
implementing strong user authentication mechanisms, and securing medical devices and

12978
21:56:51,050 --> 21:56:55,908
通过加密和安全数据备份来保护电子健康记录 EHR，实施强有力的用户身份验证机制，
并保护医疗设备和 IoT 设备，是稳健的医疗网络安全策略的核心组成部分。
IoT devices are essential components of a robust healthcare cybersecurity strategy.

12979
21:56:56,208 --> 21:57:04,772
随着医疗机构不断采用新技术，及时应对新兴威胁并投资保护这些技术至关重要。
As healthcare organizations continue to adopt new technologies, it is critical
to stay ahead of emerging threats and to invest in securing these technologies.

12980
21:57:05,088 --> 21:57:16,740
通过实施强有力的网络安全措施并了解最佳实践，医疗机构可以
保护敏感数据，改善患者护理，并降低与网络威胁相关的风险。
By implementing strong cybersecurity measures and staying informed about best practices,
healthcare institutions can protect sensitive data, improve patient care, and reduce the risks associated with cyber threats.

12981
21:57:17,008 --> 21:57:26,768
通过专注于保护医疗技术和身份验证机制，机构可以确
保为医疗提供者和患者提供更安全、更高效的医疗环境。
By focusing on securing healthcare technology and authentication mechanisms, organizations can ensure a more secure and efficient
healthcare environment for both providers and patients.

12982
21:57:27,008 --> 21:57:29,968
建立具有韧性的医疗安全计划。
Building a resilient healthcare security program.

12983
21:57:30,670 --> 21:57:41,168
随着医疗行业不断拥抱数字化转型，保护技术基础
设施和敏感数据免受网络安全威胁已变得至关重要。
As the healthcare sector continues to embrace digital transformation, safeguarding the technology infrastructure and sensitive data
from cybersecurity threats has become paramount.

12984
21:57:41,486 --> 21:57:50,448
针对医疗系统的网络攻击可能会干扰患者护理，破坏个人健康信息，并严重损害机构的声誉。
Cyber attacks on healthcare systems can disrupt patient care, compromise personal health information,
and severely damage an organization's reputation.

12985
21:57:50,830 --> 21:58:00,128
一个有韧性的医疗安全计划对于应对、响应和从这些攻击中恢复，
同时确保医疗服务的连续性至关重要。
A resilient healthcare security program is crucial for preparing for, responding to,
and recovering from these attacks while ensuring the continuity of care.

12986
21:58:00,398 --> 21:58:13,808
本模块将探讨构建稳健医疗安全计划的关键要素，包括事件响应、业务连续性、人为因素、
意识培训以及新兴的网络安全威胁。
This module explores key elements of building a robust healthcare security program, including incident response, business continuity,
human factors, awareness training, and emerging cybersecurity threats.

12987
21:58:14,158 --> 21:58:16,548
事件响应和业务连续性。
Incident response and business continuity.

12988
21:58:17,102 --> 21:58:23,088
在任何组织中，特别是在医疗领域，数据泄露都可能产生深远的影响。
In any organization, particularly in healthcare, a security breach can have far-reaching consequences.

12989
21:58:23,342 --> 21:58:29,488
因此，为网络攻击做准备并制定明确的响应计划，对于减少损害至关重要。
Therefore, preparing for cyber attacks and having a well-defined response plan is critical to minimizing harm.

12990
21:58:29,838 --> 21:58:42,928
事件响应 IR 和业务连续性 BC 计划是医疗安全计划的核心组成部分，
帮助组织管理攻击并在没有重大中断的情况下继续提供医疗服务。
Incident response, IR, and business continuity, BC, plans are essential components of a healthcare security program,
helping organizations manage attacks and continue providing care without significant disruption.

12991
21:58:43,278 --> 21:58:46,768
为医疗数据泄露制定有效的事件响应计划。
Creating an effective incident response plan for healthcare breaches.

12992
21:58:47,150 --> 21:58:54,288
事件响应计划 IRP 概述了医疗机构在应对网络攻击时必须采取的步骤。
An incident response plan, IRP, outlines the steps healthcare organizations must take when responding to a cyber attack.

12993
21:58:54,574 --> 21:59:03,648
拥有有效的 IRP 可以确保在发生数据泄露时，响应能够迅速、有序，
并最大限度地减少对患者护理和敏感数据的影响。
Having an effective IRP ensures that when a breach occurs, the response is swift, organized,
and minimizes the impact on patient care and sensitive data.

12994
21:59:03,982 --> 21:59:10,020
医疗领域稳健的 IRP 应包括以下关键组件：识别与检测。
A solid IRP in healthcare should include the following key components: identification and detection.

12995
21:59:10,478 --> 21:59:15,408
任何事件响应的第一步都是识别到数据泄露或攻击正在发生。
The first step in any incident response is identifying that a breach or attack is occurring.

12996
21:59:15,694 --> 21:59:28,208
医疗机构必须部署入侵检测系统 IDS 和安全信息和
事件管理解决方案，来监控网络并识别可疑活动。
Healthcare organizations must deploy tools such as intrusion detection systems, IDS,
and Security Information and Event Management solutions to monitor networks and identify suspicious activities.

12997
21:59:28,494 --> 21:59:33,488
当事件发生时，这些工具可以提醒 IT 员工，从而触发响应进程。
These tools can alert IT staff when an incident occurs, triggering the response process.

12998
21:59:33,806 --> 21:59:34,628
遏制。
Containment.

12999
21:59:34,990 --> 21:59:39,728
一旦检测到事件，下一步就是将其遏制住，以防止进一步的损害。
Once an incident is detected, the next step is to contain it to prevent further damage.

13000
21:59:39,982 --> 21:59:49,168
例如，如果检测到勒索软件，响应团队应隔离受影响的系统和网络，
以防止恶意软件在医疗基础设施中传播。
For example, if ransomware is detected, the response team should isolate affected systems and networks to prevent the malware from
spreading across the healthcare infrastructure.

13001
21:59:49,486 --> 21:59:57,476
遏制还包括限制攻击范围，并确定最关键的系统，以便进行根除和恢复。
Containment also involves limiting the attack scope and identifying the most critical systems to protect eradication and recovery.

13002
21:59:57,904 --> 22:00:02,144
在遏制之后，必须清除受影响系统中的恶意行为者。
After containment, the affected systems must be cleansed of malicious actors.

13003
22:00:02,384 --> 22:00:09,344
这包括移除恶意软件、恢复被入侵的文件，并修复在攻击过程中被利用的漏洞。
This involves removing malware, restoring compromised files, and patching vulnerabilities that were exploited during the attack.

13004
22:00:09,614 --> 22:00:18,704
一旦根除完成，就可以开始恢复工作，包括从备份中恢复系统，
并在上线前确保所有系统都是安全的。
Once eradication is complete, recovery efforts can begin, including restoring
systems from backups and ensuring that all systems are secure before going live.

13005
22:00:19,022 --> 22:00:20,836
沟通与协调。
Communication and coordination.

13006
22:00:21,262 --> 22:00:24,304
在事件发生期间，有效的沟通至关重要。
During an incident, effective communication is crucial.

13007
22:00:24,590 --> 22:00:35,024
IRP 应包含明确的沟通协议，规定如何在组织内部以及
与外部利益相关者（如监管机构和患者）之间共享信息。
The IRP should include a clear communication protocol that defines how information is shared within the organization and with external
stakeholders, such as regulatory bodies and patients.

13008
22:00:35,310 --> 22:00:40,624
及时且透明的沟通有助于缓解对组织声誉的损害。
Timely and transparent communication can help mitigate the damage to an organization's reputation.

13009
22:00:40,974 --> 22:00:43,184
事后分析和报告。
Post-incident analysis and reporting.

13010
22:00:43,438 --> 22:00:54,304
在事件解决后，响应团队应进行彻底分析，以了解攻击的影响、攻击是如何实施的，
以及可以采取哪些措施来防止未来的数据泄露。
After the incident has been resolved, the response team should conduct a thorough analysis to understand the attack's impact,
how it was carried out, and what measures can be implemented to prevent future breaches.

13011
22:00:54,638 --> 22:01:02,144
这种事后分析对于改进 IRP 和完善组织的整体网络安全态势至关重要。
This post-mortem analysis is crucial for improving the IRP and refining the organization's overall cybersecurity posture.

13012
22:01:02,414 --> 22:01:10,144
一旦 IRP 就位，医疗机构还必须确保在网络攻击期间和之后能够维持运营。
Once the IRP is in place, healthcare organizations must also ensure that they can maintain operations during and after a cyber attack.

13013
22:01:10,384 --> 22:01:14,704
这就是业务连续性和灾难恢复规划发挥作用的地方。
This is where business continuity and disaster recovery planning come into play.

13014
22:01:15,022 --> 22:01:17,744
业务连续性和灾难恢复规划。
Business continuity and disaster recovery planning.

13015
22:01:17,984 --> 22:01:26,304
业务连续性，简称 BC，以及灾难恢复，简称 DR，是
任何安全计划的核心组成部分，尤其是在医疗领域。
Business continuity, BC, and disaster recovery, DR, are essential components of any security program, especially in healthcare.

13016
22:01:26,510 --> 22:01:35,504
这些计划有助于确保即使面临网络攻击、自然灾害或技术故障，
患者的护理也能在没有重大中断的情况下继续进行。
These plans help ensure that patient care can continue without significant disruption,
even in the face of cyber attacks, natural disasters, or technical failures.

13017
22:01:35,854 --> 22:01:38,304
业务连续性规划，简称 BCP。
Business Continuity Planning, BCP.

13018
22:01:38,624 --> 22:01:44,544
BCP 是确保关键医疗业务在灾难发生期间和灾难之后继续运行的进程。
BCP is the process of ensuring that critical healthcare operations continue during and after a disaster.

13019
22:01:44,814 --> 22:01:56,064
在网络安全的上下文中，BCP 侧重于患者护理的连续性，包括确保用于医疗服务的系统、
应用程序和数据可用且正常运行。
In the context of cybersecurity, BCP focuses on the continuity of patient care, including ensuring that systems, applications,
and data needed for healthcare delivery are available and functional.

13020
22:01:56,398 --> 22:02:07,588
医疗机构最优先考虑基本服务，如 EHR 访问、排班和患者监测，
确保如果主系统宕机时有替代方案。
Healthcare organizations most prioritize essential services, such as EHR access, scheduling, and patient monitoring,
ensuring that alternative solutions are in place if primary systems go down.

13021
22:02:07,984 --> 22:02:18,704
灾难恢复，简称 DR。虽然 BCP 侧重于维持运营，但灾难恢复侧重于在灾难性事件后恢复系统。
Disaster recovery, DR. While BCP focuses on maintaining operations,
disaster recovery focuses on restoring systems after a catastrophic event.

13022
22:02:18,990 --> 22:02:26,944
DR 计划概述了恢复系统、应用程序和数据的步骤，包括备份和恢复进程。
A DR plan outlines the steps for restoring systems, applications, and data, including backup and restoration processes.

13023
22:02:27,214 --> 22:02:33,444
定期测试和更新 DR 计划对于确保其在最需要时发挥作用至关重要。
Regularly testing and updating the DR plan is critical to ensure its effectiveness when it's needed most.

13024
22:02:33,902 --> 22:02:35,584
基于云的备份解决方案。
Cloud-based backup solutions.

13025
22:02:36,014 --> 22:02:45,024
作为 DR 规划的一部分，医疗机构应考虑实施基于
云的备份解决方案，以确保数据安全地存储在异地。
As part of DR planning, healthcare organizations should consider implementing
cloud-based backup solutions to ensure data is securely stored off-site.

13026
22:02:45,358 --> 22:02:52,704
一旦发生攻击，机构可以从云端快速恢复加密数据，从而最大限度地减少停机时间和数据丢失。
In the event of an attack, organizations can quickly restore encrypted data from the cloud, minimizing downtime and data loss.

13027
22:02:52,974 --> 22:02:55,104
冗余和故障转移系统。
Redundancy and failover systems.

13028
22:02:55,374 --> 22:02:58,784
医疗系统在设计时应考虑到冗余。
Healthcare systems should be designed with redundancy in mind.

13029
22:02:59,024 --> 22:03:06,144
例如，服务器、网络和医疗设备等关键基础设施应配备故障转移系统。
For example, critical infrastructure like servers, networks, and medical devices should have failover systems in place.

13030
22:03:06,414 --> 22:03:12,064
如果一个系统故障，另一个系统应自动接管，以避免患者护理受到干扰。
If one system fails, another should automatically take over to avoid disruption in patient care.

13031
22:03:12,334 --> 22:03:25,264
通过将这些策略整合到组织的整体网络安全计划中，医疗机构可以创建一个具有韧性的框架，
确保即使在网络攻击或灾难期间，患者护理也能继续进行。
By integrating these strategies into an organization's overall cybersecurity plan,
healthcare institutions can create a resilient framework that ensures patient care can continue even during a cyberattack or disaster.

13032
22:03:25,614 --> 22:03:34,144
既然我们了解了事件响应和连续性的重要性，现在
让我们转向探讨人为因素在网络安全中的关键作用。
Now that we understand the importance of incident response and continuity,
let's move on to explore the critical role of the human factor in cybersecurity.

13033
22:03:34,464 --> 22:03:36,464
人为因素和意识培训。
Human factor and awareness training.

13034
22:03:36,750 --> 22:03:42,704
虽然技术在网络安全中起着至关重要的作用，但人为因素往往是最薄弱的一环。
While technology plays a crucial role in cybersecurity, the human factor is often the weakest link.

13035
22:03:42,894 --> 22:03:51,184
针对医疗员工的社会工程学攻击、网络钓鱼和其他策略甚至可能破坏最先进的安全系统。
Social engineering attacks, phishing, and other tactics targeting
healthcare employees can compromise even the most advanced security systems.

13036
22:03:51,438 --> 22:03:59,344
因此，实施全面的意识培训计划至关重要，以赋能员工识别并应对网络威胁。
It is therefore essential to implement comprehensive awareness training
programs to empower employees to recognize and respond to cyber threats.

13037
22:03:59,758 --> 22:04:02,768
针对医疗工作人员的社会工程学技术。
Social engineering techniques targeting healthcare staff.

13038
22:04:03,086 --> 22:04:12,848
网络犯罪分子经常使用社会工程学技术来操纵医疗工作人员，
诱导其泄露敏感信息或授予未经授权的系统访问权限。
Cybercriminals frequently use social engineering techniques to manipulate healthcare
staff into disclosing sensitive information or granting unauthorized access to systems.

13039
22:04:13,198 --> 22:04:17,568
在医疗领域，这些攻击可以采取多种形式，包括网络钓鱼。
In healthcare, these attacks can take various forms, including phishing.

13040
22:04:17,934 --> 22:04:21,168
网络钓鱼是最常见的社会工程学策略之一。
Phishing is one of the most common social engineering tactics.

13041
22:04:21,454 --> 22:04:30,368
攻击者发送虚假的电子邮件、短信或电话，看起来
像是来自可信来源，例如同事、高管或政府机构。
Attackers send fraudulent emails, texts, or phone calls that appear to be
from trusted sources, such as colleagues, executives, or government agencies.

13042
22:04:30,606 --> 22:04:38,848
这些消息通常包含恶意链接或附件，一旦点击，就会允许攻击者安装恶意软件或窃取登录凭据。
These messages often contain malicious links or attachments that, when
clicked, allow attackers to install malware or steal login credentials.

13043
22:04:39,118 --> 22:04:40,048
鱼叉式网络钓鱼。
Spear phishing.

13044
22:04:40,270 --> 22:04:44,128
与通用的网络钓鱼攻击不同，鱼叉式网络钓鱼是高度针对性的。
Unlike generic phishing attacks, spear phishing is highly targeted.

13045
22:04:44,368 --> 22:04:50,608
攻击者利用个人信息研究受害者，以此伪造出看起来很真实的合法信息。
Attackers research their victims using personal information to craft convincing messages that appear legitimate.

13046
22:04:50,894 --> 22:04:58,928
在医疗领域，鱼叉式网络钓鱼可能涉及冒充医生或管理员，
以索要敏感的患者数据或访问电子健康记录（电子健康记录）。
In healthcare, spear phishing may involve impersonating a doctor or administrator to request sensitive patient data or access to EHRs.

13047
22:04:59,150 --> 22:04:59,968
虚构身份。
Pretexting.

13048
22:05:00,208 --> 22:05:07,888
在这种技术中，攻击者伪装成有正当理由获取敏感信息的人，比如 Auditor 或 IT 技术人员。
In this technique, attackers pose as someone who has a legitimate need for sensitive information, such as an auditor or IT technician.

13049
22:05:08,110 --> 22:05:15,968
通过编造故事或虚构身份，攻击者获取医疗人员的信任，并说服他们分享机密信息。
By creating a fabricated story or pretext, attackers gain the trust of
healthcare staff and convince them to share confidential information.

13050
22:05:16,302 --> 22:05:16,928
诱饵攻击。
Baiting.

13051
22:05:17,198 --> 22:05:25,248
诱饵攻击涉及提供诱人的奖励，比如免费软件或医疗用品，以此换取登录凭据或个人信息。
Baiting involves offering something enticing, like free software or medical supplies,
in exchange for login credentials or personal information.

13052
22:05:25,550 --> 22:05:31,968
医疗工作人员可能会收到免费培训或设备的提议，从而导致他们泄露敏感细节。
Healthcare workers might be targeted with offers of free training or equipment, leading them to reveal sensitive details.

13053
22:05:32,334 --> 22:05:36,048
网络钓鱼和垃圾邮件，识别并规避常见威胁。
Phishing and spam, identifying and avoiding common threats.

13054
22:05:36,430 --> 22:05:39,728
网络钓鱼和垃圾邮件是医疗领域的重大威胁。
Phishing and spam are significant threats in the healthcare sector.

13055
22:05:39,982 --> 22:05:45,248
攻击者利用这些手段渗透系统，窃取个人信息和医疗信息。
Attackers use these tactics to infiltrate systems and steal personal and healthcare information.

13056
22:05:45,582 --> 22:05:52,368
为了保护医疗人员和系统，必须培训员工识别网络钓鱼尝试和垃圾邮件。
To protect healthcare staff and systems, it is essential to train employees to recognize phishing attempts and spam emails.

13057
22:05:52,622 --> 22:05:54,528
识别可疑邮件。
Recognizing suspicious emails.

13058
22:05:54,798 --> 22:06:04,608
员工应接受培训，识别可疑邮件的特征，例如拼写错误的
URL、异常的发件人地址，以及未经请求的附件或链接。
Employees should be trained to look for suspicious email characteristics, such as
misspelled URLs, unusual sender addresses, and unsolicited attachments or links.

13059
22:06:04,846 --> 22:06:09,168
他们应避免点击来自未知发件人的链接或下载附件。
They should avoid clicking on links or downloading attachments from unknown senders.

13060
22:06:09,408 --> 22:06:11,888
核实敏感信息的请求。
Verifying requests for sensitive information.

13061
22:06:12,174 --> 22:06:20,048
应鼓励医疗工作人员通过既定渠道直接联系请求人，以核实敏感信息的请求。
Healthcare workers should be encouraged to verify requests for sensitive
information by contacting the requester directly through an established channel.

13062
22:06:20,334 --> 22:06:27,168
例如，如果一封邮件要求提供登录凭据，接收者应通过致电所谓的请求人来确认该请求。
For example, if an email asks for login credentials, the recipient should confirm the request by calling the supposed requester.

13063
22:06:27,662 --> 22:06:29,248
实施邮件过滤。
Implementing email filters.

13064
22:06:29,518 --> 22:06:32,608
许多邮件系统提供网络钓鱼和垃圾邮件过滤功能。
Many email systems offer phishing and spam filters.

13065
22:06:32,878 --> 22:06:40,768
医疗机构应确保启用这些过滤器，并配置它们以拦截已知的恶意发件人和潜在有害内容。
Healthcare organizations should ensure that these filters are enabled and
configured to block known malicious senders and potentially harmful content.

13066
22:06:41,006 --> 22:06:48,368
通过将这些做法纳入日常运营，医疗机构可以降低社会工程学攻击的风险。
By incorporating these practices into daily operations, healthcare organizations can reduce the risk of social engineering attacks.

13067
22:06:48,622 --> 22:06:58,116
既然我们已经涵盖了社会工程学手段和网络钓鱼，现在让我们
深入探讨为所有员工建立全面的安全意识培训计划的重要性。
Now that we've covered social engineering tactics and phishing, let's dive into the importance of developing a comprehensive security
awareness training program for all employees.

13068
22:06:58,368 --> 22:07:01,888
制定全面的安全意识培训计划。
Developing a comprehensive security awareness training program.

13069
22:07:02,414 --> 22:07:13,808
完善的安全意识培训计划可确保所有医疗工作人员了解潜在风险，
并知道如何保护自己和组织免受网络威胁。
A well-rounded security awareness training program ensures that all healthcare staff members understand the potential risks and know
how to protect themselves and the organization from cyber threats.

13070
22:07:14,126 --> 22:07:20,288
全面的培训计划应包括以下组成部分：基础网络安全原则。
A comprehensive training program should include the following components basic cybersecurity principles.

13071
22:07:20,528 --> 22:07:29,728
员工应了解网络安全的基础知识，包括强密码、多因素身份验证 MFA 以及加密的重要性。
Employees should understand the fundamentals of cybersecurity, including the importance of strong passwords,
multifactor authentication, MFA, and encryption.

13072
22:07:30,128 --> 22:07:31,460
特定角色培训。
Role-specific training.

13073
22:07:31,662 --> 22:07:35,568
医疗机构的不同部门有不同的安全需求。
Different departments in a healthcare organization have different security needs.

13074
22:07:35,758 --> 22:07:44,848
例如，行政人员应接受处理敏感患者数据的培训，
而 IT 人员则应接受网络安全和事件响应的培训。
For example, administrative staff should be trained on handling sensitive patient data,
while IT staff should be trained on network security and incident response.

13075
22:07:45,134 --> 22:07:47,248
网络钓鱼和社会工程学意识。
Phishing and social engineering awareness.

13076
22:07:47,534 --> 22:07:55,088
培训应重点关注识别网络钓鱼企图、社会工程学手段，以及如何报告可疑活动。
Training should specifically focus on recognizing phishing attempts,
social engineering tactics, and how to report suspicious activities.

13077
22:07:55,328 --> 22:07:56,928
定期测试和演练。
Regular testing and drills.

13078
22:07:57,166 --> 22:08:03,808
为了强化培训，医疗机构应定期进行网络钓鱼模拟演练和安全演练。
To reinforce training, healthcare organizations should conduct regular phishing simulation exercises and security drills.

13079
22:08:04,048 --> 22:08:09,808
这些演练旨在测试员工在实时系统中识别和应对网络威胁的能力。
These exercises test employees' ability to recognize and respond to cyber threats in real time.

13080
22:08:10,094 --> 22:08:11,168
持续学习。
Continuous learning.

13081
22:08:11,408 --> 22:08:16,368
网络安全威胁在不断演变，因此持续的教育至关重要。
Cybersecurity threats are constantly evolving, so ongoing education is essential.

13082
22:08:16,654 --> 22:08:21,808
应鼓励员工随时了解最新的安全威胁和最佳实践。
Employees should be encouraged to stay up to date with the latest security threats and best practices.

13083
22:08:22,030 --> 22:08:32,928
通过投资全面的安全意识培训，医疗机构可以建立安全文化，
并让员工成为抵御网络攻击的第一道防线。
By investing in comprehensive security awareness training, healthcare organizations can create a culture of security and empower staff
to act as the first line of defense against cyber attacks.

13084
22:08:33,230 --> 22:08:35,168
未来趋势和新兴威胁。
Future trends and emerging threats.

13085
22:08:35,408 --> 22:08:44,448
随着技术的不断进步，医疗机构必须走在新兴威胁和趋势的前面，以保持强大的网络安全防御。
As technology continues to advance, healthcare organizations must stay ahead
of emerging threats and trends to maintain strong cybersecurity defenses.

13086
22:08:44,718 --> 22:08:55,808
供应链攻击的兴起、对第三方供应商日益增长的依赖，以及即将到来的量子计算威胁，
都是医疗网络安全未来的关键考量因素。
The rise of supply chain attacks, the growing reliance on third-party vendors, and the impending threat of quantum computing are all
critical considerations for the future of healthcare cybersecurity.

13087
22:08:56,078 --> 22:08:59,328
供应链攻击的兴起和第三方供应商风险。
The rise of supply chain attacks and third-party vendor risk.

13088
22:08:59,568 --> 22:09:05,488
供应链攻击涉及针对拥有组织系统和数据访问权限的第三方供应商。
Supply chain attacks involve targeting third-party vendors with access to an organization's systems and data.

13089
22:09:05,742 --> 22:09:13,328
医疗机构经常与多个供应商合作，包括软件提供商、医疗设备制造商和服务提供商。
Healthcare organizations often work with multiple vendors, including
software providers, medical equipment manufacturers, and service providers.

13090
22:09:13,614 --> 22:09:18,288
如果这些供应商被入侵，攻击者就可以获取敏感的医疗数据。
If these vendors are compromised, attackers can gain access to sensitive healthcare data.

13091
22:09:18,574 --> 22:09:19,888
供应商风险管理。
Vendor risk management.

13092
22:09:20,078 --> 22:09:25,808
医疗机构必须评估并管理第三方供应商带来的网络安全风险。
Healthcare organizations must assess and manage the cybersecurity risks posed by third-party vendors.

13093
22:09:26,048 --> 22:09:34,288
这包括进行安全评估、审查供应商的安全政策，并确保供应商遵守 HIPAA 等行业标准。
This includes conducting security assessments, reviewing vendor security policies,
and ensuring that vendors adhere to industry standards such as HIPAA.

13094
22:09:34,688 --> 22:09:36,368
数据共享与整合。
Data sharing and integration.

13095
22:09:36,622 --> 22:09:42,448
随着医疗系统的日益互联，组织与供应商之间的数据共享在不断增加。
As healthcare systems become more interconnected, data sharing between organizations and vendors increases.

13096
22:09:42,734 --> 22:09:50,848
安全的数据整合和传输对于确保第三方访问不会给医疗系统引入漏洞至关重要。
Secure data integration and transmission are critical to ensuring that
third-party access does not introduce vulnerabilities into healthcare systems.

13097
22:09:51,118 --> 22:09:54,208
针对供应商的多因素身份验证，即 MFA。
Multi-factor authentication, MFA, for vendors.

13098
22:09:54,478 --> 22:10:03,088
医疗机构应要求其供应商实施 MFA 和其他强身份验证措施，以保护其系统和数据的访问安全。
Healthcare organizations should require their vendors to implement MFA and
other strong authentication measures to secure access to their systems and data.

13099
22:10:03,438 --> 22:10:13,328
通过加强供应链安全和供应商风险管理实践，医疗机构可
以降低外部数据泄露的风险，并为量子计算威胁做好准备。
By strengthening supply chain security and vendor risk management practices, healthcare organizations can reduce the risk of external
breaches, preparing for quantum computing threats.

13100
22:10:13,568 --> 22:10:20,928
虽然量子计算在推动技术进步方面具有巨大的潜力，但它也对当前的加密标准构成了重大威胁。
While quantum computing holds great promise for advancing technology,
it also poses a significant threat to current encryption standards.

13101
22:10:21,198 --> 22:10:27,568
量子计算机有潜力破解传统的加密算法，这可能会导致敏感的医疗数据泄露。
Quantum computers have the potential to break traditional encryption algorithms which could expose sensitive healthcare data.

13102
22:10:27,888 --> 22:10:29,488
后量子加密。
Post-quantum cryptography.

13103
22:10:29,710 --> 22:10:36,368
医疗机构必须通过采用后量子加密，开始为量子计算的到来做准备。
Healthcare organizations must begin preparing for the advent of quantum computing by adopting post-quantum cryptography.

13104
22:10:36,622 --> 22:10:43,968
这些密码学算法旨在抵御来自量子计算机的攻击，确保敏感的医疗数据保持安全。
These cryptographic algorithms are designed to resist attacks from quantum computers,
ensuring that sensitive healthcare data remains secure.

13105
22:10:44,270 --> 22:10:45,808
抗量子系统。
Quantum-resistant systems.

13106
22:10:46,048 --> 22:10:53,088
关于抗量子系统的研究正在进行中，医疗机构应关注该领域的最新进展。
Research into quantum resistant systems is ongoing, and healthcare
organizations should stay informed about advancements in this field.

13107
22:10:53,326 --> 22:11:01,088
通过采用抗量子加密方法，医疗机构可以确保其网络安全基础设施在未来依然稳固。
By adopting quantum-resistant encryption methods, healthcare organizations
can ensure their cybersecurity infrastructure remains robust in the future.

13108
22:11:01,422 --> 22:11:13,808
结论：建立一个有韧性的医疗安全计划需要综合方法，结合有效的事件响应、业务连续性、
意识培训以及应对新兴威胁的主动措施。
Conclusion: Building a resilient healthcare security program requires a holistic approach that combines effective incident response,
business continuity, awareness training, and proactive measures to address emerging threats.

13109
22:11:14,030 --> 22:11:22,688
通过在这些领域进行投入，医疗机构可以加强防御，降低风险，
并确保患者护理不会受到网络攻击的干扰。
By investing in these areas, healthcare organizations can strengthen their defenses, minimize risks,
and ensure patient care is not disrupted by cyber attacks.

13110
22:11:22,928 --> 22:11:24,128
让我们从第一个问题开始。
Let's start off with question one.

13111
22:11:24,368 --> 22:11:25,648
什么是 OSI 模型？
What is the OSI model?

13112
22:11:25,968 --> 22:11:28,164
解释 OSI 模型的不同层级。
Explain the different layers of the OSI model.

13113
22:11:28,526 --> 22:11:38,692
OSI 在很大程度上是一个理论模型，用于理解网络
技术，以及数据包是如何创建和被计算机处理的。
OSI largely is a theoretical model utilized to understand networking and
how data packets are created and how they are being processed by a computer.

13114
22:11:39,248 --> 22:11:45,540
这通常由 TCP/IP，即传输控制协议/互联网协议软件套件来使用。
This is normally used by the TCPIP, the Transmission Control Protocol over Internet Protocol Software Suite.

13115
22:11:46,414 --> 22:11:50,308
所以，OSI 被称为开放系统互连模型。
So, OSI is known as the Open Systems Interconnection Model.

13116
22:11:50,542 --> 22:11:56,192
它是一个参考模型，描述了应用程序如何通过计算机网络进行交互。
It is a reference model that describes how applications are going to interact via the computer network.

13117
22:11:56,432 --> 22:11:59,268
我们需要了解七个不同的层级。
There are seven different layers that we need to understand.

13118
22:11:59,598 --> 22:12:00,548
它们如下所示。
They are as follows.

13119
22:12:01,230 --> 22:12:04,032
所以在这个图表中，有这七个不同的层级。
So in this diagram, there are these seven different layers.

13120
22:12:04,112 --> 22:12:05,284
我们从底部开始。
We start up from the bottom.

13121
22:12:05,646 --> 22:12:12,132
首先是物理层、数据链路层、网络层、传输层、会话层、表示层和应用层。
First is the physical layer, the data link layer, network layer, transport layer, session layer, presentation, and application.

13122
22:12:12,592 --> 22:12:23,030
当面试中被问到这个问题时，我们不仅要识别这七个层级，还要先解释什么是 OSI 模型，
然后尝试识别这七个层级并对每一个层级进行简要描述。
When such a question is asked in an interview, it is not only that we identify these seven layers,
explaining what the OSI model is in the first place, we then try to identify

13123
22:12:23,030 --> 22:12:27,812
当面试中被问到这个问题时，我们不仅要识别这七个层级，还要先解释什么是 OSI 模型，
然后尝试识别这七个层级并对每一个层级进行简要描述。
these seven layers and we give a brief description about each and every layer.

13124
22:12:28,112 --> 22:12:32,676
如果有任何额外的问题，它们都会在这些基础问题之后出现。
If there are any additional questions, they will come after this basic question.

13125
22:12:33,774 --> 22:12:35,792
那么让我们从物理层开始。
So let's start off with the physical layer.

13126
22:12:36,046 --> 22:12:38,592
这是 OSI 模型的最底层。
This is the lowest layer of the OSI model.

13127
22:12:38,672 --> 22:12:42,992
现在，这是计算机的所有物理硬件涉及的地方。
Now, this is where any and every physicality of your computer comes into the picture.

13128
22:12:43,214 --> 22:12:54,724
它可以是网络接口卡，可以是 RJ45 或 Cat 5 网线，任何
允许数据从你的机器到另一台机器进行物理传输的东西。
So it could be a network interface card, it could be an RJ45 or a Cat 5 cable, anything
that allows data to be transmitted physically from your machine to another machine.

13129
22:12:55,118 --> 22:12:56,708
接下来是数据链路层。
Next comes the data link layer.

13130
22:12:57,870 --> 22:13:05,952
所以在数据链路层，就网络技术而言，我们只需要了解数据包在此层被编码和解码为比特。
