13285
22:27:48,206 --> 22:27:52,132
进入第六题：分布式处理有哪些优点？
Moving on to question number six What are the advantages of distributed processing?

13286
22:27:52,656 --> 22:27:58,372
在进入分布式处理的优点之前，我们首先得了解什么是分布式处理。
Now, before we go into advantages of distributed processing, we first have to understand what is distributed processing.

13287
22:27:59,182 --> 22:28:05,636
这是一个描述使用多个处理器来运行应用程序的各种计算机系统的术语。
So it is a term which describes various computer systems that use more than one processor to run an application.

13288
22:28:06,702 --> 22:28:11,280
在这里，分布在不同位置的多台计算机共享同一个处理器。
Here, multiple computers across different locations share the same processor.

13289
22:28:11,534 --> 22:28:14,080
分布式处理的优点如下。
The advantages of distributing processes are as follows.

13290
22:28:14,160 --> 22:28:23,360
但在进入优点之前，分布式计算基本上就是多台机器将资源池化在一起来运行单个应用程序。
But before we go into the advantages, distributed computing is basically where
multiple machines will pool their resources together to run a singular application.

13291
22:28:23,520 --> 22:28:29,092
也就是说，一个拥有多种资源，并且可以根据需要随时扩展或缩减规模的应用程序。
So an application that has multiple resources and can scale up and scale down as and when required.

13292
22:28:29,774 --> 22:28:34,308
它的优点是，在数据恢复方面非常有用。
The advantages are that it can be very useful in data recovery.

13293
22:28:35,022 --> 22:28:40,132
例如 RAID，就是将数据分布在不同的硬盘上。
For example, RAID, where you're striping data on various hard disks.

13294
22:28:40,430 --> 22:28:48,612
它是可靠的，成本更低，而且由于我们刚才提到的可扩展性因素，它很容易扩展。
It is reliable, it is cheaper, lower cost can be achieved, and it is easy
to expand because of the scalability factor that we just talked about.

13295
22:28:48,910 --> 22:28:53,760
如果一台计算机的数据丢失，可以通过另一台互连的计算机来恢复。
If there is loss of data in one computer, it can then be recovered by another interconnected computer.

13296
22:28:53,920 --> 22:28:57,440
比如在当今世界，区块链就是一个例子，对吧？
And one of the examples would be blockchain in today's world, right?

13297
22:28:57,582 --> 22:28:58,400
什么是区块链？
What is blockchain?

13298
22:28:58,480 --> 22:29:03,600
就是数据是实时生成的，并存储在连接的计算机上。
That this data is created live and stored on a connection of computers.

13299
22:29:03,680 --> 22:29:12,640
所以如果其中一台计算机掉线，网络中的其他计算机仍
保留这些数据，区块链仍能正常运行，不会出任何问题。
So if one of the computers goes offline, the other computers in that network will
still have that data and the blockchain will still function without any issues.

13300
22:29:12,910 --> 22:29:19,204
第二点是，一台机器的故障不会影响处理过程，因
为还有其他多台机器，就像我们讨论的区块链一样。
The second point, a glitch in one machine does not affect the processing as
there will be multiple other machines, like we discussed in the blockchain.

13301
22:29:19,694 --> 22:29:23,440
这里使用的是几台高性价比的小型机，而不是昂贵的机器或大型机。
Several cost-effective mini computers are used instead of costly or mainframe machines.

13302
22:29:23,520 --> 22:29:35,268
所以，我不需要建立服务器集群，我可以把多台机器连接在一起，
它们可以在特定的区块链或特定的分布式处理机制中运行。
So instead of having a server bank, I can have multiple machines interconnected together and they can function in that particular
blockchain or for that particular distributed processing mechanism.

13303
22:29:36,334 --> 22:29:40,240
根据数据处理量的大小，可以连接更多的计算机到网络中。
Depending on the amount of data processing, more computers can be attached to the network.

13304
22:29:40,400 --> 22:29:47,040
因此，你可以增加参与该区块链的计算机数量，也可以根据需要随时减少数量。
Thus, you can increase the number of computers that can be a part of that blockchain or you can reduce them as and when necessary.

13305
22:29:47,246 --> 22:29:50,948
接下来看第七个问题：什么是 TCP IP？
Moving on to question number seven: what is TCP IP?

13306
22:29:52,142 --> 22:30:01,280
TCP IP，即传输控制协议在互联网协议之上，是一套用于连接互联网上网络设备的通信协议。
TCP IP or transmission control protocol over internet protocol is a set of communication
protocols that are used to interconnect networking devices on the internet.

13307
22:30:01,870 --> 22:30:07,040
该协议通过提供端到端通信，定义了数据应如何在互联网上传输。
This protocol defines how data should be transmitted over the internet by providing end-to-end communications.

13308
22:30:07,246 --> 22:30:12,164
所以基本上，如果你想在机器上建立网络，你就需要 TCP IP。
So essentially, if you want networking to be established on your machine, you will need TCP IP.

13309
22:30:12,880 --> 22:30:17,360
如果没有 TCP IP，就不会有工作组，也不会有域。
Without TCP IP, there will be no work groups, there will be no domains.

13310
22:30:17,550 --> 22:30:20,320
基本上，你的互联互通也全靠它。
Basically, your interconnectivity will go for it also.

13311
22:30:20,878 --> 22:30:33,796
TCP IP 是一种软件，安装到机器上后，它会与硬件（即你的网络接口卡）、交换机、电线、
电缆等交互，所有这些都是通过预先配置好的协议实现的。
TCP IP is a software that once installed on your machine will then interact with the hardware, which is your network interface cards,
and then your switches, wires, cables, and all those through protocols that have been already pre-configured in it.

13312
22:30:34,160 --> 22:30:48,580
所以在 TCP IP 软件套件中，你会拥有所有的协议、OSI 模型的所有功能，
并且在每个层上运行的每一个协议都会被预定义并预配置，以按特定方式运行。
So within the TCP IP suite of softwares, you will have all the protocols, all the functionality of the OSI layer,
and each and every protocol that works on each and every layer will be predefined and pre-configured to work in a particular manner.

13313
22:30:48,878 --> 22:30:53,796
互联网协议的核心就是路由每一个独立的数据包，确保它到达目的地。
The internet protocol is all about routing each individual packet to make sure it reaches its destination.

13314
22:30:54,094 --> 22:31:02,148
而 TCP 则是指允许你格式化数据并生成数据的协议，以便你可以在网络上进行通信。
So with the TCP, you're talking about the protocols that will allow you to
format the data and generate it so that you can communicate it over the network.

13315
22:31:02,350 --> 22:31:10,148
IP 随后负责这些数据包的路由，以便数据包能被路由到正确的计算机并被接收者接收。
The IP will then deal with the routing of those packets so that the packet
can be routed to the correct computer and be received by the recipient.

13316
22:31:10,670 --> 22:31:14,000
所以 TCP IP 模型是 OSI 模型的压缩版本。
So the TCP IP model is the compressed version of the OSI model.

13317
22:31:14,080 --> 22:31:20,836
七层模型被转换成四层：网络访问层、互联网层、传输层和应用层。
The seven layers will get converted into four layers the network access layer, internet layer, transport layer, and application layer.

13318
22:31:21,070 --> 22:31:25,540
继续看第 8 个问题：IP config 和 IFconfig 是什么意思？
Going on to question 8, what do you mean by IP config and IFconfig?

13319
22:31:25,920 --> 22:31:31,236
这两个都是命令，第一个是在 Windows 机器上，第二个是在 Linux 机器上。
