13885
23:34:31,374 --> 23:34:35,552
下一个问题是如何避免 ARP欺骗或 ARP。
The next question is how to avoid ARP poisoning or ARP.

13886
23:34:35,790 --> 23:34:38,112
首先，让我们了解什么是 ARP。
Now, first let's understand what ARP is.

13887
23:34:38,446 --> 23:34:44,516
ARP 代表地址解析协议，是计算机在网络上进行通信时使用的协议。
ARP stands for address resolution protocol, which is a protocol used by computers to communicate over the network.

13888
23:34:44,912 --> 23:34:50,992
当你的计算机启动后，它会开始发现过程来识别其邻居。
Once your computer boots up, it starts a discovery process of identifying its neighbors.

13889
23:34:51,214 --> 23:35:03,620
如果我在特定的子网中，我的机器会主动发送出 ARP 请求和地址解析协议，
以找出哪些机器在同一个网络内且处于在线状态。
So if I'm in a particular subnet, my machine will proactively send out ARP requests and address resolution protocol to find out which
other machines are within the same network and which are live.

13890
23:35:03,792 --> 23:35:10,596
一旦它发出查询，在线机器将回复该查询并附带其 MAC地址。
Once it sends out a query, a live machine will respond to that query along with its MAC address.

13891
23:35:12,078 --> 23:35:19,941
这些信息随后被存储在所谓的 ARP 表或机器缓存上的 ARP 表中。
This information is then stored in what is known as an ARP table or an ARP table on the machine's cache.

13892
23:35:20,750 --> 23:35:29,472
因此，每当我的机器想要向特定机器发送数据包时，它会查阅 ARP 表，
识别 IP地址及其关联的 MAC地址。
So whenever my machine now wants to send out a packet to this particular machine, it will go to the ARP table,
it will identify the IP address and the associated MAC address.

13893
23:35:29,552 --> 23:35:38,112
它会将这些信息打印在数据包上作为目标 IP 和目标 MAC，然后将该数据包发送到交换机。
It will print that onto the data packet as a destination IP and destination MAC and send that packet across to the switch.

13894
23:35:38,192 --> 23:35:45,188
交换机随后将识别 MAC地址，并将数据包发送到连接到该特定交换机的相关机器。
The switch will then identify the MAC address and send the packet to the relevant machine that is connected to that particular switch.

13895
23:35:45,712 --> 23:35:52,832
现在，为了迷惑交换机将其发送到不同的机器，ARP欺骗攻击就产生了。
Now to confuse the switch into sending it to a different machine, the R poisoning attack is created.

13896
23:35:53,152 --> 23:35:58,980
这种攻击通常是为了发起中间人攻击。
This attack is generally launched to create a man in the middle attack.

13897
23:35:59,312 --> 23:36:05,952
现在，为了从一开始就防止这种 ARP欺骗发生，我们可以利用三个不同的方面。
Now to prevent this R poisoning from happening in the first place, there are three different aspects that we can utilize.

13898
23:36:06,158 --> 23:36:12,752
首先，我们可以使用数据包过滤，它将过滤并拦截具有相同源地址的数据包。
First, we can use packet filtering, which will filter out and block packets that are the same source address data.

13899
23:36:12,832 --> 23:36:17,552
也就是说，如果你识别出一些恶意的 IP地址，并且想要拦截某些 IP地址。
So you have identified some malicious IP addresses and you want to block out some IP addresses.

13900
23:36:17,632 --> 23:36:27,472
那么你就在使用数据包过滤防火墙，你构建该防火墙来过滤来自特定 IP地址范围的某些数据包。
So you're using a packet filter firewall where you have constructed the firewall
to filter out certain packets originating from particular range of IP addresses.

13901
23:36:27,662 --> 23:36:32,228
这个防火墙和这种技术随后将拦截这些进入的数据包。
This firewall and this technique will then block those kind of packets coming in.

13902
23:36:33,072 --> 23:36:36,100
第二，远离信任关系。
Second, keeping away from trust relationships.

13903
23:36:36,366 --> 23:36:44,192
组织将开发不依赖于信任关系的协议，因此你希望让该协议远离那些关系。
Organizations will develop protocols that do not depend on trust relationships and thus you want to keep this protocol away from that.

13904
23:36:44,352 --> 23:36:52,432
一旦建立了信任关系，这些机器一开始就不应该向其他机器发送 ARP 请求。
Once you have created a trust relationship, these machines should
not be sending out ARP requests to other machines in the first place.

13905
23:36:52,592 --> 23:37:00,612
既然信任关系已经定义好，且这些机器知道要与谁通信，那么此类协议就应该被禁用。
Since the trust relationship has been defined and these machines know whom to communicate with,
such kind of protocols should then be disabled.

13906
23:37:01,294 --> 23:37:03,472
或者你可以使用 ARP欺骗软件。
Or you can use an ARP spoofing software.

13907
23:37:03,552 --> 23:37:10,592
市面上有一些软件可以检测 ARP欺骗，并从一开始就防止其发生。
So there are some softwares out there that will look for ARP spoofing and prevent that from happening in the first place.

13908
23:37:10,672 --> 23:37:18,832
如果有人发送了伪造的 ARP 数据包，该数据包将被此软件捕获并得到缓解。
So if somebody has sent out a spoofed ARP packet, that packet will be picked up by this software and it will be mitigated.

13909
23:37:19,886 --> 23:37:31,072
像 GlassWire 这样的网络可视化工具，或者 Sophos 这样的杀毒软件，
它们内置了识别 ARP欺骗攻击并第一时间缓解攻击的功能。
Network visualizers like glasswire, antiviruses like Sophos, they have inbuilt
capabilities of identifying ARP spoofing attacks and mitigate them in the first place.

