所以，正如你在屏幕上看到的，攻击者成为了中间人攻击者，
这意味着他们正在窃听客户端和服务器之间的对话。
So, as you can see on the screen, the attacker becomes man in the middle, which means that they are now eavesdropping on the
conversation that is happening between the client and the server.

14877
25:27:19,758 --> 25:27:23,584
下一个问题：谁是黑帽黑客和白帽黑客？
The next question who are black hat hackers and white hat hackers?

14878
25:27:23,664 --> 25:27:27,044
核心点在于黑帽黑客和白帽黑客的区别。
The main thing is the differentiation between a black hat hacker and a white hat hacker.

14879
25:27:27,344 --> 25:27:32,544
黑帽黑客是擅长非法入侵系统的技术人员。
Now, black hat hackers are skilled individuals who illegally hack into a system.

14880
25:27:32,654 --> 25:27:35,684
此类攻击背后的动机大多是为了谋取金钱利益。
The motive behind such an attack is mostly for monetary gain.

14881
25:27:36,014 --> 25:27:38,864
这些人也被称为安全破解者。
These individuals are known also known as security crackers.

14882
25:27:38,944 --> 25:27:49,124
如果你看这些犯罪黑客，他们带有恶意意图，为了个人获利或破坏目的而进行黑客攻击。
Now, if you look at your criminal hackers, those who have malicious intent, those
who do hacking for the intent of personal gain or for the matter of disruption.

14883
25:27:49,424 --> 25:27:54,212
黑帽黑客主要缺乏的是授权。
The main thing that black hat hackers lack is authorization.

14884
25:27:54,542 --> 25:28:04,548
他们没有权限执行他们即将进行的活动，他们将获得
未经授权的访问权限，从而导致相关组织遭受损失。
They are not authorized to do the activity that they are about to do, and they are going to get unauthorized access to devices or to
data which is going to cause losses to the organization involved.

14885
25:28:05,184 --> 25:28:09,892
另一方面，白帽黑客也被称为道德黑客。
Whereas on the other side, a white hat hacker are also known as ethical hackers.

14886
25:28:10,464 --> 25:28:18,532
他们是发现计算机网络漏洞的人员，他们帮助组织缓解这些漏洞。
These are the individuals who discover vulnerabilities in a computer
network, and they help the organizations mitigate these vulnerabilities.

14887
25:28:18,830 --> 25:28:22,064
他们帮助组织防御黑帽黑客。
They help the organizations defend themselves from black hat hackers.

14888
25:28:22,144 --> 25:28:29,264
所以这两类黑客，黑帽和白帽，的主要区别在于意图和授权。
So the main difference between these two types of hackers, a black hat and a white hat, is the intent and the authorization.

14889
25:28:29,550 --> 25:28:37,504
黑帽黑客具有恶意意图，他们试图通过寻找漏洞从攻击中获取个人利益。
So black hat hackers will have malicious intent, they will try to
personally gain from that attack from by finding out vulnerabilities.

14890
25:28:37,678 --> 25:28:41,824
他们也没有权限执行他们正在进行的任何活动。
They also will not have authorization to conduct whatever activity they are doing.

14891
25:28:41,984 --> 25:28:51,424
而另一方面，白帽黑客受雇于组织，他们会被授予授权，去执行某些活动以发现那些漏洞。
Whereas on the other side, white hat hackers will be hired by organizations, they will be provide authorization for certain activity
that the white hat hacker can do to find out those vulnerabilities.

14892
25:28:51,662 --> 25:29:01,584
一旦白帽黑客发现了这些漏洞，他们会向管理层报告，并指导他们实施安全控制来缓解这些漏洞。
Once those vulnerabilities have been found out by the white hat hacker, they will report it to the management and guide them in
implementing security controls to mitigate those vulnerabilities.

14893
25:29:01,902 --> 25:29:07,104
黑帽和白帽的主要区别就是授权和意图。
The main difference between a black hat and a white hat is the authorization and the intent.

14894
25:29:07,502 --> 25:29:09,540
下一个问题：什么是蜜罐？
The next question what are honey pots?

14895
25:29:10,766 --> 25:29:16,448
现在，蜜罐是可以在网络中引入的一种非常有趣的设备。
Now, honey pots are a very interesting device that can be introduced in a network.

14896
25:29:17,008 --> 25:29:23,908
这些基本上是部署在网络中的诱饵服务器，用来吸引攻击者的注意力。
These basically are decoy servers that are implemented in a network to attract the attention of an attacker.

14897
25:29:24,288 --> 25:29:34,180
它的作用是诱骗攻击者去攻击那个特定的设备，从而为其他设备提供一层安全保护。
It is there to lure an attacker into attacking that particular device, thus creating a security blanket for the rest of the devices.

14898
25:29:34,798 --> 25:29:45,568
所以，如果攻击者能够绕过防火墙并试图扫描特定网络，
当他们进行扫描时，会发现网络中存在的各种设备。
So if an attacker has been able to bypass a firewall and is now trying to scan a particular network, when they scan,
they will come across various devices that are there in the network.

14899
25:29:45,728 --> 25:29:49,248
他们接着会对这些设备进行漏洞扫描。
They will then proceed to do a vulnerability scan on these devices.

14900
25:29:49,646 --> 25:30:02,276
此时，蜜罐会作为一种吸引点，因为它会向黑客展示一些漏洞，从而分散他们的注意力。
The honeypot at that point in time will provide as an or prove as an attraction to these attackers because it will demonstrate some
vulnerabilities to the hacker which will divert their attention.

14901
25:30:02,510 --> 25:30:05,248
这些漏洞是在这些设备上模拟出来的。
So these vulnerabilities are simulated on these devices.

14902
25:30:05,328 --> 25:30:06,724
实际上，这些漏洞并不存在。
These actually do not exist.

14903
25:30:07,054 --> 25:30:18,048
但就在攻击者开始与蜜罐交互的那一刻，蜜罐会识别出这是恶意流量，
并警告管理员可能正在发生的攻击。
But the moment the attacker then starts interacting with the honeypot, the honeypot will identify that as a malicious traffic and will
warm the warn the administrator about a possible attack that is going on.

14904
25:30:18,350 --> 25:30:27,428
管理员随后会通过蜜罐调查正在发生的活动，然后
重新配置安全控制，以阻止攻击者或缓解攻击本身。
The administrator will then investigate through the honeypot of what activity is going on and then reconfigure the security controls
to block the attacker or mitigate the attack itself.

14905
25:30:28,142 --> 25:30:38,768
所以它更像是一个诱饵服务器，向攻击者展示或模拟一些漏洞，
以此来诱骗他们并保护网络的其余部分。
So it is more of a decoy server that will showcase or simulate some vulnerabilities to an attacker,
thus to lure them and safeguard the rest of the network.

14906
25:30:39,022 --> 25:30:43,620
进入下一个问题：定义密码学、加密和解密。
Moving on to the next question: define cryptography, encryption, and decryption.

14907
25:30:43,968 --> 25:30:54,308
现在，安全专业人员使用密码学将数据打乱成不可读的格式，用于保护这些信息。
Now, cryptography is used by security professionals to scramble data
into non-readable format, which is used in securing that information.

14908
25:30:55,630 --> 25:31:02,404
所以它涉及将数据从可读格式转换为不可读格式，然后再将其转换回可读格式。
So it involves converting data from a readable format into a non-readable format and then reversing it back to readable format again.

14909
25:31:03,054 --> 25:31:09,408
例如，单词“computer”现在被打乱成看起来像不可读的格式。
For example, the word computer is now scrambled into looking like an unreadable format.

14910
25:31:09,568 --> 25:31:18,852
现在，如果你看这个被打乱后的单词，人类很难猜出原来的单词是什么。
Now, if you look at this word that it has been scrambled into, it would
be very difficult for a human to figure out what the actual word was.

14911
25:31:19,214 --> 25:31:29,168
在这个场景中，我们采用了一个算法，对字母表进行了偏移，我们将当前字母增加了两个字母。
Now in this scenario, we have taken an algorithm where we have made a
shift of the alphabet where we have added two alphabets to the current one.

14912
25:31:29,328 --> 25:31:36,208
所以 C 加 2 变成 E，O 加 2 变成 Q，M 加 2 变成 O。
So C plus 2 becomes E, O plus 2 becomes Q, M plus 2 becomes O.

14913
25:31:36,526 --> 25:31:38,372
所以我们做了 2 个单位的偏移。
So we have done a shift of 2.

14914
25:31:38,768 --> 25:31:44,448
因此，这个算法的密钥就是字母表加 2。
And thus the key over here for this algorithm is the alphabet plus 2.

14915
25:31:44,528 --> 25:31:50,724
所以任何弄清楚这一点的人，就能够解开这个打乱的字符，并将其转换回可读文本。
So any person who figures that out will be able to unscramble this and convert this back into readable text.

14916
25:31:51,248 --> 25:32:00,324
使用特定的密钥将可读文本数据打乱成不可读的内容，这就是密码学的核心。
The fact of scrambling a readable text data into something that is
unreadable by using a particular key is what cryptography is all about.

14917
25:32:01,358 --> 25:32:08,848
现在正如我们讨论过的，解密是再次替换字母表，并将其向前回退两个字符。
Now as we discussed the decryption again is replacing the alphabet and taking it further back by two characters.

14918
25:32:09,102 --> 25:32:16,048
所以 E 减 2 变成 C，Q 减 2 变成 O，O 减 2 变成 M，以此类推。
So E minus 2 becomes C, Q minus 2 becomes O, O minus 2 becomes M, and so on so forth.

14919
25:32:16,128 --> 25:32:24,288
所以任何知道这个密钥、也就是偏移密钥的人，都能解密这个特定的字符。
So anybody who knows this key, the shift key, anybody will able to decrypt this particular character.

14920
25:32:24,368 --> 25:32:25,968
所以这取决于用户。
So this depends on the user.

14921
25:32:26,048 --> 25:32:35,588
如果我想使用字母表加 5，那么那个字符的间距或偏移将是该字符之后的第五个字符，以此类推。
If I want to utilize alphabet plus 5, then the spacing, the shifting of that character
will be the fifth character from that particular character, and so on so forth.

14922
25:32:36,046 --> 25:32:39,940
现在是最后一个问题：密文和明文有什么区别？
And now the last question: what is the difference between ciphertext and clear text?

14923
25:32:40,654 --> 25:32:44,053
密文是指被加密且完全不可读的文本。
Ciphertext refers to the text which is encrypted and totally undesirable.

14924
25:32:46,254 --> 25:32:48,928
解密后收到的消息被称为明文。
The message received after decryption is known as clear text.

14925
25:32:49,102 --> 25:32:50,608
这段文字是可以理解的。
This text is comprehensible.

14926
25:32:50,848 --> 25:32:53,568
所以“computer”这个词就是明文。
So the word computer is clear text.

14927
25:32:53,648 --> 25:32:59,140
这意味着它没有经过任何密码学措施，就是它原本的样子。
That means that it has not been treated to any cryptographic measures, it is what it is intended to be.

14928
25:32:59,630 --> 25:33:07,716
但是，如果我们对它进行加密，意思就是通过我们
即将看到的任何算法，把它变成无法阅读的文本。
However, if the moment we encrypt it, that means we scramble it into
unreadable text by using any of the algorithms that we'll be looking at.

14929
25:33:08,494 --> 25:33:10,468
那段文本就被称为密文。
That text is known as a ciphertext.

14930
25:33:11,182 --> 25:33:13,828
而且如果没有密钥，它就变得无法阅读。
And without the key, this becomes unreadable.

14931
25:33:14,702 --> 25:33:18,928
正如我们讨论的，明文就是我们所使用的普通单词。
The clear text, as discussed, is the plain word that we have utilized.

14932
25:33:19,008 --> 25:33:23,620
在这个实例中，我们使用的是英语，所以普通单词“computer”就是明文。
We are using the English language in this instance, so the plain word computer is the clear text.

14933
25:33:23,822 --> 25:33:29,168
一旦我们给它加上加密层，它就变成了密文。
Once we add the encryption layer to it, we get the ciphertext to it.

